ted/', 'snippet': 'Intel Takeover of Altera Is Expected | Humana Said to Consider Sale | Big Payouts in Charter-Time Warner Cable Merger | Vanguard and Fidelity Resist Proxy Access', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTEL TAKEOVER OF ALTERA IS EXPECTED | Just days after  Avago Technologies agreed to buy Broadcom for about $37 billion, the semiconductor industry is on the verge of yet another takeover deal, this time between Intel and Altera,  Michael J. de la Merced and Quentin Hardy write in DealBook. Intel is in talks to buy the chip maker Altera for more than $15 billion, a person briefed on the matter said on Friday. Intel is expected to pay about $54 a share for Altera, whose specialized chip designs would help Intel expand beyond chips for personal computers, this person said. An agreement could be announced this week, but the person said the talks are continuing and might still collapse. Shares in Altera rose 4 percent on Friday, to $48.85, after  The New York Post reported that the two companies were close to an agreement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Intel Takeover of Altera Is Expected', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, John A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALTERA CORP', 'rank': 9, 'maj