7ac-5bca-950e-ea1cd9bb22b0', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2193356a-b7ac-5bca-950e-ea1cd9bb22b0'}, {'abstract': 'South Kensington Club has wellness at its core, and values niceness when considering potential members.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/01/london-new-south-kensington-club/', 'snippet': 'South Kensington Club has wellness at its core, and values niceness when considering potential members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London has a long history of private clubs, with perhaps more members-only establishments per capita than any other city in the world. That latest is the South Kensington Club, which officially opens today and has wellness as its focus. Luca Del Bono, the owner and a co-founder of Quintessentially concierge service, says he got the idea while living in New York, where he’d often go to the Russian Turkish Baths in the East Village. “At the time, Londoners were too prudish. Fifteen years ago, an English man would not even admit they would have a massage,” he recalls. “But nowadays people are so conscious about being healthy and fit.” He describes South Kensington Club as a “members club with a gym, a bathhouse and a saltwater Watsu pool.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/t-magazine/01club-suqi-1/01club-suqi-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/01/t-magazine/01club-suqi-1/01club-suqi-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/t-magazine/01club-suqi-1/01club-suqi-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06