, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/02giants-1/02giants-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/02/us/02giants-1/02giants-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/02giants-1/02giants-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Punter Steve Weatherford Is in Wreck, He Practices With the Giants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Punter Is in Wreck, He Practices With Giants ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weatherford, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-02T03:23:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26fd35ec-c6fc-5f07-8f64-f6be01b448a5', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26fd35ec-c6fc-5f07-8f64-f6be01b448a5'}, {'abstract': 'Susanne Kaufmann brings her hippie sensibility to the all-natural realm of haircare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/02/t-magazine/susanne-kaufmann-hair-products.html', 'snippet': 'Susanne Kaufmann brings her hippie sensibility to the all-natural realm of haircare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Susanne Kaufmann first launched her holistic skincare line over 10 years ago in her Austrian spa, her hand-packaged creams and cleansers have gained a cult following for their hippie essence: built with natural ingredients and perfumed with non-allergenic scents. Her new haircare collection — a suite of seven products to wash, condition and repair free-flowing strands — is equally pure. “Our focus was purely to encourage the natural beauty of the hair from within, hair that is strong and grows well, without any extra help or wild promises,” Kaufmann says. “Just let that hair grow and give it what it needs, and the result will be hair just as it should be.” The range uses silk and sugar-based cleansing systems and is free from synthetic additives, silicone and chemical agents. Next, Kaufmann plans to introduce styling products.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/t-magazine/02kaufmann-mosci/02kaufmann-mosci-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Suite of Pure Hair Products', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-02T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renata Mosci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renata', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mosci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/188118e2-66aa-5362-b0bd-85cba9ab8d00', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/188118e2-66aa-5362-b0bd-85cba9ab8d00'}, {'abstract': 'The designer, hotelier, artist, creative director (and, D.J.) infused his Chelsea apartment with relics of his various design projects and a life well lived.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/02/t-magazine/robert-mckinleys-beach-chic-style-at-home-in-chelsea.html', 'snippet': 'The designer, hotelier, artist, creative director (and, D.J.) infused his Chelsea apartment with relics of his various design projects and a life well lived.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This piece of wood, I can see having for the rest of my life,” says Robert McKinley, rubbing his hand along the edge of an ash wood table in the Chelsea apartment he shares with his fianceé, Kate Nauta. “Maybe it will be a bench or something else one day,” says the 38-year-old designer, hotelier, D.J., artist and creative director. “I try to reuse wood as much as possible.” The slab of wood began its life as the leftovers of a project: McKinley brought the scrap home while designing the hotel Ruschmeyer’s in Montauk. Now, it sits atop matte black powder-coated tubular steel legs in the couple’s third-floor brownstone space, where they like to entertain. “He makes fabulous pasta,” says Nauta, a model, actor and singer who just returned from the Bahamas, where she recorded her first album with Lenny Kravitz as producer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/05/02/t-magazine/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO/02mckinley-levine-slide-58QO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert McKinley’s Beach-Chic Style at Home in Chelsea', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-02T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37d7ff6c-65c8-544f-85c4-84ee0abac130', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37d7ff6c-65c8-544f-85c4-84ee0abac130'}, {'abstract': 'A new book provides a retrospective of indie music flyers by the graphic artist Dan Stiles, who has also worked for IBM and with the President’s farm-to-table initiative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/02/t-magazine/rock-posters-with-a-mod-touch.html', 'snippet': 'A new book provides a retrospective of indie music flyers by the graphic artist Dan Stiles, who has also worked for IBM and with the President’s farm-to-table initiative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Portland, Ore.-based artist Dan Stiles is known for his bright colors, clean lines and witty abstractions. Over the course of his two decades as a graphic designer, he’s worked with some of the world’s most recognizable corporations (IBM, Old Navy, the X Games), reimagined book jackets by beloved 20th-century authors (Anthony Burgess, Bohumil Hrabal) and even created unique soda packaging in honor of the President’s commitment to farm-to-table eating. In his new book, “One Thing Leads to Another” ($25, PowerHouse) Stiles’s work is given a career-spanning retrospective, with full-color pages that showcase his eye-popping, overprinted style.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock Posters With a Mod Touch', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-02T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed4f3a46-9b39-5425-9f44-65f566b256e3', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed4f3a46-9b39-5425-9f44-65f566b256e3'}, {'abstract': 'The source they really rely on for their questions about health information is their parents, a new survey finds.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/02/teenagers-seek-health-information-online-but-dont-always-trust-it/', 'snippet': 'The source they really rely on for their questions about health information is their parents, a new survey finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four out of five teenagers turn to the Internet for health information, but they don’t always put much stock in what they find, according to a national survey released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/science/02teens/02teens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/02/science/02teens/02teens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capti