t know it.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You don’t need to experience something to remember it,” a former child soldier remarks in the final pages of Sara Novic’s outstanding first novel, “Girl at War.” She’s describing how the memory of the Yugoslav civil war will be conveyed to future generations, but she might also be describing the possibility that good literature allows: Charge language with enough vitality and its story will be remembered by readers a world away.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 631}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 974, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2040, 'width': 1940, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/books/review/07MARRA/07marra-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 't