a-nunca-muere-in-spanish/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jaramillo plays Fidel Castro in this farce at Repertorio Español.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features Germán Jaramillo in a Spanish-language excerpt from “Hierba Mala Nunca Muere” (“Weeds Just Won’t Die”), a farce by Juan Claudio Lechín at Repertorio Español. Set in Cuba, the show is a comedic look at Fidel Castro (Mr. Jaramillo) as he rants about his country’s future from his deathbed. “The pain I feel is a feline that is clawing at my heart,” he says. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Germán Jaramillo of ‘Hierba Mala Nunca Muere’ (in Spanish)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaramillo, German', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lechin, Juan Claudio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Repertorio Espanol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-02T12:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5661a744-ca68-522f-adcb-71496aba8068', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5661a744-ca68-522f-adcb-71496aba8068'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Bernie Sanders, on “Late Night With Seth Meyers,” joked about past writing and musical endeavors, and heard applause from the audience when the interview dealt with substantive issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/06/02/bernie-sanders-finds-appreciative-audience-on-late-night-tv/', 'snippet': 'Senator Bernie Sanders, on “Late Ni