99d1-6337-5e71-bc72-8cc64e689b9d', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dcf99d1-6337-5e71-bc72-8cc64e689b9d'}, {'abstract': 'Caitlyn Jenner looks great on the cover of Vanity Fair—and there’s a lesson in that.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/02/for-our-daughters-a-lesson-in-call-me-caitlyn/', 'snippet': 'Caitlyn Jenner looks great on the cover of Vanity Fair—and there’s a lesson in that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Magazine covers can often start conversations with children what with their lurid headlines and provocative imagery. I frequently find them hard to explain: There is no really comprehensible answer, for an 8-year-old, to the question of why the girl on the cover of Sports Illustrated is taking off her swimsuit bottom. (And there’s really no comprehensible answer for me about why our general store stacked those up next to the brownie mix).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/motherlode-jenner/motherlode-jenner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/02/us/motherlode-jenner/motherlode-jenner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/motherlode-jenner/motherlode-jenner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/motherlode-jenner/motherlode-jenner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/us/motherlode-jenner/motherlode-jenner-thumbStandard.jpg