abstract': 'Mr. Andersson’s signature style as a writer and director comes through in “A Pigeon Sat on a Branch Reflecting on Existence.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/movies/review-a-pigeon-sat-on-a-branch-roy-anderssons-rumination-on-life.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Andersson’s signature style as a writer and director comes through in “A Pigeon Sat on a Branch Reflecting on Existence.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Pigeon Sat on a Branch Reflecting on Existence” begins with three vignettes on death. In one of them, a man has expired in a cafeteria on board some kind of ferry or cruise ship. Officers and passengers stand around him with expressions of concern, but the server has a more practical worry: what to do with the beer and the shrimp sandwich the dead customer had already paid for. A stout older gentleman shuffles forward. “I guess I’ll take the beer,” he says with a shrug. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/arts/03PIGEON/03PIGEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/arts/03PIGEON/03PIGEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/arts/03PIGEON/03PIGEON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/arts/03PIGEON/03PIGEON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1099, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/arts/03PIGEON/03PIGEON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 