,000 South Sudanese had fled since January, mostly to Sudan, Ethiopia and Uganda, bringing the total number of refugees to 555,000 since December 2013, when the conflict erupted. Mr. Edwards said that 1.5 million people had been displaced within the country and that a third of the population lacked sufficient food. The news came a day after United Nations officials said South Sudan’s government had decided to expel the organization’s aid coordinator there, Toby Lanzer, who has criticized the South Sudanese armed forces for their role in the fighting. He was nearing the end of his tenure anyway, but Secretary General Ban Ki-moon condemned the expulsion. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Sudan: U.N. Dismayed by Decline', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; South Sudan: U.N. Dismayed by Decline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations High Commission for Refugees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T00:20:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/620b382b-80f6-5a1d-b714-e3194d18be62', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/620b382b-80f6-5a1d-b714-e3194d18be62'}, {'abstract': 'As large movie theaters have negotiated with studios for the exclusive rights to show films in certain geographic areas, some smaller independent theaters have taken legal action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/business/media/antitrust-scrutiny-for-3-big-us-theater-chains.html', 'snippet': 'As large movie theaters have negotiated with studios for the exclusive rights to show films in certain geographic areas, some smaller independent theaters have taken legal action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A simmering federal investigation into whether the big movie theater chains are misusing their market clout to keep new films away from independent competitors gained steam on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Antitrust Scrutiny for 3 Big U.S. Theater Chains ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Antitrust Scrutiny for 3 Big U.S. Theater Chains ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cinemark Holdings Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regal Entertainment Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC ENTERTAINMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T00:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/273d360a-1ba4-549b-aa5b-2c742d86eb5d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273d360a-1ba4-549b-aa5b-2c742d86eb5d'}, {'abstract': 'Forensic psychologists say a taped interview with James E. Holmes provides an exceedingly rare and chilling window into the plotting and psyche of a mass killer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/us/video-shows-james-holmes-recalling-colorado-theater-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Forensic psychologists say a taped interview with James E. Holmes provides an exceedingly rare and chilling window into the plotting and psyche of a mass killer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — The gunman’s voice was flat, unshaded by emotion, as he told a psychiatrist how he had slipped through the emergency exit door of a packed movie theater and opened fire on the crowd. He was on autopilot, he said. He turned up the electronic music in his headphones to drown out the screams. He knew he would probably end up arrested or dead, but he was carrying out what he called “the mission.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows James Holmes Recalling Colorado Theater Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gunman Calmly Recalls Theater Rampage in Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, James Eagan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T00:28:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2689830-fe66-52f6-a8ef-ce0f132deb5a', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2689830-fe66-52f6-a8ef-ce0f132deb5a'}, {'abstract': 'A conflict between the Oneida Indian Nation and the developer Wilmorite has led to accusations of parasitic business plans and a possible casino war in upstate New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/nyregion/tribe-opening-new-casino-says-a-competitors-site-is-too-close-for-comfort.html', 'snippet': 'A conflict between the Oneida Indian Nation and the developer Wilmorite has led to accusations of parasitic business plans and a possible casino war in upstate New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHITTENANGO, N.Y. — The state’s newest casino opened here on Tuesday, brimming with hundreds of slot machines, scores of smiling employees and four flying-monkey sculptures adorning a “Wizard of Oz”- — — themed gambling floor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/nyregion/CASINOweb1/CASINOweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/nyregion/CASINOweb1/CASINOweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/nyregion/CASINOweb1/CASINOweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/nyregion