 York State, similar care would be taken to gather the memories of witnesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/nyregion/a-plan-to-combat-mistaken-identifications-and-false-confessions.html', 'snippet': 'For generations, evidence at crime scenes has been collected in ways to reduce contamination. Now, under a proposal in New York State, similar care would be taken to gather the memories of witnesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For generations, physical evidence at crime scenes has been collected using techniques to reduce contamination. Technicians wear gloves on their hands, masks on their faces, bootees over their shoes. With sterile tools, they tweeze, swab and dust for hairs, bloodstains and fingerprints, and place them in individual packets for lab analysis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Plan to Combat Mistaken Identifications and False Confessions ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Plan to Combat Mistaken Identifications and False Confessions ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witnesses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T01:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe7f763-2d49-539d-b429-2ba61e081144', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe7f763-2d49-539d-b429-2ba61e081144'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration says that many people had failed to pay their share of premiums, leaving enrollment at 10.2 million people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/us/13-left-health-care-rolls-us-finds.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration says that many people had failed to pay their share of premiums, leaving enrollment at 10.2 million people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — About 13 percent of people who signed up for health insurance coverage in 2015 under the Affordable Care Act have fallen off the rolls, many because they failed to pay their share of premiums, the Obama administration said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '13% Left Health Care Rolls, U.S. Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '13% Left Health Care Rolls, U.S. Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burwell, Sylvia Mathews', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T01:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_