 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbc90419-a8f7-5727-b56a-58f4c51b8344', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbc90419-a8f7-5727-b56a-58f4c51b8344'}, {'abstract': 'The various demonstrations are a reflection of growing divisions over Hong Kong’s identity, its relationship with the Chinese mainland and where democracy advocates should concentrate their efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/rival-pro-democracy-rallies-planned-for-june-4-in-hong-kong/', 'snippet': 'The various demonstrations are a reflection of growing divisions over Hong Kong’s identity, its relationship with the Chinese mainland and where democracy advocates should concentrate their efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every June 4 for a quarter-century, people in Hong Kong who want to commemorate the 1989 Tiananmen Square crackdown have known where to go: Victoria Park, site of the world’s largest public gathering mourning the hundreds, possibly thousands, of civilians killed when troops were deployed to suppress pro-democracy demonstrations in Beijing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/world/02sino-hong/02sino-hong-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/02/world/02sino-hong/02sino-hong-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/world/02sino-hong/02sino-hong-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/02/world/02sino-hong/02sino-hong-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1