', 'value': 'SARS (Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T09:21:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ab8aea-4a02-5b9c-a9f7-fe688aa9b496', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ab8aea-4a02-5b9c-a9f7-fe688aa9b496'}, {'abstract': 'A surgeon learns a shady company has her husband’s head.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/books/review/the-new-world-by-chris-adrian-and-eli-horowitz.html', 'snippet': 'A surgeon learns a shady company has her husband’s head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whither the digital novel? Weren’t we all excited, back in the ’90s, about what technology would actually do to storytelling? Weren’t we talking about \xadhyperlinks and cybertext and interactivity? I gather there’s still a vogue in English departments for digital humanities, whatever that is. But for most of us the whole concept has been domesticated. It turns out we don’t want tech-aided experiments in form so much as little Kindles lighting our faces on subways and planes and in darkened bedrooms. We want more room in the suitcase.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The New World,’ by Chris Adrian and Eli Horowitz', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cryogenic Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Antrim, Taylor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADRIAN, CHRIS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horowitz, Eli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The New World (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T09:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Taylor Antrim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antrim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c223df-d946-5f28-a831-d4c36245af17', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c223df-d946-5f28-a831-d4c36245af17'}, {'abstract': 'These linked stories provide a group portrait of a WASPy town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/books/review/the-wonder-garden-by-lauren-acampora.html', 'snippet': 'These linked stories provide a group portrait of a WASPy town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Edith Wharton’s first published book was a nonfiction work called “The Decoration of \xadHouses.” In it, she wrote that “the essence of a style lies not in its use of ornament, but in its handling of proportion. Structure conditions ornament, not ornament structure.” She was arguing that home décor and architecture had to be linked, that content must be connected to form: an aesthetic theory that could just as easily apply to writing.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'