or': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breuer, Lanny A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T19:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ce1ffa7a-85d3-569a-a693-36b808059c74', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ce1ffa7a-85d3-569a-a693-36b808059c74'}, {'abstract': 'Amnesty International said that torture, mass shootings, starvation and the use of deadly fumigation chemicals in overcrowded cells have been routinely employed by the Nigerian military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/world/africa/abuses-nigeria-military-boko-haram-war-report.html', 'snippet': 'Amnesty International said that torture, mass shootings, starvation and the use of deadly fumigation chemicals in overcrowded cells have been routinely employed by the Nigerian military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — In the course of Nigeria’s war against the Boko Haram terrorist group, at least 7,000 people have died in government detention because of brutal conditions, an additional 1,200 have been “extrajudicially executed” by Nigerian security forces, and at least 20,000 have been “arbitrarily arrested” by the authorities, Amnesty International said in a report released Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abuses by Nigeria’s Military Found to Be Rampant in War Against Boko Haram', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Military in Nigeria Is Accused of Abuses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T19:13:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfb46756-57b5-51a9-83ca-fa105ca82a4b', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb46756-57b5-51a9-83ca-fa105ca82a4b'}, {'abstract': 'The artist unveiled a massive steel sculpture on the heels of a recent installation in Dulwich Park in London’s Southwark —\xa0and on the eve of an exhibition of his smaller-scale works.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/conrad-shawcross-london-dappled-light/', 'snippet': 'The artist unveiled a massive steel sculpture on the heels of a recent installation in Dulwich Park in London’s Southwark —\xa0and on the eve of an exhibition of his smaller-scale works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a monumental moment in the career of Conrad Shawcross. The 38-year-old British artist, who is the youngest member of London’s prestigious Royal Academy of Arts, has just unveiled “The Dappled Light of the Sun,” a colossal steel sculpture that scales the institution’s classical courtyard like an alien landing. Even for Shawcross — an artist celebrated for his feats of engineering, spanning rope machines, reconfigured robots and even a pair of rotating wooden arms for Raf Simons’s runway — this is ambitious. Each of the 8,000 pieces has been handmade in five diminishing scales; when laid flat, the piece comprises about 7 ½ miles of welded steel and weighs in at around 30 tons. “It exploits the geometry of the tetrahedron,” Shawcross explains of the mass of pyramid shapes. “Seen on their own, they’re very rational and ordered, but together, they become totally unruly. So the finished work is full of energy and movement. It looks anarchic against the order and stillness of the courtyard space.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/03/t-magazine/03shawcross-aimee-1/03shawcross-aimee-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'