t-and-more/', 'snippet': 'On Wednesday, Mr. Colbert introduced an online presence for his “Late Show,” including a video, a Twitter feed, a Facebook page, a YouTube page, and an iOS application called Colbr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As he prepares to take over CBS’s “Late Show” on Sept. 8, Stephen Colbert now has a beefed-up online and social media presence – but he no longer has a beard.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephen Colbert Debuts ‘Late Show’ Video, Podcast and More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colbert Beefs Up Social and Loses the Beard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T19:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7812e6f1-5ffd-5e23-9ee1-388fc5b8674f', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7812e6f1-5ffd-5e23-9ee1-388fc5b8674f'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln Chafee, a former Rhode Island governor and senator, has entered the race for the Democratic nomination for president. Here is what he will need to do if he hopes to win.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/06/03/us/elections/lincoln-chafee.html', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Chafee, a former Rhode Island governor and senator, has entered the race for the Democratic nomination for president. Here is what he will need to do if he hopes to win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Chafee, a former Rhode Island governor and senator, has entered the race for the Democratic nomination for president. Here is what he will need to do if he hopes to win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-paths/04CHAFEE-paths-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Lincoln Chafee Would Need to Do to Win', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T19:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Elections', 'byline': {'original': 'By JONATHAN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e9e6a2f6-bc58-5b0f-bd29-18892bf9cb2c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e9e6a2f6-bc58-5b0f-bd29-18892bf9cb2c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Chafee, a former Republican and independent who is running for the Democratic nomination, favors a warming in relations with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/us/politics/lincoln-chafee-on-the-issues.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Chafee, a former Republican and independent who is running for the Democratic nomination, favors a warming in relations with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Chafee, 62, a former governor and senator from Rhode Island, on Wednesday entered the race for the Democratic presidential nomination. He was appointed to the Senate in 1999 as a Republican to replace his father, John H. Chafee, who had died. He was elected the next year and was the only senator in his party to vote against going to war in Iraq. After being defeated by Sheldon Whitehouse in 2006, Mr. Chafee was elected governor in 2010 as an independent but later became a Democrat. He did not seek re-election. Here are his stands on important issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/us/04CHAFEE-issues/04CHAFEE-issues-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'