/23f5a25f-3cd3-59e5-ac33-ca78e7481130'}, {'abstract': 'The museum has acquired Jasper Johns’s “Flag” (1983) and four works by Louise Bourgeois, which aids its mission of featuring more women in its collection of American artists.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/03/crystal-bridges-museum-buying-more-art-by-women/', 'snippet': 'The museum has acquired Jasper Johns’s “Flag” (1983) and four works by Louise Bourgeois, which aids its mission of featuring more women in its collection of American artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art will soon announce major purchases that fill gaps in its collection and fulfill its mission to include more women in the canon of American art: Jasper Johns’s renowned “Flag” painting from 1983, which the museum bought at Sotheby’s in November for $36 million (outlasting three other ardent bidders), and four works by Louise Bourgeois, including her monumental bronze, steel and marble spider sculpture “Maman.” The Bourgeois purchases, concluded in December 2014, together are worth an estimated $35 million to $40 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crystal Bridges Museum to Announce Major Purchases', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crystal Bridges Museum To Unveil Acquisitions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourgeois, Louise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walton, Alice L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith H. Dobrzynski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname'