e': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/books/review/03childrens-1/03childrens-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/books/review/03childrens-1/03childrens-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1470, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/books/review/03childrens-1/03childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/03/books/review/03childrens-1/03childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/books/review/03childrens-1/03childrens-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf: About a Girl', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Books', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARIA RUSSO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RUSSO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8d30bc33-019f-5585-9d79-d2105941c809', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8d30bc33-019f-5585-9d79-d2105941c809'}, {'abstract': 'An Act II dance in this George Balanchine work is the largest point of several in which Balanchine does something unlike Shakespeare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/arts/dance/review-new-york-city-ballet-with-heartfelt-pas-de-deux-in-a-midsummer-nights-dream.html', 'snippet': 'An Act II dance in this George Balanchine work is the largest point of several in which Balanchine does something unlike Shakespeare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the center of Act II of George Balanchine’s “A Midsummer Night’s Dream” is an intricate, hushed, slow, gentle, spellbinding pas de deux that has nothing to do with either the ballet’s story or the Shakespeare play on which it is based. Danced by an anonymous woman and man during the divertissement given by Duke Theseus for the triple wedding, it is an image of perfect chivalrous love and cooperation. On Tuesday night, when “Midsummer” made its annual return to City Ballet repertory at the David H. Koch Theater, it was danced by Tiler Peck and Tyler Angle as beautifully as I have ever known it, the legato of their phrasing spinning threads like gossamer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 603}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2038, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/MIDSUMMER/MIDSUMMER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: New York City Ballet, With Heartfelt Pas de Deux, in ‘A Midsummer Night’s Dream’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Setting a Tone in Heartfelt Step', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balanchine, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/697e3a0b-d2a0-5321-9a75-f1ccdbce347d', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/697e3a0b-d2a0-5321-9a75-f1ccdbce347d'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer staged five short works (including “Division,” a New York premiere) with his troupe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/arts/dance/review-brian-brooks-moving-company-keeps-things-off-center-at-the-joyce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer staged five short works (including “Division,” a New York premiere) with his troupe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Brooks has been a regular at the Joyce Theater lately, performing last week with Wendy Whelan in “Restless Creature,” for which he was one of four choreographers, and this week with his Brian Brooks Moving Company. Watching his fine dancers in a program of five short works, which opened on Tuesday, you can see why Ms. Whelan, looking to break out of ballet’s verticality, would gravitate toward Mr. Brooks. He treats the body as an axis that’s never upright, or only upright on its way from one incline to another. The body’s momentum, whipped up by a brisk calligraphy of the limbs, keeps the axis swaying off-center. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Brian Brooks Moving Company Keeps Things Off-Center at the Joyce Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comfortably Off-Center ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whelan, Wendy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooks, Brian, Moving Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:24:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/24966e71-1891-5166-90f6-64f3648ea97f', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24966e71-1891-5166-90f6-64f3648ea97f'}, {'abstract': 'The film, which shows scenes of prostitutes in Marrakesh servicing wealthy Saudi clients, had its premiere at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/movies/morocco-defends-ban-of-much-loved-attack-on-actor-is-called-unrelated.html', 'snippet': 'The film, which shows scenes of prostitutes in Marrakesh servicing wealthy Saudi clients, had its premiere at the Cannes Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morocco’s communications minister on Wednesday defended the government’s decision to ban the film “Much Loved,” which shows scenes of prostitutes in Marrakesh partying and servicing wealthy Saudi clients. Meanwhile, the state-run news agency said there was no link between the film and a knife attack on a cast member.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morocco Defends Ban of ‘Much Loved’; Attack on Actor Is Called Unrelated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moroccan Official Defends Film Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alami, Aida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayouch, Nabil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aida Alami', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alami', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/300624dd-090f-5a92-b1bd-79ed5ee17e6a', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300624dd-090f-5a92-b1bd-79ed5ee17e6a'}, {'abstract': "The sealed papers from the soccer official Chuck Blazer's criminal case were released on Wednesday. Blazer pleaded guilty in 2013 to charges that included racketeering, wire fraud, money laundering and income tax evasion.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/06/03/sports/soccer/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public.html', 'snippet': "The sealed papers from the soccer official Chuck Blazer's criminal case were released on Wednesday. Blazer pleaded guilty in 2013 to charges that included racketeering, wire fraud, money laundering and income tax evasion.", 'lead_paragraph': "The sealed papers from the soccer official Chuck Blazer's criminal case were released on Wednesday. Blazer pleaded guilty in 2013 to charges that included racketeering, wire fraud, money laundering and income tax evasion.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-articleLarge.png', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-jumbo.png', 'height': 384, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-superJumbo.png', 'height': 384, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/sports/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public/document-chuck-blazer-court-papers-made-public-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chuck Blazer Court Papers Made Public', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blazer, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-03T21:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5d46231c-0138-58cb-a992-caf432290e70', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5d46231c-0138-58cb-a992-caf432290e70'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday Martin’s anthropologically themed memoir examines the women of the Upper East Side of Manhattan — their snootiness, their Birkin bags and their derrières in gymwear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/books/review-primates-of-park-avenue-making-fun-of-the-rich.html', 'snippet': 'Wednesday Martin’s anthropologically themed memoir examines the women of the Upper East Side of Manhattan — their snootiness, their Birkin bags and their derrières in gymwear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No book in recent memory has been as splashily misrepresented as Wednesday Martin’s “Primates of Park Avenue.” It is supposed to have blown the lid off the darkest secrets of the wealthy, glamorous Upper East Side wife-and-mommy set. Ms. Martin unearthed these secrets — including that of the buzzed-about “wife bonus,” which her book barely mentions — by living among and masquerading as one of those rich RoboMoms while also doing “fieldwork” in anthropology and primatology, like an urban Jane Goodall with an interest in social-climbing and fashion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/04BOOKMARTIN/04BOOKMARTIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/04BOOKMARTIN/04BOOKMARTIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 892}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/04BOOKMARTIN/04BOOKMARTIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 689, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/04BOOKMARTIN/04BOOKMARTIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1377, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/arts/04BOOKMARTIN/04BOOKMARTIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thum