nández de Kirchner denounced “a culture that devastates women.” More than 1,800 women died between 2008 and 2014 in episodes of domestic violence, according to La Casa del Encuentro, a local women’s rights group. Organizers of the rallies urged officials to enforce the provisions of a 2009 law devised to crack down on violence against women. Speaking in Buenos Aires, Juan Minujín, an actor, said: “This is a unanimous cry for coordinated action that tackles the problem. We don’t want more tears of mourning.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Rallies to Protect Women', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Americas; Argentina: Rallies to Protect Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T01:12:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c5f6a54-6e8c-5a7f-9b86-ad6f07f439dc', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c5f6a54-6e8c-5a7f-9b86-ad6f07f439dc'}, {'abstract': 'Jordan Spieth, 21, and Rory McIlroy, 26, are successful young golfers, but youth is rare in a sport that has been called slow, difficult and expensive by a younger generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/sports/golf/to-find-the-next-nicklaus-dont-look-to-a-nicklaus.html', 'snippet': 'Jordan Spieth, 21, and Rory McIlroy, 26, are successful young golfers, but youth is rare in a sport that has been called slow, difficult and expensive by a younger generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN, Ohio — At 21, Jordan Spieth is younger than a few of the golfers on the Louisiana State and University of Southern California teams that squared off Wednesday in the N.C.A.A. Division I match-play final. Spieth, one of the marquee players in this week’s Memorial Tournament, is the closest pursuer to the world No. 1, Rory McIlroy, who last month turned 26, leading Jack Nicklaus, the Memorial host and 18-time major champion, to observe, “The game of golf is in pretty good hands.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/sports/Y-JP-GOLF/Y-JP-GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Find the Next Nicklaus, Don’t Look to a Nicklaus ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Find the Next Nicklaus, Don&#8217;t Look to a Nicklaus ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spieth, Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicklaus, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T01:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/210c43c5-f6d6-53e6-aa2a-472d5b65f77e', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/210c43c5-f6d6-53e6-aa2a-472d5b65f77e'}, {'abstract': 'Palestinian militants launched two rockets from Gaza toward southern Israel late Wednesday, the Israeli military said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/world/middleeast/gaza-militants-fire-rockets-into-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Palestinian militants launched two rockets from Gaza toward southern Israel late Wednesday, the Israeli military said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Palestinian militants launched two rockets from Gaza toward southern Israel late Wednesday, the Israeli military said. The rockets landed in open ground and caused no injuries but were a blow to the informal cease-fire that ended last summer’s 50-day Gaza war. It was the second rocket attack in eight days after a period of relative calm. Although Hamas, the Islamic militant group that controls Gaza, has worked to enforce the cease-fire with Israel, smaller, more radical groups are thought to have been responsible for the recent rocket fire, a sign of internal Palestinian tensions. One such group claimed responsibility for firing the rockets on Wednesday, but Israel says it holds Hamas responsible for all fire emanating from Gaza. In retaliation, Israel on Thursday bombed three militant training camps, but there were no casualties, Reuters reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Militants Fire Rockets Into Israel', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Gaza: Militants Fire Rockets Into Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T01:17:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role