 suit, the city’s Department of Finance put some older New Yorkers in danger of eviction by improperly altering deadlines for the rent program and by failing to properly inform them of the rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/nyregion/new-york-city-is-sued-over-rule-change-to-rent-freeze-program.html', 'snippet': 'According to the suit, the city’s Department of Finance put some older New Yorkers in danger of eviction by improperly altering deadlines for the rent program and by failing to properly inform them of the rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mayor Bill de Blasio signed legislation a year ago that increased the number of older New Yorkers eligible to have their rents frozen, he called it a “godsend” and an “extraordinary lifeline” for people whose incomes could not keep pace with the cost of living.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/nyregion/04HOUSING2citysub/04HOUSING2citysub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Is Sued Over Rule Change to Rent-Freeze Program', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Is Sued Over Rule Change to Rent-Freeze Program ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Letitia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Finance (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T03:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ad2e16-1e18-568b-888d-5e36f0bcdbbf', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ad2e16-1e18-568b-888d-5e36f0bcdbbf'}, {'abstract': 'N.H.L. Commissioner Gary Bettman on Wednesday stood by his recent comment that there was no definitive evidence linking hockey and chronic traumatic encephalopathy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/sports/hockey/gary-bettman-denies-brain-disease-link.html', 'snippet': 'N.H.L. Commissioner Gary Bettman on Wednesday stood by his recent comment that there was no definitive evidence linking hockey and chronic traumatic encephalopathy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.H.L. Commissioner Gary Bettman on Wednesday stood by his recent comment that there was no definitive evidence linking hockey and chronic traumatic encephalopathy, a degenerative brain disease that scientists have found in many athletes who played contact sports. Bettman said his views echoed those of the federal court judge who approved a settlement between the N.F.L. and thousands of retired players. The N.H.L. is being sued by former players who say the league did not warn them of the dangers of concussions.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gary Bettman Denies Brain Disease Link', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bettman Denies Brain Disease Link', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T03:56:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42ef4ae-f284-5d3e-8848-3c1128cbefe4', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42ef4ae-f284-5d3e-8848-3c1128cbefe4'}, {'abstract': 'The Serbian-born furniture designer, illustrator, photographer and model opens up her Lower East Side apartment to T.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/t-magazine/at-home-with-ana-kras-new-york-design-star-of-the-moment.html', 'snippet': 'The Serbian-born furniture designer, illustrator, photographer and model opens up her Lower East Side apartment to T.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s an improvisation of an apartment,” says Ana Kras, the Serbian-born furniture maker, illustrator, photographer and model, of the whitewashed one-bedroom she recently moved into on New York’s Lower East Side. With its double-size windows and high ceilings, the space feels substantially larger than its 500 square feet. The spontaneous, uncluttered aesthetic is due in part to circumstance: Kras has only been living in this apartment a week or so, and most of her things are still with her parents in Belgrade, where she grew up and studied at the University of Applied Arts, and in Los Angeles, her home base until she relocated to New York two years ago. In addition, she has just returned from a 5-day trip to Marfa, Tex., where she shot the fall/holiday look book for Lou & Grey as the new face of the brand (she has also contributed to the Ampersand, its new online magazine).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Home With Ana Kras, New York Design Star of the Moment', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'report