, 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5b4ef9-822a-57ea-8080-520f82f438b7'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (AMC) JAWS (1975) Steven Spielberg directed this summer blockbuster classic. Amity Island, a beach town, is on alert after a shark attack, but local officials want to avert economic disaster at the height of the tourist season. Martin Brody (Roy Scheider) is the police chief, new to Amity Island, who teams up with the oceanographer Matt Hooper (Richard Dreyfuss) and the grizzled fisherman Quint (Robert Shaw, above right, with Mr. Scheider, center, and Mr. Dreyfuss) to hunt the shark. “It may not look like much but it puts good actors to the test,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. “They have to work very hard just to appear alive, and Mr. Scheider, Mr. Shaw and Mr. Dreyfuss come across with wit and easy self-assurance.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alec M. Priester', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alec', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d1764f6-fe30-5052-ba33-25c757b6d962', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d1764f6-fe30-5052-ba33-25c757b6d962'}, {'abstract': 'In his return from the disabled list, Gee, the Mets’ sixth starter, couldn’t get through five innings for the first time in his last 52 starts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/sports/baseball/dillon-gee-falters-as-does-the-mets-fielding.html', 'snippet': 'In his return from the disabled list, Gee, the Mets’ sixth starter, couldn’t get through five innings for the first time in his last 52 starts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — Dillon Gee stood on the mound — tossing the ball in the air with one hand, the way someone might when he is bored — as the Mets’ infield converged on him and his manager, Terry Collins, emerged from the dugout to take him out of the game. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/05/sports/04metsweb/04metsweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06