nder airman named Logan Ireland, who recently completed a deployment serving as male, the gender he knows himself to be. Remarkably, after telling his leaders and some peers that his sex was assigned female at birth, he received their support—despite military policy that prevents transgender people from serving openly. Meanwhile, his fiancée, Laila Villanueva, who was assigned male at birth, has a similar scenario, but works without the support of her command.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Transgender, at War and in Love’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T07:36:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fiona Dawson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fiona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dawson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ac5c698-bd4c-5ad8-abd9-9a10edc232b7', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ac5c698-bd4c-5ad8-abd9-9a10edc232b7'}, {'abstract': 'This short documentary shares the challenges of a transgender military couple, who are banned from serving openly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000003720527/transgender-at-war-and-in-love.html', 'snippet': 'This short documentary shares the challenges of a transgender military couple, who are banned from serving openly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This short documentary shares the challenges of a transgender military couple, who are banned from serving openly.', 'source': 'The New York Time