aa8e0fb5827c'}, {'abstract': 'A pretty big deal.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/fracking-and-the-texas-non-miracle/', 'snippet': 'A pretty big deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grr. I’ve been meaning to write about the Texas economic stumble, but have to some extent been scooped by the business desk. Still, there’s more to say, particularly about the role of the energy sector in the previous boom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fracking and the Texas Non-Miracle', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T14:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a3b0ac0-9f7e-5311-9e29-e51d91e6fe74', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a3b0ac0-9f7e-5311-9e29-e51d91e6fe74'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s art world can seem like a boiling caldron of bile and tears heated by a bonfire of money. This transporting show offers relief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/arts/design/review-robert-irwin-shows-a-calming-installation-at-diabeacon.html', 'snippet': 'Today’s art world can seem like a boiling caldron of bile and tears heated by a bonfire of money. This transporting show offers relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of contemporary art is agitating. Gratuitous sexual provocation and moral bullying; sensory irritation and intellectual grandiosity; gaudy spectacle and cults of personality. Roiled by such strident forms of sociopathology, today’s art and its attendant New York society can sometimes seem like a boiling caldron of bile and tears heated by a bonfire of money. In many 