d bright benches in his new “Please Touch the Art” space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Brooklyn Bridge Park, Jeppe Hein’s 18 new installations include a labyrinth of mirrors (reflective planks that recall the Manhattan skyline across the water), timed-cycle fountain (walls of water shoot up from the ground, rotating every so often to create distinct rooms where guests can stand without getting wet) and 16 bright red, playfully shaped benches. The artist aptly titled the lot “Please Touch the Art” — and shows us, in the above video, how to do just that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Enjoy Brooklyn Bridge Park’s New Public Art, According to the Artist', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hein, Jeppe (1974- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Art Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T15:25:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec79bd1-7e3b-5a58-9228-22c4621d0b9a', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec79bd1-7e3b-5a58-9228-22c4621d0b9a'}, {'abstract': 'Sheryl Sandberg’s post on her late husband, Dave Goldberg, marking the end of a 30-day mourning period, has sparked numerous meditations on grief.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/sheryl-sandbergs-post-on-late-husband-sets-off-medit