ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dafaf35-c086-58ae-b478-bde1483449f9', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dafaf35-c086-58ae-b478-bde1483449f9'}, {'abstract': 'The architect and glassblower Alison Berger’s latest lighting fixture is inspired by the anatomy of a pocket watch.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/alison-berger-clock-chandelier/', 'snippet': 'The architect and glassblower Alison Berger’s latest lighting fixture is inspired by the anatomy of a pocket watch.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I like instruments that try to quantify the ephemeral; a barometer traces air pressure, or an astrolabe charts the stars, and this measures the passing of time,” says the artist Alison Berger, gesturing to a printout from the book “Pocket Watches: From the Pendant Watch to the Tourbillon.” The anatomy of the once-everyday trinket, and her training as an architect and as a glassblower, informed her latest creation, the Clock Chandelier. “One gear moves slowly and the other moves quickly — large and small, fast and slow,” she says, a rhythm articulated in the spacing of the chandelier’s lightbulbs and candles suspended from three interlocking bronze and steel rings. Berger, who has made so-called heirlooms for the upcoming generation (think cereal bowls, in lieu of egg cups) for Hermès and has constructed a new façade for a Comme des Garçons store, considered each detail: The candlelit lanterns can be unhooked for cleaning and the rings fit together using pins, as they would in a timepiece. “The chandelier looks open and endless from one view, but on the other side it is more compressed,” Berger says — a metaphor, she explains, for the feeling of, “Oh my god, it’s already 5 o’clock.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/04/t-magazine/04moss-chandelier2/04moss-chandelier2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chandelier That Stands the Tests of Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T19:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T 