icle', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/db6ed72d-1d30-5b07-aace-e2f7971e8737', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db6ed72d-1d30-5b07-aace-e2f7971e8737'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Myanmar, China, Greece and Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/04/june-4-2015-pictures-of-the-day/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Myanmar, China, Greece and Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Myanmar, China, Greece and Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 4, 2015 — Pictures of the Day', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-04T21:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0688f213-da0f-5582-af62-5546fe5063f9', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0688f213-da0f-5582-af62-5546fe5063f9'}, {'abstract': 'This well-loved company, which lost its entire funding base when a Walmart heiress withdrew her support, will leave 15 dancers seeking work after a farewell performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/arts/dance/review-cedar-lake-ballet-taking-its-final-bows.html', 'snippet': 'This well-loved company, which lost its entire funding base when a Walmart heiress withdrew her support, will leave 15 dancers seeking work after a farewell performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As ballet companies across the country struggle to build audiences, especially young audiences, the troupe with one of the youngest, most adoring fan bases is closing. Cedar Lake Contemporary Ballet was founded 12 years ago by Nancy Laurie, a Walmart heiress who, through an unusual single-patron model, financed most of the enterprise — until recently, when she decided to stop. Suddenly, the company was preparing to vacate its Chelsea theater; its next New York show would be its last. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1829, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/05/arts/06CEDAR/06CEDAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7