in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'prefatory • \\ˈpre-fə-ˌtȯr-e\\ • adjective ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | prefatory', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T04:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d900606-a5bc-5c8c-bbf7-9a76aa2dfe55', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d900606-a5bc-5c8c-bbf7-9a76aa2dfe55'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:48 A.M. (Comedy Central) NATIONAL LAMPOON’S ANIMAL HOUSE (1978) Delta House, the misfit fraternity at Faber College, is put on double secret probation by Dean Vernon Wormer (John Vernon) in an attempt to boot it off campus. In response, the fraternity members (Tim Matheson, John Belushi, above, and others) concoct a series of stratagems to improve their grades while making mischief. “At its best,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times, “the movie isn’t strictly satirical, because it doesn’t need to be. The filmmakers have simply supplied the appropriate panty-girdles, crew-neck sweaters, frat-house initiation rites and rituals of the toga party, and let all that idiocy speak — very eloquently, and with a lot of comic fervor — for itself.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pu