rp approach to eurozone negotiations taken by Greece’s finance minister is received sharply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/magazine/re-continental-divide.html', 'snippet': 'The sharp approach to eurozone negotiations taken by Greece’s finance minister is received sharply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our May 24 cover story, Suzy Hansen profiled the new finance minister of Greece, Yanis Varoufakis, whose defiance in financial negotiations with his European counterparts over austerity measures threatens the notion of a united Europe. Varoufakis stated that he would rather resign than lead Greeks further into economic ruin. “It’s not good for Europe,” he told Hansen, “and it’s not good for Greece.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1593, 'width': 1303, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/24/magazine/07threadcover/07threadcover-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Re: Continental Divide', 'kicker': 'The Thread', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Re: Continental Divide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T08:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07299984-2b1d-5fe1-a9bc-de68c91c6ec5', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07299984-2b1d-5fe1-a9bc-de68c91c6ec5'}, {'abstract': 'Looking at the world from on high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/magazine/dronestagrams-view.html', 'snippet': 'Looking at the world from on high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smartphones have sneaked a camera into every pocket and purse, but there is much they can never witness. The drone, though, sees and shares all. On the social network Dronestagram, users upload images and videos they’ve captured in midair, soaring over cathedrals and waterfalls and fireworks from a vantage point we once described as bird’s — or God’s — eye. (Dronestagram is not to be confused with @dronestagram, an Instagram account that shows the sites of attacks by U.S. military drones.) This photograph was shared by Grant Sheehan, who flew his drone over the Kereru Sheep Station in Hawkes Bay, New Zealand. In the gaze of its ovine inhabitants, we glimpse their dim recognition that a new sort of shepherd has arisen.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07endpaper/07mag-07endpaper-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dronestagram’s View', 'kicker': 'End Paper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Overlord', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dronestagram', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T08:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c623934f-6410-59a2-8155-4cc013a60d16', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c623934f-6410-59a2-8155-4cc013a60d16'}, {'abstract': 'The string of numbers that allowed me to stay close to home, and to her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/magazine/a-life-in-a-password.html', 'snippet': 'The string of numbers that allowed me to stay close to home, and to her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a triumph of rotten timing, I began dating my first girlfriend in my final weeks of high school, just before I was to leave India for college in the United States. It was 1999, but it already feels like an unrecognizable age. We had no Skype, and phone calls would have broken the bank. Personal email addresses, however, were newly popular in India, and she had a Hotmail ID. We walked to a cybercafe, near my house in Chennai, to sign me up for a MailExcite account. In my password, I included her date of birth.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-articleLarge.png', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-jumbo.png', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1067, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07herbirthday/07herbirthday-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life in a Password', 'kicker': 'My Internet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Birthday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Subramanian, Samanth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T08:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samanth Subramanian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samanth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Subramanian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/862c92a5-33b1-532e-a2cb-e5586ffeec80', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/862c92a5-33b1-532e-a2cb-e5586ffeec80'}, {'abstract': 'The innocent narcissism of the early Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/magazine/self-googling-in-1997.html', 'snippet': 'The innocent narcissism of the early Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a spring afternoon in 1997 in Vienna, I googled myself for the first time. Technically speaking, of course, I didn’t. Google didn’t exist yet. Altavista’s search engine was the best one around then.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-articleLarge.png', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-jumbo.png', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1159, 'width': 1611, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07firsttime/07firsttime-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Self-Googling in 1997', 'kicker': 'My Internet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Narcissism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T08:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Kehlmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehlmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2eaace4-d8a8-53ca-8fc3-a6b9d96fa93d', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2eaace4-d8a8-53ca-8fc3-a6b9d96fa93d'}, {'abstract': 'Hiding in the long pauses of an ink-and-paper correspondence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/magazine/snail-mail-and-the-safety-of-distance.html', 'snippet': 'Hiding in the long pauses of an ink-and-paper correspondence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fall of 1994, eight years after emigrating from Leningrad to the United States, I started using email on a regular basis. But when I wrote to my friends and parents back home, I avoided this new mode of correspondence, continuing to exchange letters with them. The reasons were not technological but emotional.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/magazine/07snailmail/07mag-07introiosselsidebar-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'height': 603, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 