7:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'NYT Now', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeel Hassan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hassan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58520824-32b7-5edb-a19c-70edd8098a12', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58520824-32b7-5edb-a19c-70edd8098a12'}, {'abstract': 'Friday: Bright spots of street art, more clouds and the original Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/new-york-today-191st-street-now-in-technicolor/', 'snippet': 'Friday: Bright spots of street art, more clouds and the original Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning on this cloud-covered Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: 191st Street Tunnel, Now in Technicolor', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T09:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tatiana Schlossberg and Benjamin Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tatiana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlossberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c25dacbc-90e9-559f-a616-2f2f78378cc2', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c25dacbc-90e9-559f-a616-2f2f78378cc2'}, {'abstract': 'British regulators announced the penalty as part of a settlement for unfairly treating customers after they complained about the improper sales of payment protection insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/06/business/lloyds-banking-group-payment-protection-insurance-fine.html', 'snippet': 'British regulators announced the penalty as part of a settlement for unfairly treating customers after they complained about the improper sales of payment protection insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — British regulators on Friday said they had imposed a fine of about $180 million on the Lloyds Banking Group over its handling of customer complaints about a contentious loan insurance product that has cost the industry billions of dollars. As a result, the bank said it would cut its 2015 bonus pool.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lloyds Bank Fined $180 Million Over Handling of Insurance Complaints', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Conduct Authority (Great Britain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lloyds Banking Group Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T10:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray and Patrick Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61dd1930-f612-57a0-8b3e-1ed74b7fef8b', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61dd1930-f612-57a0-8b3e-1ed74b7fef8b'}, {'abstract': 'A special welcome to the newest member of the sisterhood of people who share my name.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/opinion/to-caitlyn-from-a-caitlin.html', 'snippet': 'A special welcome to the newest member of the sisterhood of people who share my name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Hello, Caitlyn! It is my pleasure indeed to #callyouCaitlyn, as everyone #callsmeCaitlin. Yes, I, too, am a Caitli(y)n, and I’m so pleased to welcome you to the sisterhood. You’re in excellent company! Like Caitlin Lowe, another American Olympian, Caitlin FitzGerald, a talented actress currently on “Masters of Sex,” and Caitlin Macnamara, who became Caitlin Thomas when she married the poet Dylan Thomas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/opinion/05gillWeb/05gillWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Caitlyn, From a Caitlin', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Caitlyn, From a Caitlin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenner, Caitlyn (1949- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T10:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7de82763-24dd-5ab7-8d3c-a4c8ae3c04d1', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7de82763-24dd-5ab7-8d3c-a4c8ae3c04d1'}, {'abstract': 'The sun, for starters. Also lightning, choking on a chicken bone, drowning in the bathtub, and people who text and drive. But probably not terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/opinion/what-to-be-afraid-of.html', 'snippet': 'The sun, for starters. Also lightning, choking on a chicken bone, drowning in the bathtub, and people who text and drive. But probably not terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some time ago, a friend of mine was hit by a bus in New York, one of almost 5,000 pedestrians killed in traffic every year. I also lost a nephew to gun violence — one of more than 11,000 Americans slain by firearms in this country. And I fell out of a tree that I was trying to prune in my backyard. I was O.K. But the guy next to me in the trauma ward was paralyzed from his fall. He was taking down his Christmas lights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Be Afraid Of', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dfad45d-fcc2-533b-8b8d-ba44d22bc01c', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dfad45d-fcc2-533b-8b8d-ba44d22bc01c'}, {'abstract': 'A look at what the former House speaker Dennis Hastert is accused of, and why the government is so interested in what people do with their money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/06/upshot/when-its-a-crime-to-withdraw-money-from-your-bank.html', 'snippet': 'A look at what the former House speaker Dennis Hastert is accused of, and why the government is so interested in what people do with their money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis Hastert has not been indicted on a charge of sexual abuse, nor has he been indicted on a charge of paying money he was not legally allowed to pay. The indictment of Mr. Hastert, a former House speaker, released last week, lays out two counts: taking money out of the bank the wrong way, and then lying to the F.B.I. about what he did with the money.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/upshot/04UP-Hastert/04UP-Hastert-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/03/upshot/04UP-Hastert/04UP-Hastert-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/03/upshot/04UP-Hastert/04UP-Hastert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup