 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6ecd323-79f0-5999-8aa5-3683db93b9de', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6ecd323-79f0-5999-8aa5-3683db93b9de'}, {'abstract': 'When seven Republican presidential hopefuls roll into Iowa this weekend for Senator Joni Ernst’s inaugural “Roast and Ride,” only one — Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin — will truly be cruising on a motorcycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/06/05/today-in-politics-campaign-trail-makes-room-for-long-fly-balls-and-weekend/', 'snippet': 'When seven Republican presidential hopefuls roll into Iowa this weekend for Senator Joni Ernst’s inaugural “Roast and Ride,” only one — Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin — will truly be cruising on a motorcycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Friday morning from Washington. Though the ever-growing Republican field will make for a hectic late summer, for now, there’s room to mix work and play, as, for example, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey proved deft with a softball bat, and as a group of Republican candidates prepared for a day of roast pork and motorcycles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Politics: Campaign Trail Makes Room for Long Fly Balls and Weekend', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9e708d-5159-563d-8c64-53410b019c7e', 'word_count': 1422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9e708d-5159-563d-8c64-53410b019c7e'}, {'abstract': 'Special coupons to buy food at farmers’ markets are growing as a tool to improve nutrition among those on food stamps and to support the markets as well.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/closing-the-broccoli-gap/', 'snippet': 'Special coupons to buy food at farmers’ markets are growing as a tool to improve nutrition among those on food stamps and to support the markets as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, New York City’s Department of Health and Mental Hygiene invented Health Bucks, a program designed to help the city’s poor to eat more vegetables and fruit. City agencies and community groups distributed Health Bucks in high-poverty areas. If you spent $5 in food stamps at a farmers market, the Health Bucks program would give you a coupon for $2, which you could use or save.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 