}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2b1a86e-a4bc-5305-b999-95148773809f', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2b1a86e-a4bc-5305-b999-95148773809f'}, {'abstract': 'The UP channel tries for movie-franchise momentum on Sunday night with its second film adapted from the romance-novel series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/arts/television/in-love-finds-you-in-charm-an-amish-woman-ponders-a-bigger-world.html', 'snippet': 'The UP channel tries for movie-franchise momentum on Sunday night with its second film adapted from the romance-novel series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Second-tier cable channels looking to build an audience need anchors. A solid series can be one, of course, but so can a movie franchise, whether it’s the Hallmark Channel’s “Good Witch” collection or Syfy’s “Sharknado” invasion. The UP channel tries for movie-franchise momentum on Sunday night at 7 with “Love Finds You in Charm,” its second film adapted from the romance-novel series.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE5/07GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE5/07GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE5/07GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE5/07GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,