alled the most unpredictable German painter working today. Starting Wednesday, a selection of his self-portraits from the 1980s, his “Computer Paintings” and “Switch Paintings” from the 1990s and more recent works, including appropriated advertising signage, will be on view at the New Museum. Billed as his first major New York exhibition, the show, “Albert Oehlen: Home and Garden,” was organized by Massimiliano Gioni, the museum’s artistic director.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 617}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 995, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1990, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/arts/07GUIDE4/07GUIDE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 