 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Midler, Bette', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T17:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lela Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2e509c-c76b-5281-bc50-c0c8e7116dd4', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2e509c-c76b-5281-bc50-c0c8e7116dd4'}, {'abstract': 'When we correct a child too often, the message is that she’ll never get it right.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/are-we-helping-our-kids-or-nagging-them/', 'snippet': 'When we correct a child too often, the message is that she’ll never get it right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a parent’s job to teach our children: to do the right thing, use the right words, learn and practice the skills they’ll need to handle life at school and out in the world. But some mornings — after a seemingly endless stream of corrections intended to help my daughter — I end up feeling as if I am sending my unlucky child off to school with the extra burden of never getting anything right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Helping Our Kids or Nagging Them?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he