that she takes a nightclub performance as seriously as any Broadway role. Her latest show, “Starting Over,” which opened on Thursday at 54 Below, is a fully developed concept in which Ms. Lavin, 77, tells her story mostly in song. As the title suggests, this is not a conventional summing up with a beginning, a middle and an end, but a repeated cycle of new beginnings, the latest of which is her seemingly blissful 10-year marriage to Steve Bakunas, the drummer in her band.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Linda Lavin, Scratching Out Fresh Starts, at 54 Below', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating Fresh Starts With Smarts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavin, Linda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T20:03:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bda1e347-bd17-5522-ae14-f7c835dc18fe', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bda1e347-bd17-5522-ae14-f7c835dc18fe'}, {'abstract': 'The period-instrument ensemble offered a program of Beethoven, Haydn and Witt in its season finale at Alice Tully Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/06/arts/music/review-american-classical-orchestra-takes-on-friedrich-witt.html', 'snippet': 'The period-instrument ensemble offered a program of Beethoven, Haydn and Witt in its season finale at Alice Tully Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a conversation starter: What’s easier to bear? A boring performance of a boring piece or a boring performance of a masterpiece? On Thursday at Alice Tully Hall, the period-instrument American Classical Orchestra, under the direction of Thomas Crawford, offered both in a lackluster season finale. The program opened with a humdrum performance of Friedrich Witt’s justifiably overlooked Symphony in A and ended with a slack reading of Beethoven’s “Pastoral” Symphony.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: American Classical Orchestra Takes on Friedrich Witt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking a Chance on Friedrich Witt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alice Tully Hall (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witt, Friedrich (1770-1836)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Classical Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T20:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af475b50-dbfc-5cdc-b9f6-347626d5610d', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af475b50-dbfc-5cdc-b9f6-347626d5610d'}, {'abstract': 'The first time most guys go into a strip club, it’s party time. My first time was a little different.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/my-first-time-in-a-strip-club/', 'snippet': 'The first time most guys go into a strip club, it’s party time. My first time was a little different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Editor’s note: Austin Meyer is the winner of Nicholas Kristof’s 2015 Win-a-Trip contest. He will receive his master’s in journalism from Stanford University later this month. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My First Time in a Strip Club', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heroin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Naloxone (Drug)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wen, Leana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T20:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f98cb11-99f4-5707-9427-912480879ec9', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f98cb11-99f4-5707-9427-912480879ec9'}, {'abstract': 'After meeting at a wedding, two online specialists kept looking for ways to meet up without the interference of a screen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/fashion/weddings/digital-experts-head-offline-for-love.html', 'snippet': 'After meeting at a wedding, two online specialists kept looking for ways to meet up without the interference of a screen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Noland-Conlow first saw K