ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ea8a351c-fd30-5e47-bd2d-c34314d7d9fd'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion houses are offering clothes and services to nominees in an effort to jazz up outfits this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/fashion/the-tony-awards-get-dressed-up.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion houses are offering clothes and services to nominees in an effort to jazz up outfits this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little after 5 p.m. on Thursday afternoon, Beth Malone stood in the Manhattan offices of the fashion public relations company KCD trying not to appear out of place. It was a losing battle.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tony Awards Get Dressed Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Designers Lend a Hand to the Tonys', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berstein, Jacob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wintour, Anna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Long, William Ivey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN THEATER WING', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KCD', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malone, Beth (1960- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T21:20:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01ada36c-d2c9-52ee-a025-2231d57c7f67', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01ada36c-d2c9-52ee-a025-2231d57c7f67'}, {'abstract': 'Americans are losing out on building not just a sport, but also a business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/05/magazine/why-is-us-womens-soccer-still-fighting-to-exist.html', 'snippet': 'Americans are losing out on building not just a sport, but also a business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With two minutes to go in stoppage time in the quarterfinal match of the Women’s World Cup 2011, Brazil was leading the United States 2-1. As the U.S. offense advanced for its last possible possession, the crowd in Dresden chanted “U-S-A!” But on ESPN, the announcer Ian Darke was already calling it. “It will go down as the U.S.A.’s worst performance ever in the Women’s World Cup,” he told his viewers: going home a top-eight loser in the quarters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/magazine/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/05/magazine/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/magazine/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/05/magazine/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1/05mag-fifa-womens-world-cup-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbn