 '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a74bba3-2143-5105-982f-0ade41bd1e33', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a74bba3-2143-5105-982f-0ade41bd1e33'}, {'abstract': 'In the Brooklyn shop with a 1940 Buick in front lives a kooky, pell-mell paradise: a forest of ephemera that’s open every day until midnight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/nyregion/eclectic-collectibles-and-antiques-in-williamsburg-is-a-cabinet-of-wonders.html', 'snippet': 'In the Brooklyn shop with a 1940 Buick in front lives a kooky, pell-mell paradise: a forest of ephemera that’s open every day until midnight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Music lures pedestrians into Eclectic Collectibles and Antiques at 285 Metropolitan Avenue. Oldies, specifically. “I Guess That’s Why They Call It the Blues” (Elton John, from 1983) blared from the entrance on a recent sunny afternoon. The nondescript storefront would be easy to miss if not for the music and a menacing antique car parked at the curb: a tar-black 1940 Buick Super that evokes pinstripe suits, Tommy guns and Sonny Corleone’s assassination in “The Godfather.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eclectic Collectibles and Antiques in Williamsburg Is a Cabinet of Wonders', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cabinets of Wonders ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eclectic Collectibles and Antiques (Brooklyn, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T23:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'arti