kage was found on a ridge at an altitude of 11,200 feet, the army statement said, close to the epicenter of a second major earthquake. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nepal: More Victims Reported in Helicopter Crash', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia; Nepal: More Victims Reported in Helicopter Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T23:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bhadra Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bhadra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/964274a6-c2c9-5a51-82fa-aacc56d15a32', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964274a6-c2c9-5a51-82fa-aacc56d15a32'}, {'abstract': 'The rich could get much richer if American Pharoah, who has banked $3,730,300 for Zayat Stables can earn the winner’s share of $800,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/06/06/sports/purses.html', 'snippet': 'The rich could get much richer if American Pharoah, who has banked $3,730,300 for Zayat Stables can earn the winner’s share of $800,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rich could get much richer if American Pharoah, who has banked $3,730,300 for Zayat Stables can earn the winner’s share of $800,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Money Horse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-05T23:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a9e9baf2-0dee-599b-9f99-b3d1bca98785', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a9e9baf2-0dee-599b-9f99-b3d1bca98785'}, {'abstract': 'Estela, in NoLIta, made the new rankings of the World’s 50 Best Restaurants, at No. 90, but Pinterest and MindShare employees ate there because they’d “heard it was good for groups.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/nyregion/drawn-to-estela-but-not-by-a-50-best-list.html', 'snippet': 'Estela, in NoLIta, made the new rankings of the World’s 50 Best Restaurants, at No. 90, but Pinterest and MindShare employees ate there because they’d “heard it was good for groups.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the World’s 50 Best Restaurants announced its 2015 rankings last week, the only new American restaurant among upstarts from India, Dubai, South Korea and Russia — and perennial American contenders like Per Se and Le Bernardin — was Estela, a small, beverage-driven restaurant from Thomas Carter, the former beverage director of Blue Hill at Stone Barns, and Ignacio Mattos, a chef mentored by Alice Waters. While Estela is new to the list, coming in at No. 90 — naturally, the 50 Best list goes to 100 — it is not new to New York City, having occupied a space on East Houston Street in NoLIta for a couple of years.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/