8078cb4-6a47-59e5-afe3-23d366b771ce'}, {'abstract': 'If people were going to judge my book by its cover, what would they say about a different kind of author photo?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/how-to-pose-like-a-man.html', 'snippet': 'If people were going to judge my book by its cover, what would they say about a different kind of author photo?', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE cover my publisher chose for my new novel, “The Unfortunate Importance of Beauty,” was indeed very beautiful, but more feminine than I would have ideally liked. It was mostly white, but all the way at the top were the gorgeous chin and red lips of a young woman. Not wanting to be a “difficult author,” I decided not to ask my editor to find a new cover. (She had already been kind enough to change it once.) Instead, I decided to counteract the cover by other means, starting with my author photo.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1949, 'width': 1949, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07POSE/07POSE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Pose Like a Man', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Pose Like a Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-06T18:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Filipacchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Filipacchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbae4220-f1d3-5675-bc5e-b21cddb82394', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbae4220-f1d3-5675-bc5e-b21cddb82394'}, {'abstract': 'It is encouraging that more members of Congress have begun championing privacy in national security debates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/hackers-can-be-fought-without-violating-americans-rights.html', 'snippet': 'It is encouraging that more members of Congress have begun championing privacy in national security debates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The scope and sophistication of recent cyberattacks on American government, business and personal accounts are chilling. The latest, a breach of federal personnel records that could affect more than four million current and former employees, is a reminder that enhancing the nation’s cyberdefenses has to be an urgent priority.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 745}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 966, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/07sun1/07sun1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Can Be Fought Without Violating Americans’ Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sensible Response to Cyberattacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poe, Ted', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare and Defense', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-06T18:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/305b1e5d-ee69-545f-9da0-bee90d61f37c', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/305b1e5d-ee69-545f-9da0-bee90d61f37c'}, {'abstract': 'In Republican states, there is much less therapy than there is in Democratic ones, and people are suffering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/talking-red-state-blues.html', 'snippet': 'In Republican states, there is much less therapy than there is in Democratic ones, and people are suffering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN you mull over the differences between states that vote for Republicans in presidential elections and states that vote for Democrats, what do you think about? Perhaps religion: People in red states are far more likely to believe in God. Or maybe media consumption: More people in blue states like NPR.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Red State Blues', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talking Red State Blues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-06T18:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Stephens-Davidowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens-Davidowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ece24fbe-33aa-5459-b94b-481d52918685', 'word_count': 1600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ece24fbe-33aa-5459-b94b-481d52918685'}, {'abstract': 'Steamy days can defeat the body’s natural cooling system, making high temperatures that much more dangerous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/opinion/sunday/the-deadly-combination-of-heat-and-humidity.html', 'snippet': 'Steamy days can defeat the body’s natural cooling system, making high temperatures that much more dangerous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE most deadly weather-related disasters aren’t necessarily caused by floods, droughts or hurricanes. They can be caused by heat waves, like the sweltering blanket that’s taken over 2,500 lives in India in recent weeks.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'prin