’ singles final at the French Open featured two Americans, and other players from the United States made it deep into the tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/07/sports/tennis/americans-dominate-boys-play-in-paris.html', 'snippet': 'The boys’ singles final at the French Open featured two Americans, and other players from the United States made it deep into the tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — When North Carolina’s Tommy Paul beat San Diego’s Taylor Harry Fritz, 7-6 (2), 2-6, 6-2, Saturday in the first all-American boys’ final at the French Open, it formally ended a tournament in which the future of United States men’s tennis had already been declared the unanimous winner.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1266, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/sports/JUNIORS/JUNIORS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 