bout a struggling writer and a tech billionaire who share the same name, hums with the static of the cosmos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/books/review-book-of-numbers-by-joshua-cohen-is-narrative-as-rich-as-the-web.html', 'snippet': 'Joshua Cohen’s new novel, about a struggling writer and a tech billionaire who share the same name, hums with the static of the cosmos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alive with talk and dense with data, Joshua Cohen’s novel “Book of Numbers” reads as if Philip Roth’s work were fired into David Foster Wallace’s inside the Hadron particle collider.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 703, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1405, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08BOOKCOHEN/08BOOKCOHEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Book of Numbers,’ by Joshua Cohen, Is Narrative as Rich as the Web', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tale as Expansive as the Internet Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Dwight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Joshua (1980- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Book of Numbers (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-07T21:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0e9f27f-8ed5-586f-b568-543e930e61d1', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0e9f27f-8ed5-586f-b568-543e930e61d1'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Braun, who became known in the ’60s and ’70s as the go-to inventor of elaborate album covers, reflects on the design of “Sticky Fingers” and the Stones’ logo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/arts/music/art-of-the-rolling-stones-behind-that-zipper-and-that-tongue.html', 'snippet': 'Craig Braun, who became known in the ’60s and ’70s as the go-to inventor of elaborate album covers, reflects on the design of “Sticky Fingers” and the Stones’ logo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Rolling Stones prepared recently to rerelease “Sticky Fingers,” their classic 1971 album featuring hits like “Wild Horses” and “Brown Sugar,” the manufacturing process hit a snag: The functional zipper from Andy Warhol’s bulging blue jean album cover, recreated for some new deluxe editions, was taking longer than expected to produce, Universal Music announced, pushing back the release to Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art of the Rolling Stones: Behind That Zipper and That Tongue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind That Zipper and That Tongue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Craig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasche, John (1945- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sound Packaging Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-07T21:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa015f9-dbab-5aca-94a0-ae01b9484f16', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa015f9-dbab-5aca-94a0-ae01b9484f16'}, {'abstract': 'Will Rawls’s choreographic installation at the Abrons Arts Center marks the centennial of the Henry Street Settlement neighborhood playhouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/arts/dance/review-settlement-house-a-tribute-to-henry-streets-100-year-history.html', 'snippet': 'Will Rawls’s choreographic installation at the Abrons Arts Center marks the centennial of the Henry Street Settlement neighborhood playhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been 100 years since the Henry Street Settlement on the Lower East Side opened its neighborhood playhouse, a little theater that became a home to Martha Graham, John Cage and Alwin Nikolais. On Saturday, “Settlement House,” a choreographic installation organized by Will Rawls, celebrated the playhouse’s centennial by performing there and next door at the Abrons Arts Center. A program note introduced the guiding questions: “whether one can actually dance about architecture” and “whether and how architecture might be made to dance.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08RAWLS/08RAWLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08RAWLS/08RAWLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08RAWLS/08RAWLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08RAWLS/08RAWLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/arts/08RAWLS/08RAWLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail':