 PJ Harvey, Yoko Ono and many more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/t-magazine/the-many-pals-of-peaches.html', 'snippet': 'A new book of photos by the musician’s longtime tour photographer Holger Talinski features the artist with Drew Barrymore, PJ Harvey, Yoko Ono and many more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than two decades, the performance artist and musician Merrill Nisker, better known as Peaches, has sought to upend gender norms, smash stereotypes and tackle taboos. In her new book, “What Else Is in the Teaches of Peaches” ($28, Akashic), the Berlin-based, Canada-born provocateur has teamed up with her longtime tour photographer Holger Talinski to look back at a brazen career that has captured the attention of outsider artists and massive pop stars alike, ranging from Michael Stipe to PJ Harvey to Iggy Pop. “Holger shows the exhaustion, the work, the relaxation, the elation, the parties, the quiet moments and the family visits,” writes Peaches in the foreword. “It is amazing for me to look back at these photos and understand how much I have packed into these years.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Pals of Peaches', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2801db9e-3ac6-50d6-9697-68ba3ac3d2db', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2801db9e-3ac6-50d6-9697-68ba3ac3d2db'}, {'abstract': 'In a cacophony of crisscrossing lines, the artist Janaina Tschäpe finds expression for Stephen Burt’s reflection on the wonderful, ter