he First Affiliated Hospital of Kunming Medical University, seriously wounding her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/world/asia/08sino-nurse2/08sino-nurse2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/world/asia/08sino-nurse2/08sino-nurse2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/world/asia/08sino-nurse2/08sino-nurse2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/08/world/asia/08sino-nurse2/08sino-nurse2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/world/asia/08sino-nurse2/08sino-nurse2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack on Nurse Stirs Discussion of a Medical Strike in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hippocratic Community (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kunming (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T10:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8be54daa-ec67-5a93-bf39-f124a91219ed', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8be54daa-ec67-5a93-bf39-f124a91219ed'}, {'abstract': 'To the man who was raised to hunt for his dinner, a visit from loggerhead wasn’t a nature sighting. What could I do?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/i-saw-a-turtle-my-father-saw-food/', 'snippet': 'To the man who was raised to hunt for his dinner, a visit from loggerhead wasn’t a nature sighting. What could I do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The turtles didn’t stay on the beach that year. Maybe it had something to do with the stadium lights that lit up the nearby golf course so military officers could swing their clubs through the night. Or the big white domes that protected satellite dishes but looked like Epcot moons. We’d lived on MacDill Air Force Base near Tampa for a year, not far from the beach. I’d already seen two turtles who’d wandered from the surf — one in a sand trap and one by the side of the road. Then on one September day, I arrived home from school, and the loggerhead was there on the sidewalk leading to our mobile home, baking in the Florida sun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/opinion/08menagerieWeb/08menagerieWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Saw a Turtle, My Father Saw Food', 'kicker': 'Menagerie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turtles and Tortoises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T10:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Portwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Portwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ae9a5ce-6d4c-598f-ad10-a6692e516125', 'word_coun