ald Tribune archives: President Wilson replied to Germany’s note on the Lusitania in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Mr. Wilson’s new Note to Germany has been approved by the Cabinet and was to have been despatched to Berlin today [June 5]. It is understood that the communication is vigorous in tone and that it denies the allegations contained in Germany’s last Note that the Lusitania was armed or carrying explosives. According to the Daily Telegraph’s New York correspondent, it is hardly expected that Berlin will answer the new Note until Count Bernstorff’s envoy reaches Germany, so there is a prospect of two or three weeks elapsing before a reply is received.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/blogs/06iht-oldjune06-sam/06iht-oldjune06-sam-jumbo.png', 'height': 866, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/blogs/06iht-oldjune06-sam/06iht-oldjune06-sam-superJumbo.png', 'height': 866, 'width': 524, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/blogs/06iht-oldjune06-sam/06iht-oldjune06-sam-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/06/blogs/06iht-oldjune06-sam/06iht-oldjune06-sam-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/06/blogs/06iht-oldjune06-sam/06iht-oldjune06-sam-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1915: President’s Reply on Lusitania', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'GERMANY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'RMS Lusitania (Ship)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T13:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9dc85d-e54b-5ace-8546-c87352f28571', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9dc85d-e54b-5ace-8546-c87352f28571'}, {'abstract': 'With the Cavaliers and the Warriors both missing the net in the extra period, Game 2 of the N.B.A. finals came down to foul calls, no-calls and free throws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/sports/basketball/nba-finals-in-overtime-missed-shots-and-foul-calls-were-the-key.html', 'snippet': 'With the Cavaliers and the Warriors both missing the net in the extra period, Game 2 of the N.B.A. finals came down to foul calls, no-calls and free throws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in N.B.A. finals history, Games 1 and 2 went to overtime. Once again, fans were treated to five tense, vital minutes between two of the best teams in basketball, the Golden State Warriors and the Cleveland Cavaliers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/sports/09OVERTIMEweb2/09OVERTIMEweb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/sports/09OVERTIMEweb2/09OVERTIMEweb