act': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: GIs will fight alongside South Vietnamese troops in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/1965-gis-will-fight-in-ground-war/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: GIs will fight alongside South Vietnamese troops in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The State Department disclosed today [June 8] that U.S. forces in Vietnam have been authorized to fight alongside South Vietnamese troops — a move expected to produce full-scale battle between Americans and the Communist guerrillas. The department’s press officer, Robert J. McCloskey, emphasized that U.S. combat assistance was conditional on a request from the South Vietnamese government. But it seemed certain to most observers that U.S. troops were being fully committed to a direct ground war campaign against the Viet Cong. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, June 9, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: GIs Will Fight in Ground War', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'VIETNAM WAR', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T16:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9da6366d-3f6b-5a42-9c56-f424740bd434', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9da6366d-3f6b-5a42-9c56-f424740bd434'}, {'abstract': 'An estimated 20 to 50 percent of women continue hurting after mastectomy, but doctors and patients alike have at times not taken note of the issue.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/pain-after-breast-cancer-surgery-pmps/', 'snippet': 'An estimated 20 to 50 percent of women continue hurting after mastectomy, but doctors and patients alike have at times not taken note of the issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I could hear the anxiety in my sister’s voice. A week after her double mastectomy and breast reconstruction for breast cancer, she had developed a burning sensation under her right arm where her surgeon had removed several dozen lymph nodes for a postoperative biopsy. The throbbing and itching were so intense it felt “like poison ivy lit by a blowtorch.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09breast-cancer-pain/09breast-cancer-pain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09breast-cancer-pain/09breast-cancer-pain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09breast-cancer-pain/09breast-cancer-pain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09breast-cancer-pain/09breast-cancer-pain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 1501, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09breast-cancer-pain/09breast-cancer-pain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height':