 woman wore form-fitting clothes and a scarf wrapped around her head that revealed a few of her blond tresses. The men carried backpacks to official meetings. Nothing all that unusual in most places, but enough to touch off a firestorm of criticism this weekend from Iranian lawmakers, who accused their visitors of flouting Islamic law by, as one put it, wearing “extremely weird clothing.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Backpacks and Exposed Skin, European Officials Roil Iranians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'E.U. Officials Rile Iranians With Wardrobe Decisions ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaake, Marietje (1978- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larijani, Ali', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Veiling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zarif, Mohammad Javad', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weidenholzer, Josef (1950- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T20:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1875348d-fc9d-531b-94cd-f5c5a95f78ab', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1875348d-fc9d-531b-94cd-f5c5a95f78ab'}, {'abstract': 'Casey Conine, who seeks damages of at least $50,000, said the University of Illinois ignored its own protocol after she sustained a concussion in October.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/sports/soccer/former-soccer-player-sues-illinois-saying-concussion-was-mishandled.html', 'snippet': 'Casey Conine, who seeks damages of at least $50,000, said the University of Illinois ignored its own protocol after she sustained a concussion in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former women’s soccer player at Illinois has filed a lawsuit against the university, alleging that her concussion was mishandled and her career ruined after the team ignored protocol. The suit, filed Monday afternoon in Champaign County Circuit Court, seeks damages of at least $50,000, though the amount could be far greater.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Soccer Player Sues Illinois, Saying Concussion Was Mishandled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Illinois Player Files Suit Alleging Soccer Team Mishandled Her Concussion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conine, Casey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conine, Casey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T20:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b9fda73-3619-5104-ba5e-94899372912d', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b9fda73-3619-5104-ba5e-94899372912d'}, {'abstract': 'John Leland shares some of the insight he’s gathered from six months spent interviewing some of New York’s oldest residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/06/08/six-elderly-new-yorkers-provide-lessons-on-aging-what-one-reporter-learned/', 'snippet': 'John Leland shares some of the insight he’s gathered from six months spent interviewing some of New York’s oldest residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the start of the year, I’ve been reporting on six New Yorkers over the age of 85, but the guiding voice in my head has often been that of a much younger man, Karl Pillemer, one of several gerontologists I interviewed at the start of the project. When Dr. Pillemer started in the field, he viewed old age the way many of us do, as a problem to be solved. People’s bodies broke down, their minds lost function, they drained billions out of the health care system. “I was busy rewriting the Book of Job,” he said. It made for grim work. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/nyregion/20150607OLDweb3/20150607OLDweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/nyregion/20150607OLDweb3/20150607OLDweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/nyregion/20150607OLDweb