ytimes.com/2015/06/09/upshot/the-evidence-points-to-a-better-way-to-fight-insomnia.html', 'snippet': 'A review of data shows that cognitive behavior therapy works better than sleep medications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One weekend afternoon a couple of years ago, while turning a page of the book I was reading to my daughters, I fell asleep. That’s when I knew it was time to do something about my insomnia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09up-insomnia/09up-insomnia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Evidence Points to a Better Way to Fight Insomnia', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insomnia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T21:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdd684d5-b2bc-5b5e-bea4-a775c949a8d3', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdd684d5-b2bc-5b5e-bea4-a775c949a8d3'}, {'abstract': 'In Tuscany, the property celebrated its birthday with fireworks, many a French 75 and no shortage of Missoni-dressed guests.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/fifty-years-hotel-il-pellicano/', 'snippet': 'In Tuscany, the property celebrated its birthday with fireworks, many a French 75 and no shortage of Missoni-dressed guests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hotel Il Pellicano has a 50-year history of attracting a certain jet set — Hollywood royalty, fashion-world darlings, very beautiful and important humans — to its cliffside pool on the Tuscan coastline. And its impossibly chic creative director Marie-Louise Sciò, whose father, Roberto, bought the hotel in 1979, summoned regulars like the actor Josh Hartnett and his girlfriend, Tamsin Egerton, to celebrate the property’s birthday over the weekend. All gleefully flew in, heeding the suggested dress code: Missoni meets Slim Aarons (who photographed Il Pellicano’s socialite scene for more than 25 years). The crowd, co-hosted by T’s editor in chief Deborah Needleman, was as festive as the grounds, dressed up with colorful prints, strung with twinkling lights and toasted with fireworks after a fiery sun set below the perimeter’s cypress trees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fifty Years of Chic at Hotel Il Pellicano', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-08T21:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff2624c-f896-5a36-8ccf-e5db5e7b1ba9', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff2624c-f896-5a36-8ccf-e5db5e7b1ba9'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that receiving an IUD right after a cesarean delivery can help reduce unintended pregnancies and risks like prematurity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/health/study-backs-iuds-for-new-mothers-with-no-waiting.html', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that receiving an IUD right after a cesarean delivery can help reduce unintended pregnancies and risks like prematurity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After childbirth, some new mothers wishing to avoid another pregnancy ask their doctors to provide reversible contraception, like an intrauterine device. But normally, new mothers are told to return for contraception six weeks after giving birth — after fully half of them have already resumed sexual relations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/science/09CONTRACEPTION2/09CONTRACEPTION2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'su