ged nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/world/asia/earthquake-prods-nepal-parties-to-make-constitution-deal.html', 'snippet': 'They agreed to a federal model with eight provinces that would allow them to form a government and rebuild the quake-ravaged nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATHMANDU, Nepal — After almost a decade of friction over central constitutional issues, Nepal’s major political parties reached an accord on Monday night, agreeing to a federal model with eight provinces that would allow them to form a government involving all major parties and rebuild the quake-ravaged nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earthquake Prods Nepal Parties to Make Constitution Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quake Prods Nepal Parties to Make Constitution Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unified Communist Party of Nepal (Maoist)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T01:07:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bhadra Sharma and Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bhadra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30d9af54-9bce-537a-8b8f-25fc424b61b9', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30d9af54-9bce-537a-8b8f-25fc424b61b9'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Steven Beshear signed an executive order raising the hourly minimum wage for certain state employees while Republicans worried that the move could hurt the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/us/kentucky-governor-raises-minimum-wage-with-executive-order.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Steven Beshear signed an executive order raising the hourly minimum wage for certain state employees while Republicans worried that the move could hurt the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Gov. Steven L. Beshear of Kentucky signed an executive order on Monday raising the hourly minimum wage for certain state employees to $10.10. The change, which angered state Republicans and drew praise from the governor’s fellow Democrats, affects almost 800 employees, including those making the current hourly minimum of $7.25. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/us/KENTUCKY/KENTUCKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/us/KENTUCKY/KENTUCKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 868}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/us/KENTUCKY/KENTUCKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/us/KENTUCKY/KENTUCKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1416, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/us/KENTUCKY/KENTUCKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy