ney’s office said on Monday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Prosecutor Is Selected for Patz Retrial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Prosecutor Is Selected for Patz Retrial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patz, Etan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Pedro (1961- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seidemann, Joel J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T01:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ee5063-6fc2-5e8a-893c-d27a6ca8a4b0', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ee5063-6fc2-5e8a-893c-d27a6ca8a4b0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bond funded Australia’s victory in the 1983 America’s Cup, but several of his other business ventures led to convictions of misconduct and the largest corporate fraud in Australian history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/world/asia/alan-bond-yachting-hero-and-convict-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bond funded Australia’s victory in the 1983 America’s Cup, but several of his other business ventures led to convictions of misconduct and the largest corporate fraud in Australian history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — Alan Bond, who bankrolled Australia’s historic victory in the 1983 America’s Cup yacht race, and who was also a brash billion-dollar dealmaker who was sent to jail for what at the time was the largest corporate fraud in Australian history, died on Friday in Perth, Australia. He was 77. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/world/09bond-obit/09bond-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alan Bond, Yachting Hero and Convict, Dies at 77', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alan Bond, 77, Yachting Hero and Convict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Innis, Michelle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "AMERICA'S CUP", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sailboats and Sailing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bond, Alan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T01:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Innis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Innis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/081f5ef5-34c5-5c51-b131-2cec7ed522ca', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/081f5ef5-34c5-5c51-b131-2cec7ed522ca'}, {'abstract': 'A little sleight of hand on the part of the Puzzles & Games team brings you a relatively timely puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/08/by-a-nose/', 'snippet': 'A little sleight of hand on the part of the Puzzles & Games team brings you a relatively timely puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY PUZZLE — Today’s puzzle by Roy Leban runs because of a different, four-legged runner. In case you missed it, AMERICAN PHAROAH won the Triple Crown on Saturday, after leaving the other horses in the dust at the Belmont Stakes. He is the first horse to win the Triple Crown since AFFIRMED won in 1978. That’s quite a long dry spell.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By a Nose', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}