tandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/09/opinion/09Schuck/09Schuck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/opinion/09Schuck/09Schuck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Creating a Market for Refugees in Europe', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creating a Market for Refugees in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schuck, Peter H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T07:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter H. Schuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Schuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/58103b5b-23c6-5eaf-9fab-b095ae809d5e', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58103b5b-23c6-5eaf-9fab-b095ae809d5e'}, {'abstract': 'After almost 50 years, the Mauritshuis museum in The Hague has declared ‘‘Saul and David,’’ one of Rembrandt’s most important biblical works, to be authentic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/arts/international/lifting-doubt-over-a-rembrandt.html', 'snippet': 'After almost 50 years, the Mauritshuis museum in The Hague has declared ‘‘Saul and David,’’ one of Rembrandt’s most important biblical works, to be authentic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — The painting was sliced down the middle and straight through its center in the 19th century, probably to be sold as two Rembrandt portraits. At some point in the next 40 years, it was sutured back together with pieces of an entirely different canvas, and layered with paint to cover up its scars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 818, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1636, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/09iht-rembrandt09-toned/09iht-rembrandt09-toned-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt