dit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/opinion/10krastev/10krastev-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/opinion/10krastev/10krastev-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/opinion/10krastev/10krastev-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/opinion/10krastev/10krastev-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/opinion/10krastev/10krastev-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Macedonia at the Crossroads', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Macedonia at the crossroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Macedonia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T10:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Krastev', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krastev', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/25cc640c-1cdc-5a36-8cbb-8dba63348bf5', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25cc640c-1cdc-5a36-8cbb-8dba63348bf5'}, {'abstract': 'Reducing investments in companies that mine and use coal is only a first step. There’s still all that oil to worry about.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/opinion/norway-divests-from-coal.html', 'snippet': 'Reducing investments in companies that mine and use coal is only a first step. There’s still all that oil to worry about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Norwegian Parliament voted on Friday to order the country’s huge oil fund — at $890 billion, the world’s largest sovereign wealth fund — to pull billions of dollars of investments out of companies that derive 30 percent or more of their business from mining or burning coal. The move is a major boost to the three-year-old campaign to persuade large investors to divest their fossil fuel stocks. And it could add to the momentum toward concrete action at the climate-change summit conference to be held in Paris in December.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Norway Divests From Coal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Norway Divests From Coal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T10:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bec8d6b-bad5-57d0-b8c9-5507adf040af', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bec8d6b-bad5-57d0-b8c9-5507adf040af'}, {'abstract': 'Prediction markets would be a way to prevent candidates from sidestepping fund-raising restrictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/upshot/want-to-bet-that-jeb-bush-is-running.html', 'snippet': 'Prediction markets would be a way to prevent candidates from sidestepping fund-raising restrictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The potential candidate Jeb Bush — who everyone knows is running — has not faced the fund-raising restrictions that election law imposes on those of his rivals who are officially declared candidates. He has accomplished this by seemingly pretending that he is not actually running for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/09/upshot/09UP-Bushbet/09UP-Bushbet-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Bet That Jeb Bush Is Running?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d041dece-c324-5d6f-908c-a049bf342f28', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d041dece-c324-5d6f-908c-a049bf342f28'}, {'abstract': 'The sentence fragment ‘I can’t even’ is the latest in a long line of phrases deployed by millennials to obscure from adults what they really mean.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/magazine/when-you-literally-cant-even-understand-your-teenager.html', 'snippet': 'The sentence fragment ‘I can’t even’ is the latest in a long line of phrases deployed by millennials to obscure from adults what they really mean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little paradox of Internet celebrity is that a YouTube personality can amass millions upon millions of young fans by making it seem as if he’s chatting with each of them one to one. Tyler Oakley, a 26-year-old man who identifies as a “professional fangirl,” is a master of the genre. He has nerd glasses, pinchable cheeks, a quiff he dyes in shades of blue and green and more YouTube subscribers than Shakira. Some of his teenage admirers have told him that he is the very first gay person that they have ever seen. He models slumber party outfits and gushes over boy bands, giving the kids who watch him from their bedrooms a peek into a wider world.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14first_words/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When You ‘Literally Can’t Even’ Understand Your Teenager', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kic