s and much, much more.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/the-architecture-of-psychotherapy/', 'snippet': 'Waiting rooms, consulting offices and much, much more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you listen to psychotherapists when they talk to one another, you will often hear them speak of something called the “therapeutic frame.” This term, coined by the psychoanalyst Marion Milner, refers to the set of conventions and ground rules that structure the therapeutic experience. Just as the frame of a painting defines the borders of a work of art, the therapeutic frame is the “container” in which the therapy takes place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Architecture of Psychotherapy', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T11:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Esther Sperber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Esther', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sperber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3f0e61e-e73a-5d45-8483-5fde0d129618', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3f0e61e-e73a-5d45-8483-5fde0d129618'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Laura Poitras documents the dissidents Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum as they collaborate on an art project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/opinion/the-art-of-dissent.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Laura Poitras documents the dissidents Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum as they collaborate on an art project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum are artists, journalists, dissidents, polymaths — and targets. Their respective governments, China and the United States, monitor their every move. They have been detained and interrogated. Ai cannot leave China, and Appelbaum is advised not to return to the United States. They are separated from their families. Ai has been imprisoned and beaten by the police. Yet each continues his work and speaks out against government wrongdoing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Art of Dissent’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Jacob (1983- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T11:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Poitras', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poitras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a3b3a6-7827-5c61-9617-cd294a7a215c', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a3b3a6-7827-5c61-9617-cd294a7a215c'}, {'abstract': 'Laura Poitras documents the dissidents Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum as they collaborate on an art project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000003729935/the-art-of-dissent.html', 'snippet': 'Laura Poitras documents the dissidents Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum as they collaborate on an art project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laura Poitras documents the dissidents Ai Weiwei and Jacob Appelbaum as they collaborate on an art project.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/multimedia/opdoc-panda/opdoc-panda-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/08/multimedia/o