rstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poitras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/46493280-a630-504d-89e9-042eec551014', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/46493280-a630-504d-89e9-042eec551014'}, {'abstract': 'HSBC Plans 50,000 Job Cuts in Global Overhaul | Regulator Said to Have Urged Deutsche Bank Chiefs’ Exit | What Mergers Say About U.S. Economy | Calpers Aims to Reduce Money Manager Fees', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/morning-agenda-hsbc-plans-50000-job-cuts-in-global-overhaul/', 'snippet': 'HSBC Plans 50,000 Job Cuts in Global Overhaul | Regulator Said to Have Urged Deutsche Bank Chiefs’ Exit | What Mergers Say About U.S. Economy | Calpers Aims to Reduce Money Manager Fees', 'lead_paragraph': 'HSBC PLANS 50,000 JOB CUTS IN GLOBAL RESTRUCTURING | HSBC said Tuesday that it would cut as many as 50,000 jobs around the world and try to reduce costs by as much as $5 billion a year by 2017 as it laid out its plans to restructure its global businesses,  Chad Bray reports in DealBook. About 25,000 jobs will be lost through the sale of the bank’s businesses in Turkey and Brazil, and an additional 20,000 to 25,000 jobs will be eliminated as part of the restructuring. However, the bank is increasingly focusing on Asia, saying that it would expand its asset management and insurance operations in hopes of capturing “expected opportunities from emerging wealth in the region.” The bank also plans to increase its business in the Pearl River Delta in the southern Chinese province of Guangdong and in parts of Southeast Asia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: HSBC Plans 50,000 Job Cuts in Global Overhaul', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointme