t analysis just published in Washington of America’s foreign trade in April, cables the New York correspondent of the ‘‘Daily Telegraph,’’ shows that the exports to the United Kingdom in that month were valued $94,000,000. Not a cent’s worth went to Germany. In April last year, however, the exports to that country were valued at $18,000,000. This is the first time that the Government has reported that for the whole month no goods, no copper, no resin, no cotton — nothing whatever — went to Germany from the United States. — The New York Herald, European Edition, June 10, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: No U.S. Goods Sent to Germany', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T13:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e4f0693-2d86-510c-9f5a-dcf7b3a3c0f8', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e4f0693-2d86-510c-9f5a-dcf7b3a3c0f8'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of objects photographed by David Guttenfelder', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/06/10/world/asia/20150610-NKOREA-OBJECTS.html', 'snippet': 'A collection of objects photographed by David Guttenfelder', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of objects photographed by David Guttenfelder', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/wor