'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T17:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef7211b3-172f-5ada-9cfc-fe7115805e51', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef7211b3-172f-5ada-9cfc-fe7115805e51'}, {'abstract': 'A prediction market has rated the chances that potential candidates will actually run for president, and Mr. Trump’s odds are the biggest surprise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/upshot/if-youre-a-betting-man-its-time-to-start-believing-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'A prediction market has rated the chances that potential candidates will actually run for president, and Mr. Trump’s odds are the biggest surprise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politicians lie, but bettors have a habit of ferreting out the truth. And this is why my article this morning noted that it would be harder for politicians to evade the fund-raising limits that apply to candidates if we relied on prediction markets rather than lawyers to assess whether a politician was running for office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/upshot/10UP-Predict/10UP-Predict-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If You’re a Betting Man, It’s Time to Start Believing Donald Trump', 'kicker': 'Road to 2016', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T17:57:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5624a54b-463b-5466-9572-a20613b0c50f', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5624a54b-463b-5466-9572-a20613b0c50f'}, {'abstract': 'The pioneering video artist has amassed a trove of occult ephemera in his Manhattan home and studio.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/tony-oursler-archives/', 'snippet': 'The pioneering video artist has amassed a trove of occult ephemera in his Manhattan home and studio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past 20 years, the pioneering video artist has amassed a trove of occult ephemera in his Manhattan home and studio: a deck of extrasensory perception cards, spirit photos (among them, a portrait of the former first lady Mary Todd Lincoln and her late husband’s alleged ghost), a gun-shaped film projector from a ’40s magic act and tons of ectoplasmic goop. Next month, the artist will release a 600-page book that brings his entire collection together in one place, and he will debut an immersive 3D film with actors playing Arthur Conan Doyle, Harry Houdini and the mystic Margery Crandon. He cryptically calls the video project, which will screen throughout the international photography festival Les Rencontres d’Arles, his “return to narrative.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-oursler/14beauty-look-oursler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-oursler/14beauty-look-oursler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-oursler/14beauty-look-oursler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam