g up takes a weird and wondrous turn in the latest book from the photographer and T contributor Henry Bourne. “Arcadia Britannica: A Modern British Folklore Portrait” ($30, out June 16 from Thames & Hudson) was shot in the style of Irving Penn’s “Small Trades,” capturing a sample of some of the 700 folklore traditions played out across the country every year. The origin of these strange and spectacular events, with characters that include Straw Bears and Horn Dancers and Pearly Queens, is often blurry. Yet when captured\xa0by Bourne’s lens, one thing is abundantly clear: Much like fancy dress at Halloween, modern folk is fun. Why else would a Scottish graphic designer choose to cover himself in over 10,000 thistles in the bizarre tradition of the Burry Man?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Modern Face of British Folklore is Sure to Make You Smile (Maybe Giggle)', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bookshelf: Modern Folklore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T19:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06313b61-4777-51d5-8abf-a3a61d4f83ba', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06313b61-4777-51d5-8abf-a3a61d4f83ba'}, {'abstract': 'The Andrew Lloyd Webber adaptation of “School of Rock” is to begin previews at the Winter Garden Theater on Nov. 9.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/09/school-of-rock-plans-fall-opening-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'The Andrew Lloyd Webber adaptation of “School of Rock” is to begin previews at the Winter Garden Theater on Nov. 9.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May we have the attention of the class, please: “School of Rock” will indeed be in session on Broadway this fall. The Andrew Lloyd Webber musical adaptation of the 2003 Jack Black comedy has now solidified its Broadway plans, and is to begin previews at the Winter Garden Theater on Nov. 9 with its opening night scheduled for Dec. 6, its press representatives said Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘School of Rock’ Plans Fall Opening on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘School of Rock’ Sets Fall Broadway Dates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brightman, Alex (Actor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connor, Laurence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fellowes, Julian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd Webber, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slater, Glenn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T19:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3119b66-bffb-5818-a31a-de22b9b17694', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3119b66-bffb-5818-a31a-de22b9b17694'}, {'abstract': 'The reassessment has spurred mixed responses from attendees of the conf