ed in 1845, dozens of inmates have escaped over, under or through the prison’s thick walls, their exploits detailed in newspaper reports of earlier eras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/nyregion/escape-from-clinton-prison-was-neither-the-first-nor-the-boldest.html', 'snippet': 'Since the Dannemora, N.Y., prison opened in 1845, dozens of inmates have escaped over, under or through the prison’s thick walls, their exploits detailed in newspaper reports of earlier eras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In summer 1903, a former bank burglar serving a life sentence removed the last bit of earth from a tunnel that had taken him four years to complete and escaped with three other inmates under the walls of Clinton prison in far northern New York State. Almost three decades later, it was a diminutive prisoner that some newspapers called the “midget bandit” who fled the prison in a similar way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1077, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/nyregion/ESCAPES/ESCAPES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunnels, Disguises and Sewers: Clinton Prison’s Inmates Have Found Many Ways to Flee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunnels, Disguises and Sewers: A Prison&#8217;s Inmates Have Found Many Ways to Flee ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winerip, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clinton Correctional Facility', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dannemora (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-09T21:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz and Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cac461e-424c-5526-85a8-51c5872f6172', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cac461e-424c-5526-85a8-51c5872f6172'}, {'abstract': 'This play at the Two River Theater, adapted from a novel by Ned Vizzini, centers on a teenager who turns cool after ingesting a tiny computer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/theater/review-in-be-more-chill-a-nerd-finds-popularity-in-a-sci-fi-pill.html', 'snippet': 'This play at the Two River Theater, adapted from a novel by Ned Vizzini, centers on a teenager who turns cool after ingesting a tiny computer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RED BANK, N.J. — Teenage angst: the grief that just keeps on giving, to popular culture, at least. The woes of the misfit and the wallflower, the snooty brutishness of the jocks and the mean girls have been a bottomless well of material for television, movies and books for decades, and the well shows no signs of running dry. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1081, 'width': 1456, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/arts/10MORECHILL/10MORECHILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':