n-based discrimination the same way it treats discrimination based on race, religion, color, sex, age and national origin,” Mr. Carter said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Anti-Bias Policy Extended to Gays', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Anti-Bias Policy Is Extended to Gays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T02:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/db42c855-893c-5918-aa38-112408c98222', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db42c855-893c-5918-aa38-112408c98222'}, {'abstract': 'Three jury members were dismissed Tuesday from the murder trial of the gunman who opened fire inside an Aurora, Colo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/us/colorado-3-are-removed-from-theater-murder-jury.html', 'snippet': 'Three jury members were dismissed Tuesday from the murder trial of the gunman who opened fire inside an Aurora, Colo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three jury members were dismissed Tuesday from the murder trial of the gunman who opened fire inside an Aurora, Colo., movie theater because of concerns they had been “tainted” by hearing or discussing news reports about the case during breaks from the trial. One dismissed juror said in court that her husband had called her to ask about reports of an errant Twitter message the district attorney in the case sent last week. Judge Carlos A. Samour Jr. had reprimanded the district attorney, George Brauchler, for his message outside the presence of the jury. The judge has warned jurors dozens of times not to discuss the death-penalty case or read about it, and to tell him if they accidentally hear any of its details outside the courtroom. Twelve jurors and nine alternates remain on the panel. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado: 3 Are Removed From Theater Murder Jury ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colorado: 3 Are Removed From Theater Murder Jury ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, James Eagan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T02:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f03c51-388c-5d65-a474-a5fe8b898b03', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f03c51-388c-5d65-a474-a5fe8b898b03'}, {'abstract': 'Washington selected Mariano Rivera III, a right-handed pitcher, in the fourth round of the major league baseball draft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/sports/baseball/eliciting-memories-nationals-draft-mariano-riveras-son.html', 'snippet': 'Washington selected Mariano Rivera III, a right-handed pitcher, in the fourth round of the major league baseball draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Game 5 of the 2001 World Series, Matt Williams was asked to bunt against Mariano Rivera, one of baseball’s indomitable closers. In a few years, Williams could be managing Rivera’s son. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/sports/10rivera-web/10rivera-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thu