emanded money to give their sons a chance of playing when he was in charge of the Slavia Prague club. Ruzicka has denied any wrongdoing. (AP)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Czech Republic Coach Resigns', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bettman to Be Deposed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T03:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/aedc9917-799c-536c-9cb2-e2f017f01bcd', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aedc9917-799c-536c-9cb2-e2f017f01bcd'}, {'abstract': "Credo, the brainchild of a member of the executive team that first brought Sephora to the U.S., doesn't want you to sacrifice style for substance.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/t-magazine/san-francisco-credo-beauty-skin-care.html', 'snippet': "Credo, the brainchild of a member of the executive team that first brought Sephora to the U.S., doesn't want you to sacrifice style for substance.", 'lead_paragraph': 'In certain hip neighborhoods of certain hip cities, an eco-beauty boutique is nearly as likely a sight as a single-origin coffee bar. But although green has gone mainstream, until now, many sustainability-oriented apothecaries have been more focused on niche items than necessities. That, however, is set to change with the arrival of Credo, a new natural and organic emporium whose first location has just opened on San Francisco’s Fillmore Street. The brainchild of Shashi Batra, a member of the executive team that first brought Sephora to the U.S., Credo offers an experience similar to that of the LVMH-owned superstore, minus the synthetic ingredients. “You may want your tomatoes farm-to-table, but I don’t think you should get your eye shadow or mascara farm-to-table,” Batra explains. “It should be in a place where you can test it and feel good about it. It shouldn’t be in bottles that look like dog shampoo. It shouldn’t smell like tree sap. It has to deliver on all those levels.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 1480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/t-magazine/10credo-hartman/10credo-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco’s New All-Natural Boutique Isn’t for Hippies', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/217322c9-9fdc-5035-8a1c-70ddb4a5995b', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/217322c9-9fdc-5035-8a1c-70ddb4a5995b'}, {'abstract': 'The contemporary artist debuted a new program of text projections to coincide with the exhibition “Art, Garden, Life.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/t-magazine/at-the-new-york-botanical-garden-jenny-holzer-channels-frida-kahlo.html', 'snippet': 'The contemporary artist debuted a new program of text projections to coincide with the exhibition “Art, Garden, Life.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m getting a free drink for using other people’s writing!” marveled the artist Jenny Holzer earlier this week, ahead of a dinner last night at the New York Botanical Garden. The occasion served a double purpose for the artist, who was honored by the Poetry Society of America and also premiered a new program of text projections, which will continue to scroll over the glass walls of the garden’s exhibition hall starting at dusk each day through Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the New York Botanical Garden, Jenny Holzer Channels Frida Kahlo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c2c496d-6284-5e27-9155-6c27a62e4d90', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c2c496d-6284-5e27-9155-6c27a62e4d90'}, {'abstract': 'Because every woman should own a simple maillot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/t-magazine/best-black-swimsuits.html', 'snippet': 'Because every woman should own a simple maillot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because every woman should own a simple maillot.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black Swimsuits', 'kicker': 'Market Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black Swimsuits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4d66e4-6523-5301-9237-0e1bfd661507', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4d66e4-6523-5301-9237-0e1bfd661507'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 10 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/word-of-the-day-apostate/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 10 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'apostate • \\ə-ˈpäs-ˌtat, -tət\\ • adjective and noun ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | apostate', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T04:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a55c90fe-d22a-559b-89c1-ad15117bd93c', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a55c90fe-d22a-559b-89c1-ad15117bd93c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 A.M. (IFC) INTOLERABLE CRUELTY (2003) George Clooney plays Miles Massey, the crème de la crème of divorce lawyers, in this Joel and Ethan Coen film. Catherine Zeta-Jones, above with Mr. Clooney, is Marylin, a silken beauty and Miles’s latest client, who becomes mired in a vicious divorce after she catches her husband (Edward Herrmann) cheating yet again. Billy Bob Thornton is her millionaire beau and Miles’s rival for her money-hungry affections. “The Coens, bless their hearts, are too smart to apologize for avarice — it’s what gave screwball comedies a kick, and sends this movie straight to your head,” Elvis Mitchell wrote in The New York Times. “Keep in mind that it’s only a minor rush, but a rush nonetheless. It has a Jell-O-shot smoothness that makes you a little dizzy afterward in recollecting how assured and unremittingly smart ‘Intolerable Cruelty’ is.” In “Fantastic Mr. Fox” (2009), at 1:15 p.m., Mr. Clooney, Meryl Streep, Jason Schwartzman and Bill Murray lend their voices to this animated tale from Wes Anderson, adapted with Noah Baumbach from the Roald Dahl “anti-fable” about a fox who rallies his animal friends against three evil farmers. “It is precisely the movie that a child smitten with Roald Dahl’s fiction and fascinated by the enigmas of the adult world would dream of making: something to amaze and terrify the grown-ups and win the envy and adulation of his peers,” A. O. Scott wrote in The Times.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T04:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ace636d8-7c46-5991-bb0f-455a376ef738', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ace636d8-7c46-5991-bb0f-455a376ef738'}, {'abstract': 'Poems by Mr. Herrera, the newly named poet laureate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/books/selected-poems-by-juan-felipe-herrera.html', 'snippet': 'Poems by Mr. Herrera, the newly named poet laureate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poems by Juan Felipe Herrera, the newly named poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selected Poems by Juan Felipe Herrera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrera, Juan Felipe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poets Laureate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'v