html', 'snippet': 'The Obama Administration is shifting its stance on drug pricing in the Trans-Pacific Partnership talks, according to a newly leaked “transparency” annex of the proposed trade accord.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama Administration is shifting its stance on drug pricing in the Trans-Pacific Partnership talks, according to a newly leaked “transparency” annex of the proposed trade accord.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-jumbo.png', 'height': 671, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-superJumbo.png', 'height': 671, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/business/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord/document-annex-of-proposed-pacific-trade-accord-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Annex of Proposed Pacific Trade Accord', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T11:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/d2cb616d-cfc0-5a11-b9d6-a8e2188640c7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d2cb616d-cfc0-5a11-b9d6-a8e2188640c7'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicists consider if and when to share someone else’s medical news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/magazine/do-i-have-to-keep-a-secret-about-a-family-members-health.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicists consider if and when to share someone else’s medical news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My uncle’s daughter texted this message to me a few days ago: “You didn’t hear this from me, and pretend this conversation didn’t take place. My dad went to the hospital this morning in an ambulance with a heart attack. My mom told me not to tell anyone, saying this is Dad’s news to tell, but I thought you would want to know. Whatever you do, please don’t tell your mom.” My uncle and I are very close, so I understand why his daughter would think I would want to know. Telling me this news when she was asked not to is her own ethical problem to resolve. However, knowing this information puts me in a very awkward position. Should I tell my 82-year-old mother about her 70-year-old brother’s health crisis? She would surely want to know this tidbit of info. Or do I honor my uncle’s family’s wishes not to tell my mother? How do we react when we’re officially told the news of the heart attack? If we pretend not to know anything happened, we’re lying, and that in itself is unethical. Or do we reply that we were told? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 589}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1952, 'width': 1987, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14ethicists/14mag-14ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do I Have to Keep a Secret About a Family Member’s Health?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Do I Have to Keep a Secret About a Family Member’s Health?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T11:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah, Amy Bloom and Kenji Yoshino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kenji', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yoshino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c161f56b-13f7-5f96-822b-f0eaea9ddebe', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c161f56b-13f7-5f96-822b-f0eaea9ddebe'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese officials and an American research center have announced a plan to undertake trial national park projects in nine provinces over the next three years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/world/asia/china-envisions-network-of-national-parks-with-us-as-a-model.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese officials and an American research center have announced a plan to undertake trial national park projects in nine provinces over the next three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — More than 140 years ago, the United States government designated Yellowstone as the nation’s first national park — an untouched Western landscape of geysers, grizzly bears and soaring peaks. The national parks program eventually expanded to include more than 450 sites and has become one of the country’s greatest tourist draws.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/world/11China/11China-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/11/world/11China/11China-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/world/11China/11China-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/world/11China/11China-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,