three dozen hostels — important additions to the town’s once-inadequate accommodation scene. For those who fell in love with Zagreb, population 790,000, before its surge in popularity, fear not. Though the town has rejiggered its offerings with jazzy lounges, bistros and chic clothes-designer ateliers, this Slavic metropolis along the Sava River still retains plenty of cobbled-street charm.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Zagreb, Croatia', 'kicker': 'Weekend Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours in Zagreb, Croatia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crevar, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zagreb (Croatia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Croatia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T19:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Crevar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crevar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e08cb58-3704-5b1f-abeb-67c057b54e71', 'word_count': 1671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e08cb58-3704-5b1f-abeb-67c057b54e71'}, {'abstract': 'James Hadley Billington will step down from his post on Jan. 1 after nearly three decades leading the world’s largest library.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/06/10/us/document-billingtons-letter-to-president-obama.html', 'snippet': 'James Hadley Billington will step down from his post on Jan. 1 after nearly three decades leading the world’s largest library.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Hadley Billington will step down from his post on Jan. 1 after nearly