': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bed2465-2197-5bb1-b6c8-e9f346c71adb', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bed2465-2197-5bb1-b6c8-e9f346c71adb'}, {'abstract': 'The English writer is facing death the only way she knows how: line by line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/magazine/jenny-diskis-end-notes.html', 'snippet': 'The English writer is facing death the only way she knows how: line by line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last July, when the English writer Jenny Diski was told she had inoperable lung cancer and, at best, another three years to live, she responded to the news characteristically — that is, in wry poor taste. “So,” she said, turning to her husband, the poet and academic Ian Patterson, “we’d better get cooking the meth.” The Poet — as Diski always refers to Patterson, with tender-ironic reserve, in her personal essays — was just about able to keep up his end of the morbid repartee that is the currency of their marriage: “This time we quit while the going’s good.” The oncologist and the nurse, apparently not watchers of “Breaking Bad,” looked on blankly.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14diski_horizontal-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14diski_horizontal-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14diski_horizontal-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14diski_horizontal-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14mag-14diski-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14mag-14diski-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14diski_horizontal/14mag-14diski-t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jenny Diski’s End Notes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End Notes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvey, Giles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lung Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diski, Jenny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-10T20:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giles Harvey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harvey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1940e830-eaaf-50c6-a606-cbdf8ccc5c43', 'word_count': 5107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1940e830-eaaf-50c6-a606-cbdf8ccc5c43'}, {'abstract': 'Turning back the clock can be as simple as sipping a drink.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/beauty-drinks/', 'snippet': 'Turning back the clock can be as simple as sipping a drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are all sorts of magical creams and serums that promise tighter skin and fewer lines, but a new fad in cosmetics suggests that turning back the clock can be as simple as sipping a drink. The Beauty Chef’s Collagen Inner Beauty Boost mixes the wrinkle smoother with superfoods such as goji berries and acai berries. Beauty & Go’s grape-flavored Radiance drink is meant to improve elasticity with hyaluronic acid. For the follically challenged, there’s Fountain’s Hair Molecule, a silicon and biotin liquid that can be taken alone or mixed with a morning smoothie to produce extra strength and shine. The most too-good-to-be-true of the bunch comes in a six-pack: Precious, a collagen-infused beer from the Japanese brewery Suntory, is aimed at women who desire a healthy — and perhaps tipsy — glow.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-drinks/14beauty-look-drinks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-drinks/14beauty-look-drinks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-drinks/14beauty-look-drinks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14beauty-look-drinks/14beauty-look-drinks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':