to American life and literary traditions informed and improved his work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/books/review-nabokov-in-america-and-reaping-inspiration-from-amber-waves.html', 'snippet': 'A writer argues that Vladimir Nabokov’s dive into American life and literary traditions informed and improved his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His private tragedy, Vladimir Nabokov once declared, was that “I had to abandon my natural idiom, my untrammeled, rich, and infinitely docile Russian tongue for a second-rate brand of English, devoid of any of those apparatuses — the baffling mirror, the black velvet backdrop, the implied associations and traditions — which the native illusionist, frac-tails flying, can magically use to transcend the heritage his own way.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/arts/11BOOKROPER/11BOOKROPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/11/arts/11BOOKROPER/11BOOKROPER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 967}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/arts/11BOOKROPER/11BOOKROPER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 636, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/arts/11BOOKROPER/11BOOKROPER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1271, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/arts/11BOOKROPER/11BOOKROPER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'i