, water, waste and air management systems and the electric grid online.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/10/traffic-hacking-caution-light-is-on/', 'snippet': 'The threat is increasing that hackers could shut down so-called smart cities, where network sensors connect traffic, water, waste and air management systems and the electric grid online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, Cesar Cerrudo flew to Washington, strolled over to Capitol Hill and pulled out his laptop. Then he began to hack the city’s traffic system.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 841}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/10/technology/10ROADHACK/10ROADHACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015