'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T01:35:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2735689f-6cd7-5756-af21-cc22275b681b', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2735689f-6cd7-5756-af21-cc22275b681b'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department froze any assets the Lebanese might have under United States jurisdiction and prohibited Americans from doing business with them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/world/middleeast/lebanon-us-puts-3-lebanese-on-blacklist-over-hezbollah-links.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department froze any assets the Lebanese might have under United States jurisdiction and prohibited Americans from doing business with them.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Three Lebanese men and their businesses were blacklisted by American sanctions officials on Wednesday for what they described as extensive ties with Hezbollah, the Shiite political organization in Lebanon that the United States and Israel regard as a terrorist group. The Treasury Department said the actions against the Lebanese froze any assets they might have under United States jurisdiction and prohibited Americans from doing business with them. Its statement said the actions “underscore the direct ties between Hezbollah’s commercial and terrorist activities, as well as the group’s continued exploitation of the legitimate commercial sector for financial, organizational and material support.” The targets of the actions were identified as Adham Tabaja and his company, Al-Inmaa Group for Tourism Works, and its subsidiaries; Kassem Hejeij, a businessman who arranged financial services access for Hezbollah; and Husayn Ali Faour and his company, Care Care Center, which was accused of arranging transportation for Hezbollah, which is politically aligned with the governments of Syria and Iran. Mr. Faour was identified as a member of Islamic Jihad, a Hezbollah branch. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lebanon: U.S. Puts 3 Lebanese on Blacklist Over Hezbollah Links', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Lebanon: U.S. Puts 3 Lebanese on Blacklist Over Hezbollah Links', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assets, Frozen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faour, Husayn Ali', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tabaja, Adham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hejeij, Kassem', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Care Care Center', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al-Inmaa Group for Tourism Works LLC', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T01:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': 