: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/opinion/the-myth-of-a-white-minority.html', 'snippet': 'We use outdated, illogical racial and ethnic categories. Social reality is much more complex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 2012, the Census Bureau announced that nonwhite births exceeded white births for the first time. In 2013, it noted that more whites were dying than were being born. In March, it projected that non-Hispanic whites would be a minority by 2044.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Myth of a White Minority', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Myth of a White Minority', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alba, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Alba', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alba', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/144d4e9e-7f32-517c-81cd-ebd92faffc16', 'wo