, '_id': 'nyt://article/b67ddadd-31d7-5a34-9da5-3670e49b4ca9', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b67ddadd-31d7-5a34-9da5-3670e49b4ca9'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “Reading Lolita in Tehran” on writing under the eye of a watchful government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/books/review/surveillance-states.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “Reading Lolita in Tehran” on writing under the eye of a watchful government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while, every time I borrowed a book from my local library in Washington, D.C., I was greeted by an Orwellian poster: “Big Brother Is Watching You!” I often wondered if others paused to reflect on the implication of these words, if they understood how profoundly living under surveillance distorts a society. It transforms your perspective, your manners, your relationships with friends, colleagues, students, with every waiter and cabdriver you meet. It changes your relationship with yourself.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14AUTHORSNOTE/14-Authorsnote-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 528, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14AUTHORSNOTE/14-Authorsnote-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 528, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14AUTHORSNOTE/14AUTHORSNOTE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14AUTHORSNOTE/14AUTHORSNOTE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub