 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T11:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ccdecec-0274-5333-af4c-1c276f259f78', 'word_count': 2238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ccdecec-0274-5333-af4c-1c276f259f78'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court’s coming decision on health care is not the only court ruling on the law watchers have their eyes on. But most of Thursday’s action and focus will be on Utah, where Republicans will meet Mitt Romney’s list of donors and spend time in the sun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/06/11/today-in-politics-mitt-romney-conference-promises-donors-and-early-morning-hikes/', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court’s coming decision on health care is not the only court ruling on the law watchers have their eyes on. But most of Thursday’s action and focus will be on Utah, where Republicans will meet Mitt Romney’s list of donors and spend tim...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Thursday morning from Washington, where the Supreme Court’s coming decision on health care is not the only court ruling on the law watchers have their eyes on. But most of Thursday’s action and focus will be on Utah, where Republicans will meet Mitt Romney‘s list of donors and spend time in the sun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Politics: Mitt Romney Conference Promises Donors and Early Morning Hikes', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65aa9985-db03-50f0-9e24-3e7aa89978e5', 'word_count': 1454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65aa9985-db03-50f0-9e24-3e7aa89978e5'}, {'abstract': 'For one gardener, a lifetime of instant gratification yields to longer-term commitment.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/my-perennial-dilemma/', 'snippet': 'For one gardener, a lifetime of instant gratification yields to longer-term commitment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank goodness for farmers. As a mere gardener, I don’t know how they do it. The heartbreak. My phlox had powdery mildew last summer and it about killed me. The worry. Was I applying the right mildew spray? The doubt. Had I read the Department of Agriculture’s official Plant Hardiness Zone Map correctly? Was Provincetown in Zone 7A? I had to remind myself that my life and livelihood did not depend on my phlox crop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/opinion/0611PRIVATELIVES/0611PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/11/opinion/0611PRIVATELIVES/0611PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/opinion/0611PRIVATELIVES/0611PRIVATELIVES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/opinion/0611PRIVATELIVES/0611PRIVATELIVES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption