h of Christopher Lee', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gad, Josh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaiman, Neil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Christopher (1922-2015)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Elijah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T16:51:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ad99e16-3ee3-5634-b79e-0010d5547dff', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ad99e16-3ee3-5634-b79e-0010d5547dff'}, {'abstract': 'Budding lingerie brands create pieces meant to move with, not restrict, women’s bodies.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/minimal-underwear-maximum-coverage-comfort/', 'snippet': 'Budding lingerie brands create pieces meant to move with, not restrict, women’s bodies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The movement away from tight, constricting undergarments continues as budding lingerie brands create pieces meant to move with, not restrict, women’s bodies. Produced for the VPL (visible panty line) uninhibited, the designs cede to comfort, using super-soft, breathable fabrics and high-waisted, full-bottomed, generally wire-free (and all around, very minimal) elements. Created for “the sport of womanhood,” Land of Women’s functional and classic cuts — think supple, everyday sports bras and ample bottomed briefs — support any feminine endeavor. Negative combines subtle seduction (perforated lace) and playfulness (albatross feather prints) for their uncomplicated and considered pieces. And Base Range uses unexpected details, like a small triangular opening at the sternum, and organic fabrics for sustainable support.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/11/t-magazine/11lingerie-cheung/11lingerie-cheung-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Minimal Undies With Maximum Coverage and Comfort for the Win', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker'