t)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T17:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1274579f-2dab-51e4-9e47-d1a3c89d2e24', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1274579f-2dab-51e4-9e47-d1a3c89d2e24'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant in Sunnyside, Queens, started out as a bakery and has broadened its menu and ambition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/dining/hungry-city-i-love-paraguay-restaurant-in-sunnyside-queens.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant in Sunnyside, Queens, started out as a bakery and has broadened its menu and ambition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bread is coarse, flat and round, a moon at its peak, looking ready to crumble. A mix of cassava starch, milk, eggs and Muenster, given the barest amount of cohesion on a griddle, it suggests a further step in the evolution of a quesadilla, with the cheese not pent up but pervading every cranny, crazing the surface so that each bite is crispy and chewy at once.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Love Paraguay, an Ode to a Homeland', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Love Letter to Paraguay From Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sunnyside (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'I Love Paraguay (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T17:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/77757bc8-7f8f-50ef-a389-32dacea43f95', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77757bc8-7f8f-50ef-a389-32dacea43f95'}, {'abstract': 'More on the loose grip of the invisible hand.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/the-mutability-of-wages/', 'snippet': 'More on the loose grip of the invisible hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arindrajit Dube enlarges on my post about efficiency wages, pointing out that the same logic applies to firms that have monopsony power. That’s a very good point — and I think we’re circling in on an important part of the logic behind the “new view” on inequality policy, which says that policies to enhance worker bargaining power can have major effects on the distribution of market income.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mutability of Wages', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T17:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03db7bf8-ef44-50f1-b9ee-eb83b1f64152', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03db7bf8-ef44-50f1-b9ee-eb83b1f64152'}, {'abstract': 'More on the loose grip of the invisible hand.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/the-mutability-of-wages/', 'snippet': 'More on the loose grip of the invisible hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arindrajit Dube enlarges on my post about efficiency wages, pointing out that the same logic applies to firms that have monopsony power. That’s a very good point — and I think we’re circling in on an important part of the logic behind the “new view” on inequality policy, which says that policies to enhance worker bargaining power can have major effects on the distribution of market income.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mutability of Wages', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-11T17:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL KRUGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRUGMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5746c1c1-2044-57bd-b40f-ec4933ca97de', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5746c1c1-2044-57bd-b40f-ec4933ca97de'}, {'abstract': 'The annual Congressional Baseball contest will be played tonight, and we’re here to answer the question: Can anybody here play this game?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/upshot/the-babe-ruth-of-congress.html', 'snippet': 'The annual Congressional Baseball contest will be played tonight, and we’re here to answer the question: Can anybody here play this game?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cedric Richmond, a House Democrat who represents New Orleans, is the Babe Ruth of the Congressional Baseball Game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/upshot/12UP-Congressional/12UP-Congressional-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/12/upshot/12UP-Congressional/12UP-Congressional-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, 