s more so than the lawmakers themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/nyregion/dog-related-bills-flood-albany-as-major-legislation-stalls.html', 'snippet': 'The canine subjects of dozens of measures awaiting passage are perennially popular with constituents, perhaps more so than the lawmakers themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — They bark at their lobbyists, never talk to lawmakers, and periodically lose control of themselves in the halls of the State Capitol. And yet, for all of that, there is one constituency whose interests are exceptionally well represented in Albany this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/nyregion/12DOGS2/12DOGS2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dog-Related Bills Flood Albany as Major Legislation Stalls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dog-Related Measures Flood Legislature in Final Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T00:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/624f14df-2afd-5473-841e-efd7b6ec30aa', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/624f14df-2afd-5473-841e-efd7b6ec30aa'}, {'abstract': 'This costume-drama adaptation of Flaubert’s “Madame Bovary” stays true to the plot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/movies/review-madame-bovary-features-mia-wasikowska-as-a-notorious-adulteress.html', 'snippet': 'This costume-drama adaptation of Flaubert’s “Madame Bovary” stays true to the plot.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Madame Bovary, c’est moi,” Gustave Flaubert said of his most famous fictional creation. Impulsive, vain and sometimes cruel, she is hardly the most sympathetic character in 19th-century literature, but she is among the most vivid and complicated. Flaubert illuminated her inner life and outward circumstances with a clarity that set a new standard for the novel, one that continues to beguile, and often to frustrate, his followers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1520, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/12MADAME1/12MADAME1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Madame Bovary’ Features Mia Wasikowska as a Notorious Adulteress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Faithful Rendition of Serial Adultery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barthes, Sophie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasikowska, Mia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Ezra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Madame Bovary (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T00:35:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4ff3633-294d-5f7c-8dac-3e25600e4e1e', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4ff3633-294d-5f7c-8dac-3e25600e4e1e'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio of New York raised the possibilities of lower wages and costlier medicines if the trade agreement with nearly a dozen Asian nations is approved by Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/nyregion/de-blasio-calls-trans-pacific-partnership-a-huge-mistake.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio of New York raised the possibilities of lower wages and costlier medicines if the trade agreement with nearly a dozen Asian nations is approved by Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviving a public split with the White House, Mayor Bill de Blasio declared on the eve of a key vote in Washington that it would be a “huge mistake” for Congress to approve President Obama’s chief legislative priority, a sweeping trade deal known as the Trans-Pacific Partnership.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio Calls Trans-Pacific Partnership a ‘Huge Mistake’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio Urges Vote Against Obama’s Trade Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Alexander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T00:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c2f9367-37d4-5bf4-9b9e-ce346aa666f8', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c2f9367-37d4-5bf4-9b9e-ce346aa666f8'}, {'abstract': 'A color-saturated Russian movie looks at Marc Chagall’s tumultuous time leading an art school in Vitebsk, where one of the teachers was Kazimir Malevich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/movies/review-in-chagall-malevich-two-painters-clash-in-revolutionary-russia.html', 'snippet': 'A color-saturated Russian movie looks at Marc Chagall’s tumultuous time leading an art school in Vitebsk, where one of the teachers was Kazimir Malevich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Set primarily in revolutionary-era Russia, Alexander Mitta’s “Chagall-Malevich” centers on the painter Marc Chagall and fictionalizes his real-life efforts to establish an artistic bulwark amid war and ideological ferment. It’s a literally colorful and playful attempt to portray battlefields of artistic ambition and political struggle. But its dialogue and characters are also written as subtly as a radical manifesto.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print