'2015-06-12T02:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0fabc4d-d31e-5a72-8ccd-4b2897f577b5', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0fabc4d-d31e-5a72-8ccd-4b2897f577b5'}, {'abstract': 'Friday fun with David Steinberg, and why you should try to solve themeless puzzles, if you haven’t already.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/11/emulate-an-esne/', 'snippet': 'Friday fun with David Steinberg, and why you should try to solve themeless puzzles, if you haven’t already.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY PUZZLE — Are you READY to roll with the crunchy fun of a themeless Friday puzzle? Or are you letting the white space and ramped-up clues frighten you away?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emulate an Esne', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T02:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a512d4d5-92d8-5536-8499-8b7cc6d74823', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a512d4d5-92d8-5536-8499-8b7cc6d74823'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the operation was run by two stepbrothers, who enlisted their girlfriends and shared the proceeds with their mother, and extended to other New York City boroughs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/nyregion/12-held-as-police-break-up-staten-island-heroin-ring.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said the operation was run by two stepbrothers, who enlisted their girlfriends and shared the proceeds with their mother, and extended to other New York City boroughs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York police this week broke up a sprawling family-run network of drug dealers, according to the acting district attorney for Staten Island, who said the ring was run by two stepbrothers whose operation helped fuel an explosion of heroin use in the borough. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12 Held as Police Break Up Staten Island Heroin Ring', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '12 Held as Police Break Up Staten Island Heroin Ring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stack, Liam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heroin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonilla, Justin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarado, Robert (1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T02:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73619b0d-bc2b-5d36-b211-5db17e6b0ebd', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73619b0d-bc2b-5d36-b211-5db17e6b0ebd'}, {'abstract': 'Much of the growth of federal higher-education spending has been increases in veterans’ education benefits and Pell grants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/us/federal-money-for-education-surpasses-states-contributions.html', 'snippet': 'Much of the growth of federal higher-education spending has been increases in veterans’ education benefits and Pell grants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reversing a pattern, federal funding for higher education has in recent years outstripped state funding. According to a new report from the Pew Charitable Trusts, the federal government supplied $75.6 billion in 2013, the latest year for which data is available, and state governments supplied $72.7 billion. From 2000 to 2012, federal per-student spending increased by 32 percent, while state spending dropped by 37 percent. Generally, the federal government provides financial help to individual students and specific research projects, while state funds go toward public institutions’ general operations. Much of the growth of federal higher-education spending has been increases in veterans’ education benefits and Pell grants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Money for Education Surpasses States’ Contributions', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Money for Higher Education Surpasses States’ Contributions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Charitable Trusts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T02:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar L