e Rohingya of Myanmar, a Hardscrabble Existence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T03:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/04d1dc98-71a6-5e5c-9ded-2f19edc58969', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/04d1dc98-71a6-5e5c-9ded-2f19edc58969'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Field, who started a research company in 1945, was an institutional memory of public opinion in an opinionated state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/us/politics/mervin-field-dies-at-94-took-political-pulse-of-california-as-pollster.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Field, who started a research company in 1945, was an institutional memory of public opinion in an opinionated state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Mervin Field was a college dropout. He had no formal training in polling or statistics. He bagged groceries while growing up in Princeton, N.J. He went to San Francisco after World War II with the unlikely goal of starting a one-man marketing research firm. Business was so slow that he worked nights pumping gas.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/us/12FIELD-obit/12FIELD-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/12/us/12FIELD-obit/12FIELD-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, '