//www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/t-magazine/whitney-museum-untitled-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'The chefs discuss their High Line-influenced ethos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Whitney Museum of American Art moved from the Upper East Side to the Meatpacking District this spring, it traded its proximity to the large green rectangle of Central Park for sweeping views of the High Line, where Piet Oudolf’s unruly garden landscape spills onto the former railroad trestle in the most organic of ways. In the above video, the chefs at the Whitney’s new restaurant, Untitled, discuss how the museum’s change in scenery inspires the dishes they serve and the atmosphere they have created within the new Renzo Piano-designed building. And below, they share a recipe off the Untitled menu for lobster toast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Whitney’s Untitled Restaurant, Downtown Plates Mirror the Change in Scenery', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/131327c7-d6a5-503b-a109-2f2a3fd78109', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/131327c7-d6a5-503b-a109-2f2a3fd78109'}, {'abstract': 'For one couple, realizing their dream house as a cultural salon in Cuba has been more than a labor of love. It’s been a lesson in patience, perseverance and wild invention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/t-magazine/cuba-house-pamela-ruiz-damian-aquiles.html', 'snippet': 'For one couple, realizing their dream house as a cultural salon in Cuba has been more than a labor of love. It’s been a lesson in patience, perseverance and wild invention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For one couple, realizing their dream house as a cultural salon in Cuba has been more than a labor of love. It’s been a lesson in patience, perseverance and wild invention.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '94', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grand Havana Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuba Libre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Havana (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Dolce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56329fe2-b7ca-5d90-9f5c-8960643be86a', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56329fe2-b7ca-5d90-9f5c-8960643be86a'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 85 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/word-of-the-day-fleece/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 85 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'fleece • \\ˈfles\\ • noun and verb ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | fleece', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T04:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 's