roslav Slaboshpytskiy, the movie tells its story of violence and love through visuals alone, withholding translations of the nonprofessional actors’ passionate signing.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 284}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1274, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14TRIBE1/14TRIBE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Tribe,’ Set at a Grim School for the Deaf, Forgoes Subtitles for Its Fierce Sign Language', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Into a Hushed and Brutal Universe ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapold, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slaboshpytskiy, Myroslav', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sign Language', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Tribe (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T08:29:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f6b11a3-2a25-5a27-8460-09eba2327ed1', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f6b11a3-2a25-5a27-8460-09eba2327ed1'}, {'abstract': 'Principals in the making of Martin Scorsese’s “Goodfellas” reminisce about the shoot on the film’s 25th anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/movies/goodfellas-25-years-on-cast-members-reminisce.html', 'snippet': 'Principals in the making of Martin Scorsese’s “Goodfellas” reminisce about the shoot on the film’s 25th anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been 25 years since Martin Scorsese’s seminal gangster film “Goodfellas” opened to the adulation of critics, among them Vincent Canby of The New York Times, who hailed it as “breathless and brilliant.” Though it’s now considered a classic, counted by the American Film Institute as one of the country’s 100 greatest films, its foul-mouthed tale of the rise and fall of the murderous Henry Hill; his wife, Karen; and his patron, Paulie, left early audiences cold. In a nod to the anniversary, Film Forum is screening a newly restored version of the movie starting next Friday.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times