r performers. Willie Nelson, Kris Kristofferson, Johnny Cash, Waylon Jennings and Elvis Presley have all recorded his work. In the 1970s, Shaver wrote a number of anthems in the rougher, less-polished-than-Nashville subgenre called outlaw country.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 1270, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14tip/14mag-14tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Write a Country Song', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Write a Country Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wollan, Malia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaver, Billy Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4819f896-2045-5020-9929-582a11710d70', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4819f896-2045-5020-9929-582a11710d70'}, {'abstract': 'Transported back to a former life as a prison inmate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/magazine/outside-looking-in.html', 'snippet': 'Transported back to a former life as a prison inmate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day last November, at a stoplight on Route 34 in Derby, Conn., I noticed a truck idling in front of me. It was stout and white, with the requisite grime, and by outward appearance it could have been carrying anything: Portuguese rolls, hanging file folders or maybe replacement gas caps. But when the bumper sticker (Am I driving safely?) referred me to a government website, I became certain the truck was hauling human beings.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14lives/14mag-14lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/magazine/14lives/14mag-14lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehei