 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b387737-08ee-5419-8d22-86c57180c33a', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b387737-08ee-5419-8d22-86c57180c33a'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Fifty-three paintings were sold for a total of almost 1.5 million francs in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/1890-high-prices-for-art-works/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Fifty-three paintings were sold for a total of almost 1.5 million francs in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One and a half million francs — in exact figures 1,589,000 fr. — were realized by the sale of the fifty-three paintings of the Crabbe collection, at the Sedelmeyer Gallery, yesterday. The auction room of the spacious establishment in the rue de La Rochefoucauld was packed to its fullest. Corot’s enchanting ‘‘Matin,’’ which was sold in 1880 at the Hotel Drouot for 7,000 fr., and for which Senator Crabbe paid, three years ago, 42,000 fr., brought 63,000 fr. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/blogs/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau-jumbo.png', 'height': 214, 'width': 345, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/blogs/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau-superJumbo.png', 'height': 214, 'width': 345, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/blogs/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau/13iht-oldjune13-rousseau-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20