', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14PLAYLIST2/14PLAYLIST2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14PLAYLIST2/14PLAYLIST2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14PLAYLIST2/14PLAYLIST2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Releases From Marta Sánchez, Cloud Rat, Pete Rodriguez and More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Patient Layers, Serene Strains and Fervid Screams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cloud Rat (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Marta (Pianist)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Pete (Trumpeter)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrams, Joshua (Composer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arocena, Dayme', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:09:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3511ca58-2203-528d-ac31-6b3f9647444b', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3511ca58-2203-528d-ac31-6b3f9647444b'}, {'abstract': 'The singer Brodie Jenkins has a versatile voice paired with Johnny Hwin’s sultry, tender music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/arts/music/cathedrals-rb-with-a-dash-of-1980s-rock-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'The singer Brodie Jenkins has a versatile voice paired with Johnny Hwin’s sultry, tender music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Release, then clench. Release, then clench again. Everything about the Bay Area duo Cathedrals follows this simple, striking pattern. The singer Brodie Jenkins has a voice that’s both pulpy and ethereal — she leans heavy into big words, her voice robust, then fading ever so dreamily. (Ms. Jenkins is a versatile singer — as a teenager, she was signed to a country music label as part of a family band.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE2/14GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cathedrals, R&B With a Dash of 1980s Rock, at Le Poisson Rouge', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Right Side of Tweeness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cathedrals (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a7d9843-27de-5284-82b2-c4aa53d7b7e9', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a7d9843-27de-5284-82b2-c4aa53d7b7e9'}, {'abstract': 'Free outdoor movie screenings are scheduled for Randalls Island, Bryant Park and Hudson River Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/movies/jaws-opens-manhattan-parks-summer-outdoor-movies.html', 'snippet': 'Free outdoor movie screenings are scheduled for Randalls Island, Bryant Park and Hudson River Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s almost summer, which means free outdoor movie screenings are popping up around Manhattan-area parks. On June 22, for example, the HBO Bryant Park Summer Film Festival, in Midtown, commences on Mondays; the Hudson RiverFlicks Big Hit Wednesdays series kicks off on July 8, on Pier 63 in Chelsea. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jaws’ Opens Manhattan Parks Summer Outdoor Movies', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Screenings Under the Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Randalls Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bryant Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jaws (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fcfcce4-1678-5680-a47b-5fb504bb8657', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fcfcce4-1678-5680-a47b-5fb504bb8657'}, {'abstract': 'Three longtime members of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater are to make their final performances at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/arts/dance/alvin-ailey-company-says-goodbye-to-three-dancers.html', 'snippet': 'Three longtime members of the Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater are to make their final performances at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dancers don’t last forever. The Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater proves that this week as three artists bid farewell. Along with a married couple, Antonio Douthit-Boyd and\xa0Kirven Douthit-Boyd, is Alicia Graf Mack, who returns from her leave of absence for three guest appearances. This transcendent, statuesque dancer sways her hips with the company a final time as the parasol-waving woman in the “Wade in the Water” section of “Revelations” on\xa0Tuesday and Thursday and next Sunday night. Other highlights include the Douthit-Boyds in “Chroma,” “Grace” and “Revelations” on\xa0Thursday, and in “Night Creature” on Saturday. They will soon take over the Center of Creative Arts in St. Louis, where they’ll have some company. Ms. Mack, who recently gave birth to a son, will teach ballet and modern dance at Webster University and Washington University in St. Louis. There’s some solace: The next generation of Ailey is in good hands. (7:30 p.m., Tuesday\xa0through\xa0Thursday; 8 p.m., Friday\xa0and\xa0Saturday; 2 p.m., Saturday; 3 p.m. and 7:30 p.m. next Sunday; David H. Koch Theater, 212-496-0600,\xa0davidkochtheater.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE4/14GUIDE4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alvin Ailey Company Says Goodbye to Three Dancers', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Farewell Performances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douthit-Boyd, Antonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douthit-Boyd, Kirven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5db32813-71e0-5ede-aea9-24366e914555', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5db32813-71e0-5ede-aea9-24366e914555'}, {'abstract': 'This exhibition at the Met details Bingham’s depictions of life on the Missouri and Mississippi Rivers in the 19th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/arts/design/navigating-the-west-celebrates-george-caleb-binghams-paintings.html', 'snippet': 'This exhibition at the Met details Bingham’s depictions of life on the Missouri and Mississippi Rivers in the 19th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American 19th-century genre painting doesn’t often get the museum spotlight, though it should. It has a lot to tell us about where we’ve been and who we are, and some of our best artists made their careers in it. So for more than one reason, I’m looking forward to “Navigating the West: George Caleb Bingham and the River,” which arrives at the Metropolitan Museum of Art on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'