d': 'nyt://article/9207fd74-245b-5493-991a-5beecee6eb54', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9207fd74-245b-5493-991a-5beecee6eb54'}, {'abstract': 'A billionaire tech wizard with terminal cancer offers a doctor control of his estate if she’ll help him prove what, if anything, exists after the body flatlines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/arts/television/jennifer-beals-and-matthew-modine-star-in-tnts-proof-on-life-death-and-beyond.html', 'snippet': 'A billionaire tech wizard with terminal cancer offers a doctor control of his estate if she’ll help him prove what, if anything, exists after the body flatlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parachuting off Mount Everest doesn’t faze Ivan Turing, a tech wizard with a referential surname and a fondness for Steve Jobsian turtlenecks. But terminal adenocarcinoma has given him pause. “I’ve always hated unknowns,” he tells Dr. Carolyn Tyler, a cardiothoracic surgeon with little patience for speculation and a wellspring of grief all her own. “And now that I’m facing the biggest one there is, I want to know what to expect.” His offer: He’ll give her control of his $10 billion estate if she’ll help him prove what, if anything, exists after the body flatlines.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/arts/14GUIDESUB3/14GUIDESUB3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jennifer Beals and Matthew Modine Star in TNT’s ‘Proof,’ on Life, Death and Beyond', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; In Search of the Beyond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beals, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modine, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Proof (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:12:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/204c3faf-f861-58ae-8cd6-958abe0e7ed1', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/204c3faf-f861-58ae-8cd6-958abe0e7ed1'}, {'abstract': 'The ramifications of defaulting and remaining in debt deliberately are usually real and lasting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/your-money/taking-on-student-debt-and-refusing-to-pay.html', 'snippet': 'The ramifications of defaulting and remaining in debt deliberately are usually real and lasting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last couple of decades, we have been engaged in an enormous national experiment, taking impressionable and often ignorant teenagers and young adults and seeing just how much student loan debt they can handle.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1465, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/13money-web/13money-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking On Student Debt, and Refusing to Pay', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Downside of Defaulting on Student Loans ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siegel, Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Bankruptcies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a75109ed-cf14-5456-9f8a-3f870c39873f', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a75109ed-cf14-5456-9f8a-3f870c39873f'}, {'abstract': 'Stalin’s daughter tried to escape his shadow by defecting to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/books/review/stalins-daughter-by-rosemary-sullivan.html', 'snippet': 'Stalin’s daughter tried to escape his shadow by defecting to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young princess walks the corridors of an ancient palace, surrounded by adoring relatives, governesses and tutors. Her father is a beloved ruler of a vast country, and she is his only daughter and favorite child, his “little sparrow,” his “little fly.” She brings him presents of violets and strawberries, and he pets her, showering her in bristly kisses redolent of tobacco. She spends idyllic summers at the family dacha, where her father’s merry friends, whom she calls “aunts” and “uncles,” come on visits and regale her with stories and songs. The world she inhabits seems magical to her, “that place of sunshine.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1621, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/books/review/14GRUSHIN/14GRUSHIN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Stalin’s Daughter,’ by Rosemary Sullivan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaving the Fatherland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Rosemary (1947- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stalin, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Lana (1926-2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Stalin's Daughter: The Extraordinary and Tumultuous Life of Svetlana Alliluyeva (Book)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Olga Grushin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Olga', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grushin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a121f9c-1bec-52df-b55f-24459a559514', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a121f9c-1bec-52df-b55f-24459a559514'}, {'abstract': 'Led by a charismatic, one-eyed rebel and his lover, an outlaw gang roams the Brazilian badlands in the 1920s and ’30s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/books/review/backlands-by-victoria-shorr.html', 'snippet': 'Led by a charismatic, one-eyed rebel and his lover, an outlaw gang roams the Brazilian badlands in the 1920s and ’30s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Usually when reviewing a novel, you must be careful not to give away too much plot. But in the case of Victoria Shorr’s “Backlands,” there’s no such danger: Shorr herself reveals the bare bones of the story in the first few pages. Put simply, “Backlands” is the fictionalized account of a real-life one-eyed bandit called Lampião and his lover, Maria Bonita — famous Brazilian outlaws who took from the rich and gave to the poor. From the early 1920s to his capture in 1938, Lampião and his gang controlled much of the Sertão, a huge and dusty swath of land in the northeast of the country, “almost the size of Spain.” More than once, they were cornered but managed to escape. For a long time, Lampião seemed invincible and his life, as Shorr puts it, “was a tango, full of beauty and danger, mixed.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Backlands,’ by Victoria Shorr', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As if Each Day Were Their Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shorr, Victoria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T15:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Wulf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wulf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/645eae79-00e0-517b-a2db-7f47719ce15d', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/645eae79-00e0-517b-a2db-7f47719ce15d'}, {'abstract': 'New novels explore the lives of Virginia Woolf, George Sand and Emily Dickinson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/books/review/literary-lives.html', 'snippet': 'New novels explore the lives of Virginia Woolf, George Sand and Emily Dickinson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ADELINEA Novel of Virginia WoolfBy Norah Vincent280 pp. Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $23.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '