s to Europe, corruption and poor governance. Even as African economies have grown in the last decade, trade between African nations has lagged behind their exchanges with the rest of the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talks to Begin on Creating a Trade Zone Within Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talks to Begin on Creating a Trade Zone Within Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs (Tariff)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T16:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0134883e-4190-59cf-8e71-769163ee79af', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0134883e-4190-59cf-8e71-769163ee79af'}, {'abstract': 'Léon Blum led France to reform in the Depression era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/books/review/leon-blum-prime-minister-socialist-zionist-by-pierre-birnbaum.html', 'snippet': 'Léon Blum led France to reform in the Depression era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Léon Blum, age 26, imagined Goethe writing a sequel to his renowned “Faust.” Blum’s protagonist, however, was not Goethe’s famous intellectual, who wagers with the Devil to experience everything possible. He was, instead, a socialist seeking justice — although impeded by Mephistopheles. Blum’s Faust passes reforms in Parliament, but “reaction” lands him in prison. Still, obstacles only make him resolute. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Léon Blum: Prime Minister, Socialist, Zionist,’ by Pierre Birnbaum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France’s New Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birnbaum, Pierre (1940- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blum, Leon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitchell Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitchell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d9a4b78-3e96-5ea0-8494-fdc178432c52', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d9a4b78-3e96-5ea0-8494-fdc178432c52'}, {'abstract': 'Here are some of the outstanding issues that need resolution in Sunday’s season finale.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/game-of-thrones-season-5-finale/', 'snippet': 'Here are some of the outstanding issues that need resolution in Sunday’s season finale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s “Thrones” Friday, which means the pop culture cabal takes one last whack at the show before Sunday’s Season 5 finale.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/arts/thrones1/thrones1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLar