r-ways-to-die.html', 'snippet': 'A prosecutor in Germany said Andreas Lubitz looked up terms like “living will” and “dying” and sought information about obtaining poisons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The day before he crashed an Airbus 320 carrying 149 passengers and crew members into the French Alps, Andreas Lubitz safely flew an empty jet from Düsseldorf, Germany, to Berlin, then returned home to his iPad to search terms including “living will,” “suffering” and “dying.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Crash, Germanwings Pilot Searched Web for Ways to Die', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Europe; Germany: Morbid Terms on Co-Pilot’s Search History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Germanwings GmbH', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lubitz, Andreas (1987-2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T18:06:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy and Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a171b6f-8054-57e7-ad2d-a0e612b198e0', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a171b6f-8054-57e7-ad2d-a0e612b198e0'}, {'abstract': 'Recent studies show that women rate better than men in certain leadership qualities, but the number of women in leadership roles is slow to change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/business/dealbook/overcoming-the-confidence-gap-for-women.html', 'snippet': 'Recent studies show that women rate better than men in certain leadership qualities, but the number of women in leadership roles is slow to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I met Lynne Doughtie this week, I was struck by how different it felt sitting with her than with any male chief executive I had met over the years. Six weeks ago, Ms. Doughtie was elected United States chairwoman and chief executive of KPMG. When she takes over the role on July 1, she will become the first woman to serve in both of those roles for a Big Four accounting firm. Cathy Engelbert was chosen as chief executive of Deloitte in February.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/business/db-life-web2/db-life-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/13/business/db-life-web2/db-life-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/business/db-life-web2/db-life-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/business/db-life-web2/db-life-web2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1242, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/business/db-life-web2/db-life-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75