y picked berries from this village, which has been in the strawberry growing business since the mid-17th century, are renowned for their fully ripe flavor. In Brussels, 50 miles to the northwest, Wépion berries fetch a premium price, roughly twice what the competition is going for.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/07/travel/07HEADS1/07HEADS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Belgium’s Strawberry Fields, Perfection’s in the Picking', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secret to Success: Perfection’s in the Picking   ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strawberries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T19:14:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitchel L. Zoler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitchel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Zoler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4743ccea-6de1-50d6-a293-bb0f75ef9cd3', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4743ccea-6de1-50d6-a293-bb0f75ef9cd3'}, {'abstract': 'T’s latest issue celebrates models, gardens, maligned buildings and much more of what’s beautiful right now.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/inside-ts-beauty-issue/', 'snippet': 'T’s latest issue celebrates models, gardens, maligned buildings and much more of what’s beautiful right now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s latest issue celebrates beauty in its many forms. To that end, we’ve rounded up 11 of the most striking models working today — from the youthful Amilna Estevao to the 44-year-old fashion icon Stella Tennant — who epitomize what’s beautiful now. Ashley Brokaw already knows this. As the fashion industry’s leading casting director, she is largely responsible for the latest trend of unusual, unconventional beauties. As on the runway, so in architecture: In a special portfolio, seven leading architects tell us why maligned buildings from Paris to upstate New York are deserving of a second look. Elsewhere, the writer Dan Chiasson sorts through the rusted bicycles and myriad neckties of Robert Rauschenberg, whose archive-in-progress in Mount Vernon, N.Y., is a colorful manifestation of the late artist’s penchant for turning ephemera into art; a trip to Havana, Cuba opens the door to a grand home and cultural meeting place 15 years in the making; Christine Smallwood extols the introduction of so-called outsider artists into major institutions; the novelist and horticulturist Umberto Pasti pens a rumination on the art of gardening; and Natasha Lyonne and John Baldessari cast a critical eye on a zombie gnome and soap made from nightingale droppings. See all stories from this issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 748}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-Cover/14TBeauty-Cover-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/t-magazine/14TBeauty-