': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paperless Post', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T21:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Alford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b07bb1eb-8e2a-5118-a605-c273389befeb', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b07bb1eb-8e2a-5118-a605-c273389befeb'}, {'abstract': "Some of the 600 guests at the Frick Collection's lawn and garden party wore the vibrant orange color of a painting that was the focus of the festivities.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/style/bill-cunningham-flames-in-the-garden.html', 'snippet': "Some of the 600 guests at the Frick Collection's lawn and garden party wore the vibrant orange color of a painting that was the focus of the festivities.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual Fifth Avenue lawn and garden party at the Frick Collection was an exceptional experience made only more so by the rarity of the Fifth Avenue garden that’s part of the Gilded Age home. A painting was the focus of the festivities: “Flaming June” (above) by Fredrick Leighton, a Victorian artist and contemporary of James McNeill Whistler. It was shown alongside the Frick’s four Whistlers. Some of the 600 guests wore the vibrant orange color of the painting. All of the guests made a big effort to dress for the occasion. Many of the Frick family members were present.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Flames in the Garden', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flames in the Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frick Collection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lawns', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whistler, James McNeill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leighton, Frederic (1830-96)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T21:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb2203c-32f6-53c3-b3b4-bf385acfea0f', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb2203c-32f6-53c3-b3b4-bf385acfea0f'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Rogers, president and general manager of the minor league team, starts the day with a couple of cups of coffee and a call to her grandson and ends it with coffee and prayers before bed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/nyregion/how-jane-m-rogers-staten-island-yankees-executive-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Rogers, president and general manager of the minor league team, starts the day with a couple of cups of coffee and a call to her grandson and ends it with coffee and prayers before bed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Staten Island Yankees begin their season on Friday, Jane M. Rogers, the team’s president and general manager, may reflect on the day she answered a want ad for a secretary 16 years ago. She was an at-home mother who had never seen a minor-league baseball game; the Yankees had not yet come to Staten Island. “I had no idea it was going to develop into a career,” Ms. Rogers, 59, said. Now she handles all team logistics and her husband, Michael, a retired sanitation worker, manages the stadium. The two live in Tottenville with a Shih Tzu named Rocket Rogers. “I hate to be called the team mom,” she said. “Sometimes they say that but I don’t like it. I feel like I’m sitting here baking cookies for them, which I don’t.” JOHN LELAND', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14ROUTINE1/14ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': No