bd584', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/78d62562-854b-56e2-a8bb-653f963bd584'}, {'abstract': 'The orchestra closes its season with a three-week Beethoven festival performed with a vocal quartet, the San Francisco Symphony Chorus and the Pacific Boychoir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/arts/music/review-san-francisco-symphony-stages-missa-solemnis-with-a-visual-component.html', 'snippet': 'The orchestra closes its season with a three-week Beethoven festival performed with a vocal quartet, the San Francisco Symphony Chorus and the Pacific Boychoir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Walking into Davies Symphony Hall here on Thursday evening, the audience was met with a promisingly unusual sight. Hanging above the stage were four large screens, more or less rectangular and arranged as if they’d been torn from one another to form a rough cross at the center. Dozens of smaller squares trailed from the rectangles on both sides, as if exploding outward from the cross — or, perhaps, rushing inward to form it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 1797, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/MISSA1/MISSA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: San Francisco Symphony Stages ‘Missa Solemnis’ With a Visual Component', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daunting Sounds and a View to Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beethoven, Ludwig van', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T21:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/74c8c873-27b7-5dbb-a543-a5e21951ddbc', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74c8c873-27b7-5dbb-a543-a5e21951ddbc'}, {'abstract': 'The company gave Rennie Harris’s new dance its premiere as part of a program that included a tribute to Dudley Williams, the troupe’s longest-serving member.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/arts/dance/review-alvin-ailey-troupe-dances-exodus-at-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The company gave Rennie Harris’s new dance its premiere as part of a program that included a tribute to Dudley Williams, the troupe’s longest-serving member.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a choreographer creates a work for Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater, it can seem that only one option exists: try to make another “Revelations.” That, after all, is the signature work, the fail-safe masterpiece that closes nearly every performance. And although its representation of struggle and spiritual transcendence through dance has inspired many bad copies, it has also served as the model for many of the best pieces made for the troupe in recent years: Ronald K. Brown’s 1999 “Grace,” Rennie Harris’s 2011 “Home” — and now, Mr. Harris’s “Exodus.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/13/arts/AILEY/AILEY-thumbStandar