{'abstract': 'The now legal residents of C-Squat pay “house dues,” which go toward utility bills and payments on a bank loan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/nyregion/photographs-from-the-history-of-c-squat-a-punk-homestead.html', 'snippet': 'The now legal residents of C-Squat pay “house dues,” which go toward utility bills and payments on a bank loan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When squatters moved into 155 Avenue C in the late 1980s, they found the brick walk-up gutted by fire and abandoned; they climbed between floors using ladders. They later hung stairs and rebuilt the building, which was called C-Squat and in the ’90s became known for the punk shows in its basement.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographs From the History of C-Squat, a Punk Homestead', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Punk House and Garden ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correal, Annie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squatters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-12T22:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Caption', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bdb22f2-2084-53c2-9b15-c3e79ed5cb93', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bdb22f2-2084-53c2-9b15-c3e79ed5cb93'}, {'abstract': 'She yearned for love but wouldn’t change her look.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/12/the-dowdy-patient/', 'snippet': 'She yea