': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/world/GITMO/GITMO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/world/GITMO/GITMO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '6 Guantánamo Detainees From Yemen Are Transferred to Oman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '6 Guant&aacute;namo Detainees Are Transferred to Oman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T04:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d41b2df-7278-510a-9572-77d6a78b6fc0', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d41b2df-7278-510a-9572-77d6a78b6fc0'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:30 P.M. (HBO) GET ON UP (2014) Chadwick Boseman shuffles, spins and splits as James Brown, “the hardest-working man in show business” — as well as a monumental egotist, perfectionist and harsh taskmaster with a streak of paranoia — in this biopic directed by Tate Taylor (“The Help”). Nelsan Ellis is Bobby Byrd, Brown’s longtime best friend, who sticks around as the wives and girlfriends come and go. “Brown’s music and show business ascendance are the heart and soul of a movie that takes his art very seriously,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “None other than Mick Jagger, who has made no secret of his indebtedness to Brown’s stage moves, is the music producer of this film, which puts music front and center, where it belongs. Brown’s real voice, which never sounds dubbed, is used in remixes of his original recordings.” And while the film “largely skirts the issue of race” along with Brown’s alienation of black audiences because of his support of Richard M. Nixon, “in the end, he stood above it all,” Mr. Holden added. “Having won the game, he dwelt in his own realm, where he ruled once and for always as the Godfather of Soul.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/381a4acd-70bc-5650-9ab7-89555d5d1d6e', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381a4acd-70bc-5650-9ab7-89555d5d1d6e'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, June 13, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 