-response-to-mers-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'The government’s failure to share information quickly contributed to worsening the outbreak, a panel that included experts from the World Health Organization said Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The South Korean government’s failure to share information quickly with the public and establish an efficient disease-control system contributed to worsening the outbreak of Middle East respiratory syndrome in the country, a joint panel of experts from the World Health Organization and South Korea said Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Experts Fault South Korean Response to MERS Outbreak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea’s Response to MERS Cases Is Faulted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MERS (Middle East Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T07:56:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba32a2d-a318-5582-a4e9-d1a0c003af1a', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba32a2d-a318-5582-a4e9-d1a0c003af1a'}, {'abstract': 'Fabrice Grinda, who is worth an estimated $100 million, ditched his 20-acre estate and $300,000 sports car in search of an 