ajor': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T17:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e68655c-e037-5e6d-aab4-943063fe7f80', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e68655c-e037-5e6d-aab4-943063fe7f80'}, {'abstract': 'While diners can order the usual meatballs or sliders, the Southern-tinged menu at Rye House also offers more nuanced fare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/nyregion/restaurant-review-rye-house-in-port-chester.html', 'snippet': 'While diners can order the usual meatballs or sliders, the Southern-tinged menu at Rye House also offers more nuanced fare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first blush, Rye House looks a little like a mead hall, but once your eyes adjust to the dim light, it looks more like a loft apartment with bachelor accouterments: leather upholstery, rough-hewed posts and beams, tilted mirrors, dual flat screens and a well-stocked bar. Was it a surprise that on a Saturday night the Port Chester restaurant was packed with middle-aged guys in untucked Hawaiian shirts gripping frosty glasses of craft beer and goblets of red wine? Were they also holding tickets to hear the likes of Deep Purple at the nearby Capitol Theater? Showtime came and went, and few budged.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINEWE_COMBO1/14DINEWE_COMBO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINEWE_COMBO1/