: 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c83a1c-2b6d-5819-9498-5af270eb5e3b', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c83a1c-2b6d-5819-9498-5af270eb5e3b'}, {'abstract': '“I’m not running for some America,” Mrs. Clinton said at a rally at which she denounced Republican economic policies. “I’m running for all Americans.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/us/hillary-clinton-attacks-republican-economic-policies-in-roosevelt-island-speech.html', 'snippet': '“I’m not running for some America,” Mrs. Clinton said at a rally at which she denounced Republican economic policies. “I’m running for all Americans.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton, in a speech that was at times sweeping and at times policy laden, delivered on Saturday a pointed repudiation of Republican economic policies and a populist promise to reverse the gaping gulf between the rich and poor at her biggest campaign event to date.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton, in Roosevelt Island Speech, Pledges to Close Income Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sounding Populist Themes, Clinton Pledges to Close Gap in Wealth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Roosevelt Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T17:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1cfd16d-8872-5001-bddd-7c2295fa29d0', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1cfd16d-8872-5001-bddd-7c2295fa29d0'}, {'abstract': 'The former first lady and secretary of state promised to “wage and win four fights” — to improve the economy, to help families, to improve national security and to overhaul campaign-finance rules to revitalize American democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/06/13/the-chat-hillary-clintons-rally-speech-instantly-analyzed/', 'snippet': 'The former first lady and secretary of state promised to “wage and win four fights” — to improve the economy, to help families, to improve national security and to overhaul campaign-finance rules to revitalize American democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two months after announcing her presidential candidacy by video, Hillary Rodham Clinton held her first campaign rally shortly before noon Saturday on Roosevelt Island in New York City. Over instant messages, two New York Times political correspondents analyzed Mrs. Clinton’s remarks in real time — as they did with Mrs. Clinton’s announcement video and with the campaign announcements of several other 2016 candidates. Here is an edited version of their chat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/us/14firstdraft-clinton7/14firstdraft-clinton7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/us