itt, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eastern Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T19:06:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9676eabf-ce93-55d9-bf86-d418b87b1a19', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9676eabf-ce93-55d9-bf86-d418b87b1a19'}, {'abstract': 'Local cheeses, bacon, eggs, fruits or vegetables are stuffed into each whopper of a crepe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/nyregion/restaurant-review-jammin-crepes-in-princeton.html', 'snippet': 'Local cheeses, bacon, eggs, fruits or vegetables are stuffed into each whopper of a crepe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cookbook author and French food aficionado Richard Olney wrote of crepes that “their greatest pitfalls derive, no doubt, from their versatility — not in itself a fault, but a quality that teases many a cook into overstepping the boundaries of sense and taste. One should never lose sight of the fragile and delicate, thin, tender thing that is the crepe itself.” Olney, writing in the 1970s, proposed that home cooks roll savory crepes around calf’s brains or, for dessert, sauce them with chartreuse. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 237, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 237}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/nyregion/14DINENJ2/14DINENJ2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Jammin’ Crêpes in Princeton', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filling the Crepe, and the Belly ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Princeton (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Jammin' Crepes (Princeton, NJ, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T19:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phoebe Nobles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phoebe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nobles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/88c3179f-14c2-55ac-a785-e449f1d5d011', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88c3179f-14c2-55ac-a785-e449f1d5d011'}, {'abstract': 'The Cavaliers are 3-0 when the 56-year-old acrobat known as the Amazing Sladek, who will be in Cleveland for Game 6 on Tuesday, performs the death-defying tower of chairs at halftime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/sports/basketball/cavaliers-lucky-charm-teeters-on-six-chairs.html', 'snippet': 'The Cavaliers are 3-0 when the 56-year-old acrobat known as the Amazing Sladek, who will be in Cleveland for Game 6 on Tuesday, performs the death-defying tower of chairs at halftime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — On Sunday afternoon, Gary Borstelmann will load six wooden chairs into the back of his Chrysler minivan and set out for Cleveland from his home in New Smyrna Beach, Fla. He expects that the 1,200-mile drive will take two days, but at least he will have the company of his personal assistant, Patricia Murphy, and his pet turtle, Frick.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/