s', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T20:07:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cbc09f-db77-5330-8f5f-68714eb0313e', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cbc09f-db77-5330-8f5f-68714eb0313e'}, {'abstract': 'Sharing a profession and a name with a famous parent proved to be an honor and a weight for a young sportswriter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/sports/bearing-my-fathers-byline.html', 'snippet': 'Sharing a profession and a name with a famous parent proved to be an honor and a weight for a young sportswriter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until he wandered into The Baltimore Sun in the fall of 1959 and found his calling in life, it would be fair to say that my father suffered from an acute identity crisis. Though his given name was George Melvin, no one called him that, if only to avoid confusion with my grandfather. Around the rowhouse in East Baltimore where Dad grew up, everyone always called him Sonny. As a high school athlete who lettered in three sports, he was known as Otts, the origins of which are unclear. In his incarnation in later years as a fledging bush-league baseball player, he adopted the sobriquet Randy because he felt it created the illusion that he could run faster. I’m not kidding. He actually thought that. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 780}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1576, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14father1/14father1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bearing My Father’s Byline ', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bearing My Father&#8217;s Byline ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kram, Mark (1933-2002)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T20:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kram Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kram', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e40fad-98e5-5e09-8c41-30dcd9a39869', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e40fad-98e5-5e09-8c41-30dcd9a39869'}, {'abstract': 'What is “liquidity” anyway?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/regulation-and-arbitrage-implicitly-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'What is “liquidity” anyway?', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to the FT, the financial fear du jour is no longer Greece, or inflation, or any of the other things that have obsessed markets in recent years; it’s liquidity. We are pointed to a recent column by Stephen Schwarzman, who warns that lack of liquidity is just like when Hitler invaded Poland (sorry, he said that about ending the tax loophole for equity managers) may cause a financial crisis; Nouriel Roubini agrees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulation and Arbitrage (Implicitly Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T20:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL KRUGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRUGMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a372d3-249a-562f-a8a6-b4fe3f31bb36', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a372d3-249a-562f-a8a6-b4fe3f31bb36'}, {'abstract': 'What is “liquidity” anyway?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/13/regulation-and-arbitrage-implicitly-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'What is “liquidity” anyway?', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to the FT, the financial fear du jour is no longer Greece, or inflation, or any of the other things that have obsessed markets in recent years; it’s liquidity. We are pointed to a recent column by Stephen Schwarzman, who warns that lack of liquidity is just like when Hitler invaded Poland (sorry, he said that about ending the tax loophole for equity managers) may cause a financial crisis; Nouriel Roubini agrees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulation and Arbitrage (Implicitly Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-13T20:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1aee579-0d9c-56cf-a6a0-fbb0f029d2d9', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1aee579-0d9c-56cf-a6a0-fbb0f029d2d9'}, {'abstract': 'Krystof Srebrakowski, the organist at Tampa Bay Lightning games, has helped bring the crowd alive during the Lightning’s run to the Stanley Cup finals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/sports/hockey/organ-and-organist-lend-the-lightning-a-thunderous-grandeur.html', 'snippet': 'Krystof Srebrakowski, the organist at Tampa Bay Lightning games, has helped bring the crowd alive during the Lightning’s run to the Stanley Cup finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — At the south end of Amalie Arena, perched atop a stage, sits the largest organ in the N.H.L. It features five rows of keys, four rows of switches, a host of buttons and, underneath, several pedals. At times, Krystof Srebrakowski, the organist, seems to use every one of its features, bobbing his head, his eyes closed, his feet dancing between pedals, his fingers gliding along.\xa0', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/DOG-14organ/DOG-14organ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Organ and Organist Lend the Lightning a Thunderous Grandeur', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Organ and Organist Lend the Lightning Grandeur ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organs (Musical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {