mmary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a544007-2bf1-5915-987e-0dd4974bacd4', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a544007-2bf1-5915-987e-0dd4974bacd4'}, {'abstract': 'Park, ranked second in the world, is at 14 under for the tournament and leads second-place Sei Young Kim by two strokes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/sports/golf/inbee-park-with-benefit-of-early-homework-takes-two-stroke-lead-in-womens-pga-championship.html', 'snippet': 'Park, ranked second in the world, is at 14 under for the tournament and leads second-place Sei Young Kim by two strokes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HARRISON, N.Y. — Brad Beecher thought it would be a good idea to get an early sneak peek. He had heard how demanding Westchester County Club’s West Course could be, so rather than fly from Canada on Monday for a first look, he and the player he caddies for, Inbee Park, played a handful of practice rounds last month. Beecher watched as Park got a grasp on how big and bold the course is.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14LPGAsub/14LPGAsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14LPGAsub/14LPGAsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14LPGAsub/14LPGAsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14LPGAsub/14LPGAsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su