ew York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Simpler, Uncomplicated Timepieces Are Back', 'kicker': 'Watch Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Simpler Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-14T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32b1b190-13ba-524b-ad39-192b0327eeba', 'word_count': 17, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32b1b190-13ba-524b-ad39-192b0327eeba'}, {'abstract': 'The art-stuffed homes of the knitwear brand’s three designers influence their eclectic workspace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/t-magazine/in-the-east-village-and-soho-orleys-family-values.html', 'snippet': 'The art-stuffed homes of the knitwear brand’s three designers influence their eclectic workspace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Established in 2011 by Matthew Orley, his now-wife Samantha and Matthew’s younger brother, Alex, the jacquard-heavy, knitwear-centric brand Orley is 100 percent a family affair, from motivation to execution. With its men’s, and newly minted women’s, ready-to-wear lines, “our collections tend to be autobiographical,” Alex says. “The tenets of the brand take things a little nostalgic or familiar and recontextualize those retro feelings into something modern in their boldness. A lot of what we do comes from our grandparents’ strong sense of self. We grew up around them. They were very esoteric dressers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the East Village and SoHo, Orley’s Family Values', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-14T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Holmlund', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holmlund', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ee27e0-33ff-5f95-a1a9-870c0b6e0dfd', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9ee27e0-33ff-5f95-a1a9-870c0b6e0dfd'}, {'abstract': 'Antoine Vermette broke a 1-1 tie two minutes into the third period, and Chicago edged host Tampa Bay to move a victory away from winning the Stanley Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/14/sports/hockey/chicago-blackhawks-close-in-on-stanley-cup-with-another-one-goal-victory.html', 'snippet': 'Antoine Vermette broke a 1-1 tie two minutes into the third period, and Chicago edged host Tampa Bay to move a victory away from winning the Stanley Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Ben Bishop stood in the crease looking as brave as he could in the third period Saturday as the Chicago Blackhawks mounted another charge toward him. The Blackhawks knew that Bishop, the Tampa Bay Lightning goalie, was dealing with an undisclosed injury, and they had challenged him every chance they could, testing the limits of his will and his tolerance for pain.\xa0', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14NHL1/14NHL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14NHL1/14NHL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/14/sports/14NHL1/14NHL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, '