ions', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T00:58:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/704051bc-c030-52de-b7d3-dcfa22532de7', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/704051bc-c030-52de-b7d3-dcfa22532de7'}, {'abstract': 'If the Blackhawks win on Monday, it will be their third Stanley Cup since 2010 — a stunning prospect for a city that adores its sports teams, but rarely ponders championships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/us/blackhawks-fans-show-that-chicago-can-love-a-winner-too.html', 'snippet': 'If the Blackhawks win on Monday, it will be their third Stanley Cup since 2010 — a stunning prospect for a city that adores its sports teams, but rarely ponders championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The national anthem had barely begun, but the red mass of pounding, stomping, cheering people inside the United Center was in full frenzy. If there is a Midwestern version of Los Angeles’s star-speckled courtside scene, it was in this crowd: John Cusack, the actor; Danica Patrick, the auto racer; Billy Corgan, the musician.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/15/us/15chicago-01/15chicago-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/15/us/15chicago-01/15chicago-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/15/us/15ch