me runs short for Greece to make changes to unlock aid payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — A chorus of voices on Monday called on European Union authorities to plan for Greece to default on its huge pile of debt after bailout talks between Athens and its creditors deteriorated over the weekend.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Is Urged to Prepare for Greek Default as Stances Harden on Debt Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Is Urged to Prepare for Greek Default as Stances Harden on Debt Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kanter, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurozone', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weidmann, Jens', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Athens (Greece)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T11:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter, Alison Smale and Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58823f8d-7e87-5c48-84e9-e0573f9198a5', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58823f8d-7e87-5c48-84e9-e0573f9198a5'}, {'abstract': 'Greek Debt Talks Break Down Again | Conflicts of Interest in Private Equity Fee Practices | Challenges of Maintaining a Business Dynasty | Saks Fifth Avenue’s Owner to Buy German Chain', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/morning-agenda-greek-debt-talks-break-down-again/', 'snippet': 'Greek Debt Talks Break Down Again | Conflicts of Interest in Private Equity Fee Practices | Challenges of Maintaining a Business Dynasty | Saks Fifth Avenue’s Owner to Buy German Chain', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEK DEBT TALKS BREAK DOWN AGAIN | Another attempt at a bailout agreement for Greece fell apart on Sunday night after Greek officials angrily contended that their European counterparts in the weekend talks did not have the authority to negotiate any kind of deal,  James Kanter and Landon Thomas Jr. write in The New York Times. The Greek officials who traveled to Brussels for the talks were Nikos Pappas, a close confidant of Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras, and Yannis Dragasakis, the deputy prime minister. They met with senior-level European officials, none of whom had the same rank in their respective government posts. “They wanted us to hit our targets by slashing pensions and increasing taxes,” said one senior member of the Greek negotiating team, Mr. Kanter and Mr. Thomas write. “But they had no mandate to negotiate.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Greek Debt Talks Break Down Again', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Public Employees Retirement System', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T11:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e5f3503-ffc3-5609-9bc2-6b5cd37a1aba', 'word_count': 1867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e5f3503-ffc3-5609-9bc2-6b5cd37a1aba'}, {'abstract': 'Keeping it cool for the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/shouting-grexit-in-a-crowded-theater/', 'snippet': 'Keeping it cool for the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers have noted that I haven’t said much about the Greek crisis in the past few days. Indeed. It’s crunch time, and right now everyone involved needs to engage in quiet, cool deliberation. There’s really nothing more outsiders can say, at least in public, that we haven’t already said. So it seems to me that for now I should hold back a bit. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shouting Grexit in a Crowded Theater', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T11:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL KRUGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRUGMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f306e40-bb71-5d3d-9ee2-5db4b7386b96', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f306e40-bb71-5d3d-9ee2-5db4b7386b96'}, {'abstract': 'Keeping it cool for the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/shouting-grexit-in-a-crowded-theater/', 'snippet': 'Keeping it cool for the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers have noted that I haven’t said much about the Greek crisis in the past few days. Indeed. It’s crunch time, and right now everyone involved needs to engage in quiet, cool deliberation. There’s really nothing more outsiders can say, at least in public, that we haven’t already said. So it seems to me that for now I should hold back a bit. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shouting Grexit in a Crowded Theater', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T11:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508da814-d674-5439-bc95-efff022d6ad8', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508da814-d674-5439-bc95-efff022d6ad8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Chow, of the pro-Beijing Democratic Alliance for the Betterment and Progress of Hong Kong, said it would be a mistake to vote against a proposal to allow all those eligible to cast a ballot in the 2017 election for the city’s top leader.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/q-and-a-holden-chow-on-china-elections-and-hong-kongs-attitude/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Chow, of the pro-Beijing Democratic Alliance for the Betterment and Progress of Hong Kong, said it would be a mistake to vote against a proposal to allow all those eligible to cast a ballot in the 2017 election for the city’s top leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hong Kong’s legislature is set to vote this week on a proposal to allow all eligible voters in the former British colony the chance to vote in the 2017 election for the city’s top leader, the chief executive. Supporters and opponents say the measure, which will require the support of two-thirds of the 70 delegates, is likely to be voted down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/15/blogs/15sino-chow/15sino-chow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 931, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/15/blogs/15sino-chow/15sino-chow-