il down the GOP nomination, or even to establish himself as the candidate of the Republican “moderates” (I think we always need scare quotes in this context). Jeb is nowhere close to even having the kind of position Mitt Romney had at this stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Absence of Jebmentum', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T12:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL KRUGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRUGMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ccfb307-c7cf-5025-b66b-a0598066b00d', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ccfb307-c7cf-5025-b66b-a0598066b00d'}, {'abstract': 'Why him, anyway?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/absence-of-jebmentum/', 'snippet': 'Why him, anyway?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nate Cohn notes Jeb Bush’s failure to nail down the GOP nomination, or even to establish himself as the candidate of the Republican “moderates” (I think we always need scare quotes in this context). Jeb is nowhere close to even having the kind of position Mitt Romney had at this stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Absence of Jebmentum', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T12:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f9cb9c-a09a-54ff-8c26-6e0eeb55dfe4', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f9cb9c-a09a-54ff-8c26-6e0eeb55dfe4'}, {'abstract': 'She’s clearly considering fashion, as are her advisers, and using it to manipulate perception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/16/fashion/why-it-matters-that-hillary-clinton-wore-ralph-lauren.html', 'snippet': 'She’s clearly considering fashion, as are her advisers, and using it to manipulate perception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At her campaign opening rally on Roosevelt Island on Saturday (to be distinguished from her campaign announcement, in April), Hillary Rodham Clinton donned her now-signature look: a bright blue pantsuit with a matching bright blue shirt underneath. She stuck out a mile, matched her H campaign logo — which was also the design of her stage — and looked appropriately patriotic, especially when standing next to Bill Clinton in his red polo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16OTR-A/16OTR-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16OTR-A/16OTR-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16OTR-A/16OTR-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16OTR-A/16OTR-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16OTR-A/16