am was to blame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/16/world/africa/suicide-bombers-strike-chads-capital.html', 'snippet': 'At least 23 people were killed in the bombings in Ndjamena, and the president’s office said the Nigerian terrorist group Boko Haram was to blame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — Suicide bombers struck for the first time in the capital of Chad on Monday morning, apparently in retaliation for the leading role the country has played in a regional war against the Nigerian terrorist group Boko Haram, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suicide Bombers Strike Chad’s Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Africa; Chad: Suicide Bombers Strike Police Targets in Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ndjamena (Chad)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T17:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8683cc6c-6968-56e2-9ca9-ae2bfca17657', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8683cc6c-6968-56e2-9ca9-ae2bfca17657'}, {'abstract': 'This eight-part series on SundanceTV follows a young East German soldier who is recruited, a