nds overweight, but a blood test showed he might have fatty liver disease. At last, his mother took him to a pediatric weight management clinic in New Haven. But she did not at all like the dietitian’s advice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 605}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2032, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/science/16OBESITYJP/16OBESITYJP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Parents’ Denial Fuels Childhood Obesity Epidemic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blind to a Child’s Obesity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Jan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-15T21:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86ef56dd-23e8-5d25-a252-082a57117dc6', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86ef56dd-23e8-5d25-a252-082a57117dc6'}, {'abstract': 'The interdisciplinary artist Crystal Wagner’s latest mural, at 1515 Broadway, opens tomorrow.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/15/crystal-wagner-wild-efflux-viacom/', 'snippet': 'The interdisciplinary artist Crystal Wagner’s latest mural, at 1515 Broadway, opens tomorrow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The interdisciplinary artist Crystal Wagner isn’t “interested in people looking at art as an object on the wall, or a print over there,” she says. Instead, Wagner hopes to elicit a sense of wonder through her three-dimensional murals made from birthday party tablecloths stuffed into a chicken-wire armature, with paper embellishments. The ingredients are deliberate: “A lot of our aesthetic experience is defined by the places that we visit on a daily basis — you don’t even realize that they’re burning themselves into your retina,” she notes. “It’s the way that the cereals are lined up on shelves, or how Coke cans sit next to the Mountain Dew. So, I wanted to create organic bioforms that seem to grow, but using materials that people are exposed to.”'