officers with a knife. Last month, two Muslims attacked an anti-Islamic conference in Garland, Tex. The month before, a Muslim man was charged with plotting to drive a truck bomb onto a military installation in Kansas. If you keep up with the news, you know that a small but steady stream of American Muslims, radicalized by overseas extremists, are engaging in violence here in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Growing Right-Wing Terror Threat', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Other Terror Threat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kurzman, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schanzer, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Executive Research Forum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Kurzman and David Schanzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurzman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schanzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d87a9324-ec89-5fc7-8a46-1a4c826450f3', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d87a9324-ec89-5fc7-8a46-