 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spagnuolo, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierre-Paul, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T20:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2fefac2-ee5c-5daf-aa47-2ce2db4da0ab', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2fefac2-ee5c-5daf-aa47-2ce2db4da0ab'}, {'abstract': 'As I looked ahead to my husband’s long term deployment, I felt as if I were drowning—until the Navy issued me a life preserver.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/16/military-spouses-facing-deployment-but-not-alone/', 'snippet': 'As I looked ahead to my husband’s long term deployment, I felt as if I were drowning—until the Navy issued me a life preserver.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Drowning is silent.” During my high school life-guarding days, our manager used to repeat the phrase in earnest. Lately, the verbiage has played in a loop in my mind, as I struggle physically and emotionally with my husband’s coming deployment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/us/motherlode-life-preserver/motherlode-life-preserver-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/16/us/motherlode-life-preserver/motherlode-life-preserver-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo