son, Burberry, Alexander McQueen and Craig Green embody the funk and finesse that set the men’s wear shows apart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/fashion/mens-style/at-london-mens-fashion-week-bigger-is-not-necessarily-better.html', 'snippet': 'Margaret Howell, J.W. Anderson, Burberry, Alexander McQueen and Craig Green embody the funk and finesse that set the men’s wear shows apart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In this city, men’s fashion week wends inevitably, ineluctably to the pub. That British institution (unlike the suit, the coat, the tie, the shoe and almost any other institution that intersects with the twice-yearly men’s wear shows here) is all but impervious to change.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/fashion/16LONDONSMENS5/16LONDONSMENS5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Margaret Howell, J.W. Anderson, Burberry, Alexander McQueen and Craig Green,\xa0Bigger Is Not Necessarily Better', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In London, Bigger Isn’t Always Better', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bailey, Christopher (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Men's Fashion Week", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howell, Margaret (1946- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Craig', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T21:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Men’s Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/59928e0c-a295-5210-9295-320c163c3558', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59928e0c-a295-5210-9295-320c163c3558'}, {'abstract': 'The cases, one criminal and the other civil, involved an international cartel’s price-fixing of liquid-crystal displays used in computers and cellphones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/technology/supreme-court-rejects-2-antitrust-cases.html', 'snippet': 'The cases, one criminal and the other civil, involved an international cartel’s price-fixing of liquid-crystal displays used in computers and cellphones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court this week declined to review a pair of antitrust cases involving an international price-fixing cartel, despite the urging of some legal experts, economists and the National Association of Manufacturers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Rejects 2 Antitrust Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Lets Stand 2 Antitrust Case Decisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohr, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquid Crystal Displays', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motorola Mobility LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T21:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d5dcad0-9b80-54f2-9360-4d30a86b4cbc', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d5dcad0-9b80-54f2-9360-4d30a86b4cbc'}, {'abstract': 'Over the next few weeks, workmen will be taking down 30 windows for restoration. In the meantime, translucent photographs of some panels will be on display.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/16/stained-glass-at-riverside-church-removed-for-repairs/', 'snippet': 'Over the next few weeks, workmen will be taking down 30 windows for restoration. In the meantime, translucent photographs of some panels will be on display.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chiseling at sooty, buckling and leaky portraits of medieval saints in radiant red and blue, workmen are hoisting about 30 stained-glass windows out of Riverside Church in Manhattan. For the next few weeks, crews from Clagnan Stained Glass Studio in Wall Township, N.J., advised by the Massachusetts consultant Julie L. Sloan, will be digging out chunks of caulk to release the panes. Designed in the 1920s by the prominent Boston glass workshops of Wilbur H. Burnham and Wright Goodhue, the the stained-glass panels will undergo a year of repair at Clagnan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stained Glass at Riverside Church Removed for Repairs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stained Glass', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riverside Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wall Township (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T21:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de95aea4-d9ea-536c-a7bb-6dacb8e940f6', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de95aea4-d9ea-536c-a7bb-6dacb8e940f6'}, {'abstract': 'The architect Santiago Calatrava reads The New York Times of June 16, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/06/16/reading-the-times-with-santiago-calatrava/', 'snippet': 'The architect Santiago Calatrava reads The New York Times of June 16, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santiago Calatrava is a Spanish architect, structural engineer, sculptor and painter. His projects include the World Trade Center Transportation Hub, which opens this month; the Park Avenue Sculptures, installed last week along the central median on Park Avenue between 52nd and 55th Streets in New York City, are on view through November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/blogs/calatrava/calatrava-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 505, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/blogs/calatrava/calatrava-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 505, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/blogs/calatrava/calatrava-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',