name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Maurice R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starr Cos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Thomas C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-16T23:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a658b44-4ee5-5959-8ad3-34aa72406fad', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a658b44-4ee5-5959-8ad3-34aa72406fad'}, {'abstract': 'On the oral fixations of athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/16/magazine/stephen-currys-mouth-guard-an-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'On the oral fixations of athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Curry is a delirious and incorrigible show-off: He not only throws no-look passes, he also shoots no-look 3-pointers. He’s a boy wonder: See him for the first time on television and you might mistake him for a 12-year-old. (In reality he is 27, and 6 feet 3 inches tall.) He’s an egomaniac, sort of (but who isn’t, in the N.B.A.?). In 2013, an interviewer asked him whom he would pick to shoot, given one chance to win a game and a lineup of Michael Jordan, Kobe Bryant, Ray Allen, Reggie Miller — and Stephen Curry. Curry said: Jordan. But after Jordan, he continued, “I’m No. 2.” At the time, he was 25. He has since become the game’s greatest scorer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/16/magazine/