veloped in darkness, discernible only by the sound of his voice and the blinking red lights of the two GoPro cameras strapped to his helmet, seen in a series of popular YouTube videos.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Stand, World Trade Center Parachutist Stresses His Skill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trade Center Parachutist, on Stand, Stresses His Skill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remnick, Noah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parachutes and Parachute Jumping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markovich, Marko (1986- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, James (1981- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossig, Andrew (1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T03:43:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Remnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Remnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85af63dd-cf07-535b-9bd9-2776e75f39d7', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85af63dd-cf07-535b-9bd9-2776e75f39d7'}, {'abstract': '', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2015/06/16/magazine/21mag-ethicists.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxicab Confessions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T03:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/ce2860c7-a32e-5ef5-9ad7-743ab49f06e7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/ce2860c7-a32e-5ef5-9ad7-743ab49f06e7'}, {'abstract': "Régime des Fleurs' newest scent smells, according to one of its creators, like the forest reflected in a pond.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/t-magazine/regime-des-fleurs-mirror.html', 'snippet': "Régime des Fleurs' newest scent smells, according to one of its creators, like the forest reflected in a pond.", 'lead_paragraph': 'For a pair known for their noses, Ezra Woods and Alia Raza, the perfumers and co-creators of Régime des Fleurs, are surprisingly visual. They begin creating their scents by filling inspiration boards with what seem like random collages of contemporary art, ancient landscapes, baroque interiors and iconic clothing. Mirror, their newest bottle, is “a nod to Narcissus, who infamously gazed down at his own reflection in the water,” Raza says. “We also used a rare absolute of narcissus jonquil, which adds an earthy floral note without sweetness.” Made in collaboration with the fashion and design website the Line, the scent itself is “about a reflection of an image as opposed to the image itself, so the fragrance is a blurred, impressionistic take on a few different themes,” says Woods. In this case, notes of green galbanum, smoky gaiac wood, dry violet and clean charcoal come together, Raza says, like “a sketch of a forest reflected in a pond.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17perfume-bobb/17perfume-bobb-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Olfactory Ode to Narcissus', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Bobb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22aaa4c8-12fe-52e6-bf48-070593ee4f6d', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22aaa4c8-12fe-52e6-bf48-070593ee4f6d'}, {'abstract': 'The wave-riding champion and surf filmmaker Mikey DeTemple opens the doors to his nautical-themed Williamsburg apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/t-magazine/the-beachy-pad-of-brooklyns-lone-pro-surfer.html', 'snippet': 'The wave-riding champion and surf filmmaker Mikey DeTemple opens the doors to his nautical-themed Williamsburg apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mikey DeTemple is a five-year ASP World Longboard tour vet, a four-time East Coast Surfing Champion and an accomplished filmmaker whose feature “Sight/Sound” was the best-selling surf film of 2011. For the past three years, the beach-blond, Brooklyn-bearded 30-year-old and his fiancée, Lisa Myers, have shared a second-floor Williamsburg walk-up. “I needed to be somewhere I could park my truck so I could take off to go surf,” explains DeTemple, who says he’ll drive anywhere within a six-hour radius for waves. (“If you want to do it in New York,” he says, “you’ve really got to work for it.”) A space that felt like Montauk — where DeTemple lived before meeting Myers, and where the couple continues to keep a home — was also essential. “We needed it to be bright,” DeTemple says. “At heart, we are beach people, no matter where we live,” Myers adds. “I would pour sand in here if I could.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Beachy Pad of Brooklyn’s Lone Pro Surfer', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Crystal Meers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Crystal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/336d7ee4-1b05-5cbc-821f-6d875ab076d5', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/336d7ee4-1b05-5cbc-821f-6d875ab076d5'}, {'abstract': 'At not quite two months old, La Maison Plisson has quickly garnered a dedicated following.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/t-magazine/maison-plisson-paris-restaurant-store.html', 'snippet': 'At not quite two months old, La Maison Plisson has quickly garnered a dedicated following.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Paris, La Maison Plisson, a stylish new cafe-restaurant-grocery store in the Marais, hasn’t even been open for two months, but it has already become something of a gastronomic institution. The large, airy shop showcases France’s finest foodstuffs, which is why the original inspiration for this project may come as a big surprise: the specialty food shops of New York City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/t-magazine/17maison-lobrano-1/17maison-lobrano-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris’s Newest Purveyor of France’s Finest Foods Was Inspired by New York Specialty Shops', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d99db6-db12-58ab-9c98-112295cdeab7', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d99db6-db12-58ab-9c98-112295cdeab7'}, {'abstract': 'Golden State won its first N.B.A. championship since 1975 and denied LeBron James a title with Cleveland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/sports/basketball/nba-finals-2015-warriors-win-title-beating-cavaliers.html', 'snippet': 'Golden State won its first N.B.A. championship since 1975 and denied LeBron James a title with Cleveland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — The Golden State Warriors launched some 8,900 shots this season. They attempted layups and 3-pointers, runners and elbow jumpers. They dazzled fans and overwhelmed opponents. But every time the ball left their fingertips, the Warriors seemed to be building toward something bigger and better, toward the brightest stage and the grandest prize.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/sports/17finals-hp/17finals-hp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden State Warriors End N.B.A. Title Drought With Victory Over Cavaliers', 'kicker': 'Warriors 105, Cavaliers 97', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drought Ends in Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden State Warriors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NBA Championship', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06769e31-23fa-5e9b-84fc-066c17825e50', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06769e31-23fa-5e9b-84fc-066c17825e50'}, {'abstract': 'The Regal Cinemas location has seen an 88 percent increase in attendance and a threefold increase in ticket revenue since installing 4DX technology last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/business/media/seats-that-move-with-the-onscreen-action-lift-revenue-for-los-angeles-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Regal Cinemas location has seen an 88 percent increase in attendance and a threefold increase in ticket revenue since installing 4DX technology last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — As American movie theater chains look for ways to increase profits, a Regal Cinemas location here has hit by removing standard seats and replacing them with ones that move with the film, using a technology called 4DX.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seats That Move With the Onscreen Action Lift Revenue for Los Angeles Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regal Entertainment Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANSCHUTZ ENTERTAINMENT GROUP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regal Cinemas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CJ 4DPlex (Los Angeles, Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/436577e3-e661-5bd9-93fd-fa3bd5d705be', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436577e3-e661-5bd9-93fd-fa3bd5d705be'}, {'abstract': 'Almost a quarter of journalists from Syria have been forced into exile since 2010, a leading press advocacy group said in a report released Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/world/hundreds-of-journalists-exiled-globally-syria-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'Almost a quarter of journalists from Syria have been forced into exile since 2010, a leading press advocacy group said in a report released Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' At least 452 journalists around the world have been forced into exile since 2010, almost a quarter of them from Syria, a leading press advocacy group said in a report released Wednesday. The report by the group, the Committee to Protect Journalists, attributed the disproportionately large number of exiled Syrian journalists to their harassment and fear of imprisonment by the Syrian government, as well as to threats and attacks from the Islamic State and other militant groups embroiled in the country’s civil war. According to the committee’s research, the top countries from which journalists have fled over the past five years are Syria with 101, Ethiopia with 57 and Iran with 52. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hundreds of Journalists Exiled Globally, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing |', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hundreds of Journalists Exiled Globally, With 1 in 4 From Syria, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T04:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b6419b9-376d-5a91-bf21-1795b31e3a37', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b6419b9-376d-5a91-bf21-1795b31e3a37'}, {'abstract': 'The Basilica SoundScape festival in Hudson, N.Y., will take place Sept. 11-13.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/at-basilica-soundscape-festival-electronics-post-punk-and-noise/', 'snippet': 'The Basilica SoundScape festival in Hudson, N.Y., will take place Sept. 11-13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Basilica SoundScape festival in Hudson, N.Y., has announced the lineup for its fourth edition on Wednesday, to run Sept.11-13. The f