ased a series of recommendations aimed at overhauling the general election presidential debates, with the goal of drawing more viewers and allowing voters to emerge with a better understanding of the candidates and their pos...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A presidential debate season that begins in mid-September. A television studio backdrop without a live studio audience. And a “chess clock” model, where each candidate is allotted 45 minutes of speaking time, which begins ticking down when they start talking.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/17/us/politics/17firstdraft_debateoverhaul/17firstdraft_debateo