erning body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An investigation by the authorities in Switzerland into the activities of FIFA, world soccer’s governing body, will include the examination of more than 50 suspicious financial relationships, the country’s chief federal prosecutor said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspicious Swiss Bank Deals to Be Part of FIFA Investigation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swiss Prosecutor Details Scope of FIFA Inquiry ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Michael J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2018 (Soccer)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2022 (Soccer)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valcke, Jerome', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zurich (Switzerland)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T11:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/846e18ac-a005-5c07-8073-b4b1adee96f7', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/846e18ac-a005-5c07-8073-b4b1adee96f7'}, {'abstract': 'Learning to make tortilla española from the owners of Despaña, Manhattan’s Spanish-food emporium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/21/magazine/the-king-of-tapas.html', 'snippet': 'Learning to make tortilla española from the owners of Despaña, Manhattan’s Spanish-food emporium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the house that jamón built, the castle of chorizo, the mansion of manchego. The Spanish food mecca Despaña, in SoHo, is a landmark shop for food lovers, its dark wood finishes and white subway-tile walls bringing together the sights of Spain and New York. When I arrived to meet its owners, Marcos and Angélica Intriago, they welcomed me with tortilla española: potatoes and onions fat with olive oil and bound with egg into a neat little cake — the king of tapas. “But the problem with tortilla,” Angélica said to me, “is that Americans don’t want to pay for it because it’s just potatoes and eggs, and Spaniards don’t want to pay for it because it doesn’t taste like their mother’s.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/magazine/21eat1/21mag-21eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The King of Tapas', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The King of Tapas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tortillas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T11:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis Lam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d991faf8-52de-52eb-9ef1-0fd6f0fc0090', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d991faf8-52de-52eb-9ef1-0fd6f0fc0090'}, {'abstract': 'A radical idea for saving FIFA from itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/magazine/who-owns-soccer.html', 'snippet': 'A radical idea for saving FIFA from itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early this month, after Sepp Blatter trudged off the stage following his announcement that he would be retiring from the presidency of FIFA, he was followed at the podium by a man named Domenico Scala, the FIFA official who is charged with overseeing the election to replace him. Implicitly acknowledging the furor that prompted Blatter’s departure — the arrests of seven soccer officials in Zurich on corruption charges the week before — Scala said Blatter’s decision “created an opportunity for us to go further than FIFA has before — to fundamentally change the way in which FIFA is structured.” Scala also called Blatter’s announcement “courageous,” saying: “I know that he has truly acted with the best interests of FIFA and football in his heart. I have a great amount of respect for the president and the role that he has played in championing reform within FIFA.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/magazine/08mag-blatter-1/08mag-blatter-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/08/magazine/08mag-blatter-1/08mag-blatter-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/magazine/08mag-blatter-1/08mag-blatter-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/magazine/08mag-blatter-1/08mag-blatter-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/08/magazine/08mag-blatter-1/08mag-blatter-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail