ysts Expect Greek Exit to Shake, But Not Shatter, Europe', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOBS’S LEGACY SHADOWS OUSTED CHIEFS’ RETURN | Jack Dorsey’s return to Twitter invites comparisons to another high-profile comeback of a chief executive who had been ousted from the company he founded – that is, Steve Jobs,  Steven Davidoff Solomon writes in the Deal Professor column. “The legend of Steve Jobs lingers over Silicon Valley,” he writes. “One of its many forms encourages founders to return triumphantly to ‘‘save’ their brands.” Like Jobs, Mr. Dorsey will be rejoining his company as interim chief executive. And Mr. Dorsey, who is also the chief executive of the payments company Square, will now be running two companies at the same time, much like Jobs ran Apple and Pixar for nine years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Jobs’s Legacy Shadows Ousted Chiefs’ Return', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsey, Jack', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '