is might allow Russia to break the unity of the 28-nation bloc in its response to the conflict in Ukraine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.U. Agrees to Extend Economic Sanctions Against Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Is Set to Extend Sanctions on Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgins, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Seven', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T15:26:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36832fee-6132-5caa-a380-a045efd9c54d', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36832fee-6132-5caa-a380-a045efd9c54d'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Francis and the promise of systemic accountability within the Catholic Church.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/the-end-of-the-sex-abuse-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis and the promise of systemic accountability within the Catholic Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conversation about Catholicism and Pope Francis is about to be dominated by\xa0the topics of the environment and climate change, thanks to tomorrow’s (official; there have been leaks) release of the pontiff’s ecological encyclical, Laudato Si. But let me\xa0sneak in a belated comment on last week’s news that the Vatican is setting up a tribunal to handle accusations of negligence by bishops in sex abuse cases, with coincided, probably not coincidentally, with the resignations of the archbishop of Minneapolis-St. Paul and his auxiliary over their handling of a now-defrocked predator priest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The End of the Sex Abuse Crisis', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Encyclicals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T15:27:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/789aa07b-0c09-57d3-b588-f9d37eef63dd', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789aa07b-0c09-57d3-b588-f9d37eef63dd'}, {'abstract': 'A new study has found a simple way to significantly reduce teenage smoking: raise the tobacco sales age to 21.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/to-cut-teen-smoking-raise-tobacco-sales-age/', 'snippet': 'A new study has found a simple way to significantly reduce teenage smoking: raise the tobacc