/review-leon-golubs-riot-revisits-political-art-with-a-sense-of-the-absurd.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Golub’s paintings at Hauser & Wirth reflect a sardonic sense of the absurd and an acute awareness of barbarous villainy around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intrinsically theatrical, oil painting is an ideal medium for political art. Leon Golub knew this and made the most of it in mural-size pictures of terrorists, torturers and hit-squad goons that more or less fought their way into existence, being repeatedly painted and scraped down and sometimes cut up and reconfigured. These are the kinds of paintings we see on the first floor of a career sampler of Mr. Golub’s work at Hauser & Wirth, a spinoff of a recent retrospective at the Serpentine Gallery in London.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 506}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1728, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1/19LEONGOLUBGALLERY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 