s D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allende, Salvador', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinochet Ugarte, Augusto', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copa America (Soccer)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T19:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57b4cd2f-1e1e-5a81-b435-8a2a66c95bae', 'word_count': 1580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57b4cd2f-1e1e-5a81-b435-8a2a66c95bae'}, {'abstract': 'In this comedy, Sharon Horgan and Rob Delaney play a couple brought closer together after an unexpected pregnancy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/arts/television/review-catastrophe-on-amazon-prime-shares-a-special-comedy-relationship.html', 'snippet': 'In this comedy, Sharon Horgan and Rob Delaney play a couple brought closer together after an unexpected pregnancy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Catastrophe,” a bittersweet British television comedy making its American debut on Amazon Prime, is the product of an unlikely artistic union. One of its creators, Sharon Horgan, is a veteran sitcom writer and star who could be fairly called the Tina Fey of British TV, in stature if not style. The other, Rob Delaney, is an American comedian best known for having more than a million Twitter followers; he’s headlining a TV show for the first time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18CATASTROPHE/1