nt': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/04ee4a13-90fc-5329-8985-dbcc358df833'}, {'abstract': 'A new book, “Postdigital Artisans,” explores the influence of digital technology in creative fields.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/postdigital-artisans-book-jonathan-openshaw/', 'snippet': 'A new book, “Postdigital Artisans,” explores the influence of digital technology in creative fields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In creative industries where ancient techniques originally set the standards for greatness, more and more contemporary talents are embracing, instead, digital technology. And it’s the job of people like Jonathan Openshaw, the editor of LS:N Global, developed by the Future Laboratory to help explain market and consumer trends, to keep a finger on the pulse of innovation. In a new book, “Postdigital Artisans” ($39, Frame Publishers), Openshaw explores the otherworldly processes and sensational creations of artists like Daniel Arsham, fashion designers like Iris van Herpen and a host of other up-and-coming talents. In the above slideshow, he shares with T 10 of the tome’s most compelling projects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compelling Works From Some of Today’s Most Innovative Artists and Designers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ALAINNA LEXIE BEDDIE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'BEDDIE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad5cec2d-b2e8-57ec-a668-c8433b6d6022', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad5cec2d-b2e8-57ec-a668-c8433b6d6022'}, {'abstract': 'A new book, “Postdigital Artisans,” explores the influence of digital technology in creative fields.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/postdigital-artisans-book-jonathan-openshaw/', 'snippet': 'A new book, “Postdigital Artisans,” explores the influence of digital technology in creative fields.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In creative industries where ancient techniques originally set the standards for greatness, more and more contemporary talents are embracing, instead, digital technology. And it’s the job of people like Jonathan Openshaw, the editor of LS:N Global, developed by the Future Laboratory to help explain market and consumer trends, to keep a finger on the pulse of innovation. In a new book, “Postdigital Artisans” ($39, Frame Publishers), Openshaw explores the otherworldly processes and sensational creations of artists like Daniel Arsham, fashion designers like Iris van Herpen and a host of other up-and-coming talents. In the above slideshow, he shares with T 10 of the tome’s most compelling projects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compelling Works From Some of Today’s Most Innovative Artists and Designers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be0e757f-651f-58ac-8b42-9d9cc040f8b9', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be0e757f-651f-58ac-8b42-9d9cc040f8b9'}, {'abstract': 'The artist recently wrapped up a 10-day tour of Capri, Rome, Florence and Venice, and shared photographic highlights of her trip with T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/mickalene-thomas-italy-travel-diary/', 'snippet': 'The artist recently wrapped up a 10-day tour of Capri, Rome, Florence and Venice, and shared photographic highlights of her trip with T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, the artist Mickalene Thomas returned home to Brooklyn after a trip to Italy spanning 10 days and four cities, organized around her participation in a conference, “Black Portraiture{s} II,” put on by NYU in Florence. “Since it was going to be my first time in Italy, and since the conference coincided with the Venice Biennale, it seemed like a great time for me to travel all over Italy and see what was happening in the art world in what, to a New Yorker, can feel like a different part of the universe,” she says. “There was all sorts of buzz around the Biennale, and I wanted to experience firsthand all of the things I’d been hearing about Italy for years: the architecture, the food, the people, the energy, the language. I got a taste of all of that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mickalene Thomas’s Adventures in Italy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ALEXANDRIA SYMONDS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SYMONDS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad8f15d-9c65-560c-8eae-62a01acd6f93', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad8f15d-9c65-560c-8eae-62a01acd6f93'}, {'abstract': 'The artist recently wrapped up a 10-day tour of Capri, Rome, Florence and Venice, and shared photographic highlights of her trip with T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/mickalene-thomas-italy-travel-diary/', 'snippet': 'The artist recently wrapped up a 10-day tour of Capri, Rome, Florence and Venice, and shared photographic highlights of her trip with T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, the artist Mickalene Thomas returned home to Brooklyn after a trip to Italy spanning 10 days and four cities, organized around her participation in a conference, “Black Portraiture{s} II,” put on by NYU in Florence. “Since it was going to be my first time in Italy, and since the conference coincided with the Venice Biennale, it seemed like a great time for me to travel all over Italy and see what was happening in the art world in what, to a New Yorker, can feel like a different part of the universe,” she says. “There was all sorts of buzz around the Biennale, and I wanted to experience firsthand all of the things I’d been hearing about Italy for years: the architecture, the food, the people, the energy, the language. I got a taste of all of that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mickalene Thomas’s Adventures in Italy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cronin, Patricia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hajjaj, Hassan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Lyle Ashton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Mickalene', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Capri (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florence (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations',