ph': 'Muse, the arena-filling British band, has topped the Billboard album chart for the first time with its seventh studio release, “Drones” (Helium-3/Warner Bros.), which sold 79,000 copies and 84,000 total album equivalent units, counting downloads and streams, according to Nielsen Music. The group had previously peaked at No. 2 with “The 2nd Law” in 2012.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britannia Rules the Chart Again as Muse Takes No. 1 Spot', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britannia Rules Charts Again With Muse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florence and the Machine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muse (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:35:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1555cdd5-1f66-57c2-be68-79a034bb9676', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1555cdd5-1f66-57c2-be68-79a034bb9676'}, {'abstract': 'Embryo donors and recipients may be happy with their choices, but the larger debate over embryo status remains.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/17/unused-embryos-to-donate-destroy-or-debate/', 'snippet': 'Embryo donors and recipients may be happy with their choices, but the larger debate over embryo status remains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of thousands of frozen embryos — perhaps a million — sit in storage facilities nationwide, preserved in silver tanks of liquid nitrogen. Some belong to individuals and couples who are still trying to conceive, or are preserving the option. But most are leftovers from the successes of the booming assisted-reproduction industry. Families, clinics and the courts face difficult choices about what to do with those embryos — possible lives, without guarantee, unsustainable without aid, and ethically challenging, raising questions about the beginning of life and the definition of family.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/us/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO/MOTHERLODE-EMBRYO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unused Embryos, to Donate, Destroy or Debate', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARTIFICIAL INSEMINATION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d0a7e7-67c4-5b50-a79b-126d2ce4cc02', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d0a7e7-67c4-5b50-a79b-126d2ce4cc02'}, {'abstract': 'Although a judge had hash words in his ruling on the A.I.G. case, don’t expect the government to do anything different in the next financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/business/dealbook/will-aig-decision-affect-the-next-bailout-dont-bet-on-it.html', 'snippet': 'Although a judge had hash words in his ruling on the A.I.G. case, don’t expect the government to do anything different in the next financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge’s tone and harsh words in his ruling this week related to the taxpayer bailout of the American International Group seems to have put the government on notice that its tactics in rescuing the insurer during the 2008 financial crisis were improper and illegal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will A.I.G. Decision Affect the Next Bailout? Don’t Bet on It', 'kicker': 'White Collar Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Thomas C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Economic Stabilization Act (2008)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:42:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning and Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0d66bc-8883-5025-aeb2-040b282a8e4e', 'word_count': 1443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0d66bc-8883-5025-aeb2-040b282a8e4e'}, {'abstract': 'Hee Seo and Cory Stearns, who made their debuts as the lovers in 2009, enlarge their performances in Kenneth MacMillan’s interpretation of Shakespeare’s tragedy at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/arts/dance/review-romeo-and-juliet-brings-a-precise-pairing-to-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Hee Seo and Cory Stearns, who made their debuts as the lovers in 2009, enlarge their performances in Kenneth MacMillan’s interpretation of Shakespeare’s tragedy at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Kenneth MacMillan’s enduring 1965 production of “Romeo and Juliet,” there’s a spine-tingling moment in which the heroine sits on the edge of her bed stunned by her fate. She has married Romeo, who has killed her cousin Tybalt, and is engaged — against her will — to Paris, who repulses her a little more every time she sets eyes on him. With her feet propped on point and her shoulders limp, Hee Seo, portraying Juliet at American Ballet Theater on Monday, looked like an animal, both haunted and hunted. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1327, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18SEMINOVA/18SEMINOVA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Romeo and Juliet’ Brings a Precise Pairing to the Met', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Precise Pairing of Tragic Couple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seo, Hee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stearns, Cory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf81e3b-24af-5238-938d-811852c4dcca', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf81e3b-24af-5238-938d-811852c4dcca'}, {'abstract': 'This classic Wagner opera is part of the 17th season of this festival in the English countryside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/arts/music/review-tristan-und-isolde-brings-thunder-to-the-longborough-festival.html', 'snippet': 'This classic Wagner opera is part of the 17th season of this festival in the English countryside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONGBOROUGH, England — A king, Marke, damns the treachery of his adopted son. A knight, Tristan, fights his betrayer, impaling himself on his assailant’s sword. His young lover, Isolde, rushes toward him, hoping he has not yet died the death she knows will come. An orchestra seethes. The stage goes black.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18LONGBOROUGH/18LONGBOROUGH-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Tristan und Isolde’ Brings Thunder to the Longborough Festival', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Imbuing a Countryside Festival With Classic Wagnerian Thunder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tristan und Isolde (Opera)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-17T20:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc3b14d7-5bd2-5b2a-9b03-115c07151b2d', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc3b14d7-5bd2-5b2a-9b03-115c07151b2d'}, {'abstract': 'Performing with the pianist Uri Caine at the Stone, Mr. Bleckmann spliced the cycle with twangs, a yodel, electronic effects and nonsense words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/arts/music/review-theo-bleckmann-upends-a-schumann-song-cycle.html', 'snippet': 'Performing with the pianist Uri Caine at the Stone, Mr. Bleckmann spliced the cycle with twangs, a yodel, electronic effects and nonsense words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s usually not a good sign if a singer starts sounding like Elvis during a performance of Schumann’s “Dichterliebe” (“A Poet’s Love”). But then there was nothing predictable about Theo Bleckmann’s whimsical interpretation of the song cycle on Tuesday at the Stone, where he is in residence this week.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18BLECKMANN/18BLECKMANN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/arts/18BLECKMANN/18BLECKMANN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi