'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fdefe50-8f2d-5561-87e9-e46b8ee2a579', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fdefe50-8f2d-5561-87e9-e46b8ee2a579'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. has fallen behind its goal of training 24,000 Iraqi security forces by this fall, having only trained 9,000 so far.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/world/middleeast/plan-to-train-iraqi-soldiers-is-hampered-by-lack-of-recruits-defense-chief-says.html', 'snippet': 'The U.S. has fallen behind its goal of training 24,000 Iraqi security forces by this fall, having only trained 9,000 so far.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States has fallen behind its goal of training 24,000 members of Iraqi security forces by this fall because the Iraqi government has not provided enough troops to train, Defense Secretary Ashton B. Carter said Wednesday. Mr. Carter told the House Armed Services Committee that the United States military had trained only 9,000 Iraqis so far. “Our training efforts in Iraq have thus far been slowed by a lack of trainees,” Mr. Carter said. “We simply haven’t received enough recruits.” Last week the White House said the United States was adding another training site in Iraq, near Ramadi, where some 450 American troops would train Iraqi fighters, particularly Sunni tribesmen, in the war against the Islamic State group. Defense officials said the effort to train Syrian fighters to take on the militant group on the Syrian side of the border was also going slowly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan to Train Iraqi Soldiers Is Hampered by Lack of Recruits, Defense Chief Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Washington; Plan to Train Iraqi Soldiers Is Hampered by Lack of Recruits, Defense Chief Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Armed Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0a8a3c5-9843-5c38-bd65-4c5e09f81eec', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0a8a3c5-9843-5c38-bd65-4c5e09f81eec'}, {'abstract': 'In closing arguments in Manhattan, prosecutors and defense lawyers both used the wording of the felony burglary law to try to prove their cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/nyregion/case-of-world-trade-center-parachutists-goes-to-jury.html', 'snippet': 'In closing arguments in Manhattan, prosecutors and defense lawyers both used the wording of the felony burglary law to try to prove their cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As sky divers and parachute jumpers, James Brady, Marko Markovich and Andrew Rossig have exposed themselves for years to potential peril.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Case of World Trade Center Parachutists Goes to Jury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jurors Begin Deliberating Case of 3 Trade Center Parachutists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remnick, Noah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parachutes and Parachute Jumping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, James (1981- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markovich, Marko (1986- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossig, Andrew (1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:26:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Remnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Remnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b182c9a-6a02-5a49-8148-bc7fb41a1b87', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b182c9a-6a02-5a49-8148-bc7fb41a1b87'}, {'abstract': 'War crimes investigators in Serbia want to hold Former Prime Minister Ramush Haradinaj accountable for the killings of Serbs while he was a commander of Western-backed insurgents in the late 1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/world/europe/kosovo-slovenia-detains-ex-premier.html', 'snippet': 'War crimes investigators in Serbia want to hold Former Prime Minister Ramush Haradinaj accountable for the killings of Serbs while he was a commander of Western-backed insurgents in the late 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Former Prime Minister Ramush Haradinaj of Kosovo was detained in a surprise move on Wednesday at an airport in Slovenia, where the police said they had acted on a warrant from Serbia. War crimes investigators in Serbia want to hold him accountable for the killings of Serbs while he was a commander of Western-backed insurgents in the late 1990s. In 2004 he was indicted on war crimes charges by the United Nations tribunal for Yugoslavia. But he was acquitted after two trials that were hampered by witness intimidation. Mr. Haradinaj now leads a political party in Kosovo, where many see him as a war hero. He said his arrest was evidently a “mess-up,” because for several years he had traveled widely without problem. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kosovo: Slovenia Detains Ex-Premier', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe; Kosovo: Slovenia Detains Ex-Premier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Marlise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haradinaj, Ramush', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Slovenia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yugoslavia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c864a706-f4a2-56cc-9a56-333d4bcaf378', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c864a706-f4a2-56cc-9a56-333d4bcaf378'}, {'abstract': 'Huge steel girders were lifted into place near the bridge’s Rockland County side; dozens more will be added before the bridge can be open to traffic at the end of 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/nyregion/first-horizontal-piece-is-placed-along-the-new-tappan-zee-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'Huge steel girders were lifted into place near the bridge’s Rockland County side; dozens more will be added before the bridge can be open to traffic at the end of 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By definition, a bridge does not become a bridge until it has a horizontal span that leaps over water or land. On Wednesday, after months in which dozens of verticals — piles, piers and columns — have gradually been poking out of the Hudson River, the replacement for the aging Tappan Zee received its first horizontal structure and finally became a bridge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPENZEE-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPENZEE-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPENZEE-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPENZEE-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1408, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPANZEE-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPANZEE-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/nyregion/18TAPPANZEE-web/18TAPPANZEE-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Horizontal Piece Is Placed Along the New Tappan Zee Bridge', 'kicker': '21st-Century Span', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rising Up, Tappan Zee Also Starts to Fill Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tappan Zee Bridge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derricks and Cranes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Thruway Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaa93a44-8664-5e69-9dcd-08f96db8ebcc', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaa93a44-8664-5e69-9dcd-08f96db8ebcc'}, {'abstract': 'The Wayne County executive, Warren C. Evans, is asking the state to declare a financial emergency to help shore up the struggling fiscal picture for the county, the state’s most populous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/us/michigan-largest-county-seeks-emergency-status.html', 'snippet': 'The Wayne County executive, Warren C. Evans, is asking the state to declare a financial emergency to help shore up the struggling fiscal picture for the county, the state’s most populous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Wayne County executive, Warren C. Evans, is asking the state to declare a financial emergency to help shore up the struggling fiscal picture for the county, the state’s most populous. Mr. Evans described deficits over a matter of years in the county’s general fund and an underfunded pension system as among the chief problems. If state officials agree to designate the county in an emergency, several outcomes are possible, including the installation of an emergency manager. Detroit, which is in Wayne County, was determined to be in a financial emergency before it sought federal bankruptcy protection, which it emerged from last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Largest County Seeks Emergency Status ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Largest County Seeks Emergency Status ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T01:49:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d9424f4-e3e3-5679-bc1f-2ebb0b1d0dea', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article