cle/12ccc5e3-313c-59e8-8311-747788317e8c', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12ccc5e3-313c-59e8-8311-747788317e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Two proposals would crack down on nongovernmental organizations and enforce controls over ideology and culture, all in the name of national security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/opinion/western-business-stands-up-to-china.html', 'snippet': 'Two proposals would crack down on nongovernmental organizations and enforce controls over ideology and culture, all in the name of national security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While international human rights groups often protest China’s attempts to restrict freedoms of its people, foreign businesses, with profits on the line, have traditionally been less willing to do so. But now, many have joined Western governments in opposing Beijing’s latest plan to impose new controls on foreign organizations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/opinion/18thu3web/18thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/opinion/18thu3web/18thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/opinion/18thu3web/18thu3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/opinion/18thu3web/18thu3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/opinion/18thu3web/18thu3web-thumbStandard