orce-of-nature/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street Loses ‘A Force of Nature’ | Fitbit Valued at $4.1 Billion Before Trading Debut | Greek Exit From Euro Appears More Likely | 6 Banks Face New Limits on Mortgage Operations', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALL STREET LOSES ‘A FORCE OF NATURE’  | With the death of James B. Lee Jr. on Wednesday, Wall Street lost one of its most colorful and influential deal makers,  Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in DealBook. Mr. Lee, a vice chairman of JPMorgan Chase, was an early pioneer of syndicated loans and played a key role in the world of leveraged buyouts and private equity, financing deals for Henry Kravis of Kohlberg Kravis Roberts, Stephen A. Schwarzman of the Blackstone Group and the late Theodore J. Forstmann of Fortsmann Little. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Wall Street Loses ‘A Force of Nature’', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or