A.J. Warneford, British hero aviator dies in an accident.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/1915-british-hero-dies-in-accident/', 'snippet': 'From the Archives of the International Herald Tribune: 1915: R.A.J. Warneford, British hero aviator dies in an accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flight Sub-Lieutenant R.A.J. Warneford, the gallant young British aviator who ten days ago destroyed a Zeppelin airship single-handed and returned safely to the British lines, to be rewarded with the Victoria Cross and the Cross of the Legion of Honor, is dead — killed by a fall while making a trial flight on a new machine at the Buc aerodrome near Paris. The tragic accident, which has cut short a career of great promise and robbed England of the valued servant who first pricked the Zeppelin’s bubble reputation of invulnerability to aeroplane attack, occurred at five o’clock on Thursday afternoon. — The New York Herald, European Edition, June 19, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/blogs/20IHT-retrospective-warneford/20IHT-retrospective-warneford-jumbo.png', 'height': 563, 'width': 499, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/blogs/20IHT-retrospective-warneford/20IHT-retrospective-warneford-superJumbo.png', 'height': 563, 'width': 499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/blogs/20IHT-retrospective-warneford/20IHT-retrospective-warneford-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/20/blogs/20IHT-retrospective-warneford/20IHT-retrospective-warneford-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/blogs/20IHT-retrospective-warneford/20IHT-retrospective-warneford-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1915: British Hero Dies In Accident', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T14:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaad99b2-7612-5a8c-aaa5-90b6fef38063', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaad99b2-7612-5a8c-aaa5-90b6fef38063'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone beware, but especially the creditors.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/thinking-about-the-all-too-thinkable/', 'snippet': 'Everyone beware, but especially the creditors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The path toward non-Grexit — toward Greece and its creditors reaching a deal that keeps it in the euro — is getting narrower, although it’s not yet completely closed. I’ve been reticent on the subject, for fear of adding my bit to the crisis atmosphere, and I still intend to keep it cool. But there are a few things that seem to need saying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinking About the All Too Thinkable', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T14:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c061adbb-fdcc-56cb-a840-87b06c072761', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c061adbb-fdcc-56cb-a840-87b06c072761'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone beware, but especially the creditors.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/thinking-about-the-all-too-thinkable/', 'snippet': 'Everyone beware, but especially the creditors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The path toward non-Grexit — toward Greece and its creditors reaching a deal that keeps it in the euro — is getting narrower, although it’s not yet completely closed. I’ve been reticent on the subject, for fear of adding my bit to the crisis atmosphere, and I still intend to keep it cool. But there are a few things that seem to need saying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinking About the All Too Thinkable', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T14:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By PAUL KRUGMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRUGMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea95aac7-0bfd-5f7c-8384-ee87c1779143', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea95aac7-0bfd-5f7c-8384-ee87c1779143'}, {'abstract': 'Reductions at The Wall Street Journal eliminated reporting teams and some international bureaus, though the editor said jobs would be added in other areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/business/media/dow-jones-begins-new-round-of-layoffs.html', 'snippet': 'Reductions at The Wall Street Journal eliminated reporting teams and some international bureaus, though the editor said jobs would be added in other areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dow Jones, the parent company of The Wall Street Journal, began a sweeping round of job cuts on Thursday, including eliminating entire teams of reporters and closing international bureaus.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dow Jones Begins New Round of Layoffs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wall St. Journal Cuts Jobs and Closes Some Bureaus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dow Jones & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T14:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a75a073e-325a-57df-99da-7594dc290f96', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a75a073e-325a-57df-99da-7594dc290f96'}, {'abstr