, has signed a new four-year contract to remain chairwoman, president and editor in chief of the publication, ending speculation that she might leave now that its parent company, AOL, was acquired by Verizon.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19huffpo-web/19huffpo-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arianna Huffington Renews Contract for Four Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Huffington Gets New Deal to Lead Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huffington Post', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huffington, Arianna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T16:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ad5a91-1b7f-5938-ac9b-8b96fa4c3873', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ad5a91-1b7f-5938-ac9b-8b96fa4c3873'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: 1940: Hitler and Mussolini meet in Munich', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/1940-hitler-and-mussolini-meet-in-munich/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: 1940: Hitler and Mussolini meet in Munich', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the midst of Nazi military pomp, Fuehrer Adolf Hitler and his eleventh-hour ally Premier Mussolini met today [June 15] in Munich where on Sept. 19, 1938, ‘‘peace in our time’’ was arranged through the partitioning of Czecho-Slovakia. In a four-hour conference, they agreed ‘‘on the attitude to be assumed’’ by the German and Italian governments ‘‘towards the French requests for an armistice.’’ Traveling presumably in opposite directions, the two dictators left Munich soon after their meeting ended. — New York Herald Tribune, June 19, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'