w.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/business/house-sends-trade-bill-back-to-senate-in-bid-to-outflank-foes.html', 'snippet': 'The vote is part of a strategy to advance prospects for a trans-Pacific accord by uncoupling the measure from a worker-assistance provision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The House on Thursday approved a bill to give President Obama accelerated negotiating authority to pursue a sweeping, legacy-building trade agreement with 11 Pacific Rim nations, Part 1 of a complex legislative strategy devised by Republicans to get a trade package to Mr. Obama’s desk after Democrats derailed the measure in the House last week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1534, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/business/19trade-web/19trade-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House Sends Trade Bill Back to Senate in Bid to Outflank Foes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Sends Trade Bill Back to Senate in Bid to Outflank Foes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T16:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b292e18-133c-53d9-b181-8004adcb08be', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b292e18-133c-53d9-b181-8004adcb08be'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at some of Netil Market’s regulars, who vend items out of sheds, vans and shipping crates.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/saturday-london-netil-market/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at some of Netil Market’s regulars, who vend items out of sheds, vans and shipping crates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of London’s most historic markets, such as Spitalfields, have been swept up in a wave of “regeneration” that leaves niche businesses withering in the wake of big brands. Smithfield, the capital’s 800-year-old meat market is the next (contentiously) earmarked for a facelift. Others, like Borough Market – nowadays more of a gourmet tourist destination than a local amenity — are victims of their own success. Which makes below-the-radar spots like Netil Market, a small community of creative start-ups in London Fields, to the east of the city, such a rarity. This motley assortment of sheds, vans and shipping crates, which sits in the shadow of the London Overground, has a charming, if ramshackle, feel. “There’s a barber, an optician, a jeweler and lots of street food vendors,” says Paul Firmin, a co-founder of the lifestyle boutique and scent brand Earl of East London, which launched on the market last summer. “It’s like a little modern-day High Street.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/t-magazine/18market-farrell-slide-2791/18market-farrell-slide-2791-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/t-magazine/18market-farrell-slide-2791/18market-farrell-slide-2791-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/t-magazine/18market-farrell-slide-2791/18market-farrell-slide-2791-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/t-magazine/18market-farrell-slide-2791/18market-farrell-slide-2791-superJumbo.j