b_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/a-pair-of-kings-will-succeed-ken-watanabe-in-the-king-and-i/', 'snippet': 'Jose Llana and then Hoon Lee will portray the King of Siam opposite Kelli O’Hara in the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ken Watanabe steps down from his role as the King of Siam in the Tony-winning revival of “The King and I” in July, he’ll be replaced by Jose Llana, who starred as Filipino President Ferdinand Marcos in the Public Theater’s smash “Here Lies Love.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pair of Kings Will Succeed Ken Watanabe in ‘The King And I’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Kings for Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T19:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANDREW R. CHOW', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'CHOW', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffcc838-8923-5801-94a3-f0d088a73dad', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffcc838-8923-5801-94a3-f0d088a73dad'}, {'abstract': 'Jose Llana and then Hoon Lee will portray the King of Siam opposite Kelli O’Hara in the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical revival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/a-pair-of-kings-will-succeed-ken-watanabe-in-the-king-and-i/', 'snippet': 'Jose Llana and then Hoon Lee will portray the King of Siam opposite Kelli O’Hara in the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ken Watanabe steps down from his role as the King of Siam in the Tony-winning revival of “The King and I” in July, he’ll be replaced by Jose Llana, who starred as Filipino President Ferdinand Marcos in the Public Theater’s smash “Here Lies Love.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pair of Kings Will Succeed Ken Watanabe in ‘The King And I’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Kings for Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Hoon (1973- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Llana, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Hara, Kelli", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Ken', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T19:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/253bc5c6-84f3-5c6b-a140-986f05ee93da', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/253bc5c6-84f3-5c6b-a140-986f05ee93da'}, {'abstract': 'The director’s new film, a fictionalized study of the French house music scene, stars Félix de Givry and features Greta Gerwig.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/exclusive-clip-mia-hansen-love-eden/', 'snippet': 'The director’s new film, a fictionalized study of the French house music scene, stars Félix de Givry and features Greta Gerwig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take one glance at the title and premise of “Eden,” a fictionalized study of the French house music scene through the eyes of the up-and-coming D.J./producer Paul (Félix de Givry), and you might be expecting a completely different film. What could have been a hedonistic two-hour rave in the hands of others is instead, with Mia Hansen-Love at the helm, a hungover look at the morning after the party. The 33-year-old director, who’s built her career on tackling pain — loss, depression, suicide — had a major advantage when approaching the golden era of electronic music in France: she, and her co-writer and brother, Sven, lived through it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Exclusive Clip From Mia Hansen-Love’s ‘Eden’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T19:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARISSA G. MULLER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marissa', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'MULLER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da932164-0f23-5139-9664-f3af38b9cdac', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da932164-0f23-5139-9664-f3af38b9cdac'}, {'abstract': 'The director’s new film, a fictionalized study of the French house music scene, stars Félix de Givry and features Greta Gerwig.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/exclusive-clip-mia-hansen-love-eden/', 'snippet': 'The director’s new film, a fictionalized study of the French house music scene, stars Félix de Givry and features Greta Gerwig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take one glance at the title and premise of “Eden,” a fictionalized study of the French house music scene through the eyes of the up-and-coming D.J./producer Paul (Félix de Givry), and you might be expecting a completely different film. What could have been a hedonistic two-hour rave in the hands of others is instead, with Mia Hansen-Love at the helm, a hungover look at the morning after the party. The 33-year-old director, who’s built