t', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychics and Psychic Phenomena', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T20:21:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Eric Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': 'Eric', 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c56fb6a-510c-5491-9fca-4fc73007b5b2', 'word_count': 1490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c56fb6a-510c-5491-9fca-4fc73007b5b2'}, {'abstract': 'Though more an entertainer than crooner, Mr. Danza interpreted a Sinatra favorite, “It Was a Very Good Year.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/arts/music/review-tony-danza-at-the-cafe-carlyle-cabaret.html', 'snippet': 'Though more an entertainer than crooner, Mr. Danza interpreted a Sinatra favorite, “It Was a Very Good Year.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in his show “Standards and Stories,” at Café Carlyle on Wednesday, Tony Danza, that talented eternally boyish guy from the neighborhood with the ingenuous grin and cocky attitude, pulled out an obscure ballad, “I Don’t Remember Ever Growing Up,” that hit an unexpectedly poignant note. Its composer, Artie Butler, wrote the music to that inescapable nightclub standard “Here’s to Life,” with lyrics by Phyllis Molinary. “I Don’t Remember Ever Growing Up,” whose narrator has reached an age when “life goes by at twice the speed of light, leaving you with just your memories,” is in the same vein of wistful summing up songs, although not half as good.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19TONYDANZA/19TONYDANZA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Tony Danza at the Café Carlyle Cabaret', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Were Very Good Years, Worth Singing About', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danza, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-18T20:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'origi