locations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T00:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Williams Lessane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Lessane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a044609-53f9-5880-939a-bcfb24de3f28', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a044609-53f9-5880-939a-bcfb24de3f28'}, {'abstract': 'Ten consular officials kidnapped from the Tunisian Consulate in Libya were released overnight after days of negotiations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/world/africa/tunisia-gunmen-free-officials-in-libya.html', 'snippet': 'Ten consular officials kidnapped from the Tunisian Consulate in Libya were released overnight after days of negotiations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Ten consular officials kidnapped from the Tunisian Consulate in Libya were released overnight after days of negotiations, the Tunisian state news agency reported Thursday. The 10 were abducted from their consulate in the Libyan capital, Tripoli, last Friday by armed militiamen. A Tunisian court on Wednesday ruled that Walid Qulaib, a Libyan militia leader detained in Tunisia, would be extradited to Libya. Tunisian news outlets have reported that the kidnapping was carried out by members of a militia group who were demanding the release of Mr. Qulaib. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisia: Gunmen Free Officials in Libya', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; Tunisia: Gunmen Free Officials in Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Carlotta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fajr Libya (Libya Dawn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qulaib, Walid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T00:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Gall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/80001428-e0b7-5dc2-aaeb-aa5124c5302f', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80001428-e0b7-5dc2-aaeb-aa5124c5302f'}, {'abstract': 'Metal gates installed in front of apartment buildings near Columbia University are just one of the tactics the landlord, the Orbach Group, has used in its effort to push out rent-regulated residents, tenants say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/nyregion/longtime-tenants-in-manhattan-see-an-effort-to-push-them-out.html', 'snippet': 'Metal gates installed in front of apartment buildings near Columbia University are just one of the tactics the landlord, the Orbach Group, has used in its effort to push out rent-regulated residents, tenants say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The message was clear to Tommy McCarthy as soon as the sturdy metal gates were installed on his stoop and on those of nearly 20 other buildings along his block in Manhattan south of Columbia University.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'c