t': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ae59a31-99fc-5192-9ddd-486ac981c6f4'}, {'abstract': 'This film, subtitled “Diary of a French Doctor,” unfolds pretty much like an average episode of “ER,” though with more French flag waving and less storeroom romancing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/movies/review-hippocrates-offers-life-death-and-teachable-moments.html', 'snippet': 'This film, subtitled “Diary of a French Doctor,” unfolds pretty much like an average episode of “ER,” though with more French flag waving and less storeroom romancing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lives are lost and saved, vitals checked, brows furrowed, turfs protected and glasses clinked in “Hippocrates: Diary of a French Doctor,” which is more or less what its title announces. There’s also a scene in which most of the characters boogie down, because, as a friend observed, a French movie isn’t a French movie unless it has a scene in a disco or the era’s equivalent. Throw in bureaucratic entanglements and workers uniting — and voilà! ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 734}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1833, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/arts/19HIPPOCRATES/19HIPPOCRATES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Hippocrates’ Offers Life, Death and Teachable Moments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like an Episode of &#8216;ER&#8217; With Less Romance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lilti, Thomas (1976- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hippocrates (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lacoste, Vincent (1993- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T01:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f7c1dc6-519e-576c-9747-fff822f8b84b', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f7c1dc6-519e-576c-9747-fff822f8b84b'}, {'abstract': "To dismiss the shooter as a troubled lone wolf is to disregard centuries of white assaults on the city's black congregants.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/18/magazine/before-charlestons-church-shooting-a-long-history-of-attacks.html', 'snippet': "To dismiss the shooter as a troubled lone wolf is to disregard centuries of white assaults on the city's black congregants.", 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1868, three men assassinated the Rev. Benjamin Randolph in broad daylight as he was boarding a train in Abbeville County, South Carolina. Randolph, a black man, had recently won a seat in the State Senate and was then campaigning for the Republican slate. Having served as an Army chaplain with the 26th Regiment United States Colored Troops, Randolph asked the Freedmen’s Bureau to send him “where he can be most useful to his race.” He settled in South Carolina in time to take part in the 1865 rededication of the Emanuel African Methodist Episcopal Church in Charleston. It was that church’s long history of spiritual autonomy and political activism that caught the attention of the white vigilantes who gunned him down and rode away. Randolph’s fate was repeated yesterday with the murder of nine people, including the pastor of the church, the Rev. Clementa Pinckney, who, like Randolph, also served as a state senator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/magazine/18charleston-promo/18charleston-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/magazine/18charleston-promo/18charleston-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 717}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/magazine/18charleston-promo/18charleston-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/magazine/18charleston-promo/18charleston-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1786, 'width'