team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — The three years R. A. Dickey was a Met, possibly the best three years of his career, Dan Warthen, the Mets’ pitching coach, watched his bullpen sessions with great delight. Dickey was constantly tinkering with his stride, trying to perfect his knuckleball, and he would give Dave Racaniello, the bullpen catcher, fits.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1476, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/sports/CITY-METS-1/CITY-METS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'R. A. Dickey’s Knuckleball Dances as Mets Appear to Sit This One Out', 'kicker': 'Blue Jays 7, Mets 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Dickey&#8217;s Knuckleball Dances, the Mets Sit This One Out ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagares, Juan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T04:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d851fd3-a27e-5f85-8b65-4c55b3d612f0', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d851fd3-a27e-5f85-8b65-4c55b3d612f0'}, {'abstract': 'A state court judge ruled that Benson, whose daughter and her two children had sought to have him declared mentally unfit, had “clarity of thought and volition, despite some memory lapses.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/sports/football/tom-benson-is-found-capable-of-running-saints-and-pelicans.html', 'snippet': 'A state court judge ruled that Benson, whose daughter and her two children had sought to have him declared mentally unfit, had “clarity of thought and volition, despite some memory lapses.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Benson, the owner of the New Orleans Saints and the New Orleans Pelicans, is capable of running the teams, according to a state court judge in Louisiana.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Benson Is Found Capable of Running Saints and Pelicans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Football; Court Win for Saints Owner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Tom (1927- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Pelicans (Basketball)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T04:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aefe7ac2-7cf9-5625-beb0-5dffb4732276', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aefe7ac2-7cf9-5625-beb0-5dffb4732276'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) WHIPLASH (2014) Andrew (Miles Teller), an aspiring jazz drummer at a highly selective Manhattan music school, falls in thrall to Fletcher (J. K. Simmons, in an Oscar-winning portrayal), a charismatic and terrifying instructor whose pedagogical methods include browbeating, humiliation and cymbal throwing. In this second feature from Damien Chazelle, a blood bath, literal and figurative, ensues. “For all its dexterity and assurance, the movie has its share of false notes and rhythmic stumbles,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “A few plot twists test the limits of credibility. And there is something a little dispiriting — if sadly unsurprising — about the way Mr. Chazelle turns a historically African-American art form into the existential arena for a couple of white guys.” Still, he added, “the battle of master and disciple is exciting and terrifying to witness, and, at its best, the film can feel as wild and spontaneous, as risky and precise, as a live jam session.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f35aab01-ac18-5378-b593-5b22cd55998e', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f35aab01-ac18-5378-b593-5b22cd55998e'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, June 19, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/pageoneplus/corrections-june-19-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, June 19, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 19, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T05:50:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of