material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee38e8c7-b1c0-5995-87c3-5dac82db4573', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee38e8c7-b1c0-5995-87c3-5dac82db4573'}, {'abstract': 'The AmeriCorps program, which has bolstered the ranks of many nonprofit groups, is well worth protecting from proposed cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/opinion/more-community-service-not-less.html', 'snippet': 'The AmeriCorps program, which has bolstered the ranks of many nonprofit groups, is well worth protecting from proposed cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be hardhearted and counterproductive to squeeze any more money from the already meager federal funding for public service programs that help struggling schoolchildren, veterans, the elderly and communities stricken by natural disasters. Yet a House subcommittee this week approved a spending bill that cuts federal financing for the already beleaguered Corporation for National and Community Service, which oversees many programs, the most well known of which is AmeriCorps.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri2web/19fri2web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Community Service, Not Less', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Community Service, Not Less', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corp for National and Community Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICORPS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e428579-bbf4-5dab-94fb-0bded8f89177', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e428579-bbf4-5dab-94fb-0bded8f89177'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Francis’ encyclical packed an unexpectedly authoritative and confident punch, especially on global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/opinion/the-pope-and-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis’ encyclical packed an unexpectedly authoritative and confident punch, especially on global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The issue of climate change — unlike, say, the economy — may not be a matter of everyday concern to many Americans or most citizens of the planet. The debate is too often clouded by ideology and well-financed attempts to sow doubt about the underlying science. Even among those aware enough to worry, the long-term consequences can seem remote. As one futile international conference after another has attested, the facts alone have not been enough to move world governments to take decisive action.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 739}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1684, 'width': 1368, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/opinion/19fri1/19fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'