ecline.html', 'snippet': 'Woods, who had a 10-over 80 in the first round of the United States Open, demonstrated how much his game, and demeanor, had changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIVERSITY PLACE, Wash. — For Tiger Woods, the second round of the United States Open on Friday was not the disaster that Thursday’s first round had been. He shot a six-over-par 76, which was a four-stroke improvement from the day before, when he endured his worst round ever at the Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1523, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penningtonweb-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20penningtonweb-03/20penn