ameron, who has said he will not lead his party into the next general election in 2020.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/23/opinion/DAncona-new/DAncona-new-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Osborne’s Discreet Ambition', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tory’s discreet ambition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Boris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T09:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By Matthew d'Ancona", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/92bfbe5e-ec1a-5e69-9ea7-150d836c9106', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92bfbe5e-ec1a-5e69-9ea7-150d836c9106'}, {'abstract': 'Protecting the environment is part of our human obligation, and a way of expressing one’s faith.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/opinion/climate-change-and-moral-responsibility.html', 'snippet': 'Protecting the environment is part of our human obligation, and a way of expressing one’s faith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, the British medical journal The Lancet will publish a landmark report highlighting the inalienable and undeniable link between climate change and human health. We warmly welcome the report’s message of hope, which confirms the fact that climate change is more than just a technical or financial challenge (as Pope Francis did in his encyclical letter on June 18) and confirms the voice of health in the discussion on climate change. Indeed, the central premise of the Lancet commission’s work is that tackling climate change could be the single greatest health opportunity of the 21st century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Change and Moral Responsibility', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Climate Change and Responsibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T09:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By  Bartholomew and Justin Welby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bartholomew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Welby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/abd0b8cd-3365-5262-b68d-d2aa6aff138a', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abd0b8cd-3365-5262-b68d-d2aa6aff138a'}, {'abstract': 'What you need to know if you’re on a trip or planning one soon, including a restored amusement park in England and buoyant accommodations for Grateful Dead fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/travel/fridays-travel-news-and-tips.html', 'snippet': 'What you need to know if you’re on a trip or planning one soon, including a restored amusement park in England and buoyant accommodations for Grateful Dead fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our weekday morning digest that includes consumer news, deals, tips and anything else that travelers may want to know.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/travel/19intransitphoto-boat/19intransitphoto-boat-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/travel/19intransitphoto-boat/19intransitphoto-boat-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, '