ncy Meeting on Greece Set for Monday | Martha Stewart Said to Be Close to Selling Empire | Rough Week for Chinese Stock Markets | Strong Trading Debut for Fitbit', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/morning-agenda-emergency-meeting-on-greece-set-for-monday/', 'snippet': 'Emergency Meeting on Greece Set for Monday | Martha Stewart Said to Be Close to Selling Empire | Rough Week for Chinese Stock Markets | Strong Trading Debut for Fitbit', 'lead_paragraph': 'EMERGENCY MEETING ON GREECE SET FOR MONDAY | European leaders called an emergency summit meeting for Monday after a meeting of eurozone finance ministers ended on Thursday without a deal on Greece’s bailout,  James Kanter writes in The New York Times. “Too little progress has been made,” Jeroen Dijsselbloem, the head of the Eurogroup of finance ministers, said at a joint news conference on Thursday with Christine Lagarde, the managing director of the International Monetary Fund, and Pierre Moscovici, the European commissioner for financial affairs. “No agreement as yet is in sight,” said Mr. Dijsselbloem. There was still a chance to reach a deal, he said, though “very little time remains.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Emergency Meeting on Greece Set for Monday', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregula