 'lead_paragraph': 'In what may be the ultimate example of fashion high-low thinking, Anya Hindmarch, the British luxury handbag maker, is about to unveil a new incarnation of her signature “Walkers Crisps” bag — the evening purse in the shape of a crumpled bag of potato chips that became really famous when Solange Knowles used one to attack her brother-in-law, Jay Z, while in an elevator after the 2014 Met Gala. The bag will be offered in 18-karat yellow gold, as well as in white gold and rose gold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1013}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 607, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1214, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/fashion/20OTR-B/20OTR-B-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge