ier never finished his pastoral chamber opera “La Descente d’Orphée aux Enfers” (1685-86).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 1675, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21CHARPENTIER/21CHARPENTIER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Boston Early Music Festival Celebrates Charpentier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Want a Happy Story? Just Ignore the Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Early Music Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charpentier, Marc Antoine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T16:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16f992fc-b689-5572-8711-28bed2c9b24c', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16f992fc-b689-5572-8711-28bed2c9b24c'}, {'abstract': 'A highlight promises to be the afternoon set by the Bang on a Can All-Stars with music by the Pulitzer Prize-winner Julia Wolfe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/21/arts/music/bang-on-a-can-marathon-and-make-music-new-york-for-fathers-day.html', 'snippet': 'A highlight promises to be the afternoon set by the Bang on a Can All-Stars with music by the Pulitzer Prize-winner Julia Wolfe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ties? Socks? Forget the tired old Father’s Day staples and celebrate Dad with music this year. It’s never been easier (or cheaper): Sunday brings both the Bang on a Can Marathon to the newly spiffy Brookfield Place (now featuring one of the city’s best food courts) and a swarm of more than 1,000 live performances across town as part of Make Music New York. Yes, all free.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21GUIDE6/21GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/21/arts/21GUIDE6/21GUIDE