Jones’s mother-in-law during World War II, at Montclair State University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTCLAIR, N.J. — At the start of World War II, Dora Amelan, a Jewish girl of 19, was living in Belgium. At the end of the war, she was still alive, though much of her family was not. The story of her survival is, in her telling, a story of luck but also of choices. That she spent much of the war in France helping others in internment camps and saving children did not save her from the kind of moral dilemmas that remain insoluble through a lifetime of remembering.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 1687, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/arts/ANALOGY/ANALOGY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'h