800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8f54914-7c6f-5e4e-81c1-f62853dc3883'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Rodriguez became the latest player to reach 3,000 hits. His home runs make up 22 percent of those hits, a higher percentage than any other player on the list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/06/19/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart.html', 'snippet': 'Alex Rodriguez became the latest player to reach 3,000 hits. His home runs make up 22 percent of those hits, a higher percentage than any other player on the list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Rodriguez became the latest player to reach 3,000 hits. His home runs make up 22 percent of those hits, a higher percentage than any other player on the list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 997, 'width': 1502, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/18/sports/baseball/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458/ARod-3000-chart-1434648156458-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Rodriguez, the Most Powerful in the 3,000-Hit Club', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T23:37:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/26995023-7a59-598a-8eb1-58fc62ecd23e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/26995023-7a59-598a-8eb1-58fc62ecd23e'}, {'abstract': 'The standards, which have been adopted by more than 40 states, mandated many changes to traditional teaching, but one of the most basic was a call for students to read more nonfiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/nyregion/english-class-in-common-core-era-nonfiction-joins-the-classics.html', 'snippet': 'The standards, which have been adopted by more than 40 states, mandated many changes to traditional teaching, but one of the most basic was a call for students to read more nonfiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Harrison, N.Y., 10th graders read articles about bipolar disorder and the adolescent brain to help them analyze Holden Caulfield. In Springdale, Ark., ninth graders studying excerpts from “The Odyssey” also read sections of the G.I. Bill of Rights, and a congressional resolution on its 60th anniversary, to connect the story of Odysseus to the challenges of modern-day veterans. After eighth graders in Naples, Fla., read how Tom Sawyer duped other boys into whitewashing a fence for him, they follow it with an op-ed article on teenage unemployment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/17/nyregion/COMMONCOREweb1/COMMONCOREweb1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'ma