artment (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosekind,  Mark R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scovel, Calvin L III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T23:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a768c6e-8eae-51af-a4ab-eaa3fbf9f2a4', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a768c6e-8eae-51af-a4ab-eaa3fbf9f2a4'}, {'abstract': 'Something special and new.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/19/friday-night-music-pavo-pavo/', 'snippet': 'Something special and new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I went to see Lucius at Celebrating Brooklyn on Saturday; for those who asked for a link, someone took quite good videos here and here. But let me feature the first opening act, a new band named Pavo Pavo. It was great to be part of the audience, most of whom, like me, didn’t know the band at all; little by little everyone began to realize that we were experiencing something special, that these very young musicians definitely have the magic:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Pavo Pavo', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-19T23:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e91823c9-b83d-57a1-857b-a1c255bfa240', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e91823c9-b83d-57a1-857b-a1c255bfa240'}, {'abstract': 'The death was the first linked to Takata’s airbags involving a rental car, and it underscored the holes in safety regulations for used or rental cars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/business/airbag-death-in-honda-rental-car-reveals-a-gap.html', 'snippet': 'The death was the first linked to Takata’s airbags involving a rental car, and it underscored the holes in safety regulations for used or rental cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honda Motor confirmed on Friday that an airbag rupture killed the driver of a rented 2001 Civic in September 2014, making it the eighth death linked to faulty airbags made by the Japanese supplier Takata. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Airbag Death in Honda Rental Car Reveals a Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airbag Death in Rental Car Reveals a Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tabuchi, Hiroko (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takata Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liability for Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 9, 'majo