ives and Records Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Morning News', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADDINGTON, DAVID S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T00:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27674f1c-912a-5e35-8a0f-20d178a0b6b6', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27674f1c-912a-5e35-8a0f-20d178a0b6b6'}, {'abstract': 'The French foreign minister will travel to the Middle East for meetings that the government asserts will be an effort to restart peace negotiations between Israel and the Palestinians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/world/europe/france-mideast-peace-on-agenda.html', 'snippet': 'The French foreign minister will travel to the Middle East for meetings that the government asserts will be an effort to restart peace negotiations between Israel and the Palestinians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French foreign minister, Laurent Fabius, will travel this weekend to Egypt, Jordan, Israel and the West Bank for meetings that the government asserts will be an effort to restart peace negotiations between Israel and the Palestinians. Although the French are not talking publicly about it, the other pressing issue for Mr. Fabius is the proposed nuclear deal with Iran. Talks between Iran and its negotiating partners over Iran’s nuclear program are set to finish by the end of June. In Jordan, Mr. Fabius will meet with his Jordanian counterpart as well as with King Abdullah II. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Mideast Peace on Agenda', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe; France: Mideast Peace on Agenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Alissa Johannsen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T00:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2357ffc7-2b0f-5a17-8481-05a48ba5fa71', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2357ffc7-2b0f-5a17-8481-05a48ba5fa71'}, {'abstract': 'The former governor of the northeast Mexican border state of Tamaulipas has been indicted on money-laundering charges in South Texas, prosecutors said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/world/americas/mexico-ex-governor-charged.html', 'snippet': 'The former governor of the northeast Mexican border state of Tamaulipas has been indicted on money-laundering charges in South Texas, prosecutors said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The former governor of the northeast Mexican border state of Tamaulipas, Eugenio Hernández Flores, has been indicted on money-laundering charges in \xa0South Texas, prosecutors said Friday. The charges stem from allegations by United States law enforcement\xa0agencies that Mr. Hernández had received bribes from the Zetas drug gang to allow it to operate freely in Tamaulipas while he was governor from 2005 to 2010. Mr. Hernández, 57, is a fugitive but he called in to a Mexican radio show on Friday to declare his innocence. The governor preceding him, Tomás Yarrington, also faces money-laundering and drug-trafficking charges. He, too, remains a fugitive.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Ex-Governor Charged', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Americas; Mexico: Ex-Governor Charged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez Flores, Eugenio (1959- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamaulipas (Mexico)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T00:50:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0469c29-6357-5ae9-a4b5-8b495073751c', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://ar