s genome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After tracking tiny mutations in the genome of Ebola, scientists from around the world are developing a fuller picture of how the virus spread and evolved genetically during the world’s worst outbreak of the disease.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genome Studies Show How Ebola Spread Initially ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genome Studies Show How Ebola Spread Initially ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fink, Sheri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T00:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheri Fink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56ead1b6-d05a-527f-861f-3c8500118bbb', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56ead1b6-d05a-527f-861f-3c8500118bbb'}, {'abstract': 'The expected mass deportation of Haitian immigrants in the Dominican Republic failed to materialize in the two days after the government’s deadline for them to normalize their status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/world/americas/dominican-deadline-passes-without-ma