east for a while. The best starting pitcher for the Mets this season, deGrom took a two-hit shutout into the bottom of the eighth inning, when he was undermined by some resistance by the host Atlanta Braves and some shaky defense from his own work-in-progress infield in a 2-1 loss.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/20/sports/20BASE/20BASE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jacob deGrom Takes Shutout of Braves Into Eighth Before the Mets Fold', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DeGrom Takes Shutout of Braves Into Eighth Before the Mets Fold ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schreiber, Jay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'deGrom, Jacob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T04:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d99f005f-31db-526b-923b-f37a4f4d338d', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d99f005f-31db-526b-923b-f37a4f4d338d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) GONE GIRL (2014) After losing their writing jobs in New York, Nick Dunne (Ben Affleck) and his wife, Amy (Rosamund Pike, in an Oscar-nominated portrayal), move to his small Missouri hometown to attend to his mother after her cancer diagnosis. Then she dies, and so does their marriage. So when Amy goes missing on their fifth wedding anniversary after what looks like a struggle, with broken glass and mopped-up blood, Nick is the prime suspect. And suddenly he and the town are trapped in a nationwide media circus. “At its strongest, ‘Gone Girl’ plays like a queasily, at times gleefully, funny horror movie about a modern marriage, one that has disintegrated partly because of spiraling downward mobility and lost privilege,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about David Fincher’s thriller, adapted from the novel by Gillian Flynn. “Yet, as sometimes happens in Mr. Fincher’s work, dread descends like winter shadows, darkening the movie’s tone and visuals until it’s snuffed out all the light, air and nuance.” By the movie’s second half, she added, “you may wish that Amy would stay gone.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T05:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b84ca4-713c-500e-a488-698a24883f70', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b84ca4-713c-500e-a488-698a24883f70'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, June 20, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/20/pageoneplus/corrections-june-20-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, June 20, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE ARTS', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 20, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-20T05:52:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://arti