us-how-your-church-addressed-the-popes-encyclical.html', 'snippet': 'The Times wants to know how places of worship in the United States and around the world are responding to Francis’ message on the environment and climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The encyclical by Pope Francis released on Thursday did not merely present a papal view on the environment and climate change. It was also an urgent call to action. The document appeared intended to persuade followers around the world to change their behavior, in hopes of protecting a fragile planet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22CHURCHVOICES/22CHURCHVOICES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us How Your Church Addressed the Pope’s Encyclical', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '<b>\xa0</b>', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Encyclicals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-21T13:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b133e9b0-0793-5bd1-aa1a-d4c7504cb586', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b133e9b0-0793-5bd1-aa1a-d4c7504cb586'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the Intentional Herald Tribune: Troops bear down on demonstrators protesting the ouster of President Ahmed Ben Bella in a coup.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/21/1965-army-occupies-algiers/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the Intentional Herald Tribune: Troops bear down on demonstrators protesting the ouster of President Ahmed Ben Bella in a coup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALGIERS — Riot police and troops occupied the center of Algiers tonight after angry youths took to the streets here for the second time in 24 hours to protest the ouster of President Ahmed Ben Bella. The demonstration which broke out this afternoon — despite a government edict banning all mass gatherings — was dispersed after the police and army troops fired shots into the air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Army Occupies Algiers', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None