ically motivated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — An Egyptian-British journalist working for the television news network Al Jazeera remained in German custody on Sunday pending a court ruling on the validity of an Egyptian arrest warrant that served as grounds for his detention at a Berlin airport over the weekend. His lawyers said the charges were politically motivated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1323, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/21/world/europe/22JAZEERA/22JAZEERA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Jazeera Journalist Held in Germany Awaits Verdict on Egyptian Arrest Warrant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germans Hold Jazeera Anchor on Warrant From Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mansour, Ahmed (1962- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eddy, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkpatrick, David D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interpol (International Criminal Police Organization)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-21T16:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f35bb2d-8cb4-5b70-8a79-53570132c754', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f35bb2d-8cb4-5b70-8a79-53570132c754'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/21/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (HBO) TRUE DETECTIVE Three law enforcement officers (Colin Farrell, above; Rachel McAdams; and Taylor Kitsch) in a fictional Los Angeles suburb and a career criminal (Vince Vaughn) trying to go legit collide when a city manager is murdered — and a lucrative land scheme disrupted — in Season 2 of this anthology series, created and written by Nic Pizzolatto. “This time, Mr. Pizzolatto doubles down on much of what made the first season so distinctive,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. “That doesn’t make it twice as good, though. Not nearly.” In the premiere of “Ballers,” at 10, Dwayne Johnson plays a former football pro trying to build a career out of giving financial advice to current players in Miami. The characters’ shenanigans make for “unrewarding, predictable drama, though the writers occasionally try for better,” Neil Genzlinger wrote. And in “The Brink,” a dark comedy at 10:30, the fate of the world rests in the hands of the secretary of state (Tim Robbins), a lowly foreign service officer (Jack Black) and a Navy fighter pilot (Pablo Schreiber) after a rogue general (Iqbal Theba) seizes control of Pakistan and its nuclear arsenal. The writers don’t go very near Islamic extremism or terrorism, Ms. Stanley wrote. “Instead,” she said, “the creators of ‘Brink’ take aim at American wrongdoing. So nobody is going to get in trouble because of this show. But people aren’t going to die laughing, either.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subjec