 sequences. You do the math.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/arts/dance/review-twyla-tharps-the-one-hundreds-math-thats-easy-on-the-eyes.html', 'snippet': 'Twyla Tharp’s “The One Hundreds,” in the River to River Festival, is made up of 11-second sequences. You do the math.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was misty early in the evening on Saturday, and the lawn of Nelson A. Rockefeller Park in Battery Park City was damp as 100 volunteers danced en masse for 11 seconds. This extremely brief burst of activity was the finale of Twyla Tharp’s 1970 work “The One Hundreds.” The duration of the preceding part of the piece could be measured in minutes: about 20. That was less time than I spent waiting for a subway train on my way home afterward. But “The One Hundreds” was well worth the trip. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1208, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22THARP/22THARP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Twyla Tharp’s ‘The One Hundreds’: Math That’s Easy on the Eyes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' In a 50th-Anniversary Year, Tharp Revisits Her Math From 1970 ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tharp, Twyla', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'River to River Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelley, Ramona (Dancer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Daniel (Dancer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-21T21:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/851f0653-5325-5b55-985b-b9c17d37ce01', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/851f0653-5325-5b55-985b-b9c17d37ce01'}, {'abstract': 'The church massacre in Charleston, S.C., gives this documentary extra topicality, but it also underscores the project’s voyeuristic shallowness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/arts/television/review-requiem-for-the-dead-on-hbo-explores-gun-violence-in-america.html', 'snippet': 'The church massacre in Charleston, S.C., gives this documentary extra topicality, but it also underscores the project’s voyeuristic shallowness.