 madcap prose of Mr. Kram, who wrote for Sports Illustrated in the 1960s and ’70s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/books/review-great-men-die-twice-a-collection-of-sports-reporting-by-mark-kram.html', 'snippet': 'This book highlights the energetic, inventive and slightly madcap prose of Mr. Kram, who wrote for Sports Illustrated in the 1960s and ’70s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The list of sportswriters whose career highlights are worth anthologizing is probably finite: Ring Lardner, Red Smith, Roger Angell, add a few others of your own. But one who shouldn’t be forgotten is Mark Kram, and not simply because he may be the greatest writer ever — of sports or anything else — whose name is a palindrome. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 431, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 431, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB/22BOOKKRAMER-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline':