: 'Last week’s run of performances by American Ballet Theater of Kenneth MacMillan’s version of this ballet included three important performances as Juliet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/arts/dance/review-three-romeo-and-juliet-performances-including-julie-kents-farewell.html', 'snippet': 'Last week’s run of performances by American Ballet Theater of Kenneth MacMillan’s version of this ballet included three important performances as Juliet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hail, hail, hail and farewell. Last week’s run of Kenneth MacMillan’s “Romeo and Juliet” by American Ballet Theater included three important performances as Juliet and a distinguished new Romeo. On Thursday evening the Russian ballerina Evgenia Obraztsova made her debut with this company; on Saturday afternoon the company soloists Misty Copeland and Joseph Gorak gave the performance originally planned for their joint debuts as the star-crossed duo (Ms. Copeland had also, on short notice, danced it earlier in the week); and on Saturday evening Julie Kent, Ballet Theater’s longest-serving principal dancer, took her departure from this company. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22ROMEO-REF/22ROMEO-REF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22ROMEO-REF/22ROMEO-REF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22ROMEO-REF/22ROMEO-REF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/arts/22ROMEO-REF/22ROMEO-REF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 13