nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d19ece17-4e27-5417-8207-8d572bffeb88', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d19ece17-4e27-5417-8207-8d572bffeb88'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government attempted to give new life to the idea that yoga can help restore national pride and a return to ancient values could help illness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/world/asia/india-narendra-modi-international-yoga-day.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government attempted to give new life to the idea that yoga can help restore national pride and a return to ancient values could help illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — It was a rare sight — after a brief speech to inaugurate International Yoga Day on Sunday, Prime Minister Narendra Modi descended from a huge stage in front of the presidential palace and took off his glasses and his shoes. He quietly took his place before a sea of schoolchildren and others, mats neatly arranged in a checkerboard as far as the eye could see, to begin what was billed as the largest yoga demonstration in a single venue in history. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22YOGA1/22YOGA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22YOGA1/22YOGA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22YOGA1/22YOGA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/world/22YOGA1/22