swer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is the SWAP instrument aboard the New Horizons spacecraft and how much energy does it use? Try our quiz if you think you know the answer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/science/space/sos-pluto-swap/sos-pluto-swap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/science/space/sos-pluto-swap/sos-pluto-swap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/science/space/sos-pluto-swap/sos-pluto-swap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/14/science/space/sos-pluto-swap/sos-pluto-swap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/science/space/sos-pluto-swap/sos-pluto-swap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s That Science Thing: Pluto Flyby Edition', 'kicker': 'Summer of Science ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-21T22:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/806349f5-7e67-58da-ac87-0bb6ae5a55f5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/806349f5-7e67-58da-ac87-0bb6ae5a55f5'}, {'abstract': 'The interdisciplinary festival, organized by the French Institute Alliance Française, includes several premieres.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/arts/crossing-the-line-festival-announces-2015-lineup.html', 'snippet': 'The interdisciplinary festival, organized by the French Institute Alliance Française, includes several premieres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The interdisciplinary Crossing the Line festival, organized by the French Institute Alliance Française, has announced its 2015 lineup, which includes several premieres. The festival will run from Sept. 10 through Oct. 4 and begin with the United States premiere of “Suite n°2,” a concert by the French artist Joris Lacoste. The British artist Shezad Dawood will delve into the aftereffects of Hurricane Sandy in “It was a time that was a time,” a post-apocalyptic film shot in Far Rockaway, Queens; on Coney Island; and on Staten Island. The film’s world premiere will be on Sept. 11. Other artists from around the world also have premieres planned: The Brazilian artist Gustavo Ciriaco and the Austrian artist Andrea Sonnberger will bind themselves together and walk through Red Hook (Sept. 19-20); the New York choreographer Miguel Gutierrez will dance his way through the past, present and future in “Age & Beauty” (Sept. 16-26); and the French photographers Mazaccio & Drowilal, who repurpose images from popular culture, will have their first New York exhibition, at the French Institute’s gallery. More information is at fiaf.org/ctl.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crossing the Line Festival Announces 2015 Lineup', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crossing the Line Festival Announces 2015 Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Institute/Alliance Francaise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutierrez, Miguel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lacoste, Joris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dawood, Shezad (1974- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ciriaco, Gustavo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sonnberger, Andrea (Artist)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-21T22:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/091ca34d-28c5-5fea-bc02-14122d0545e0', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/091ca34d-28c5-5fea-bc02-14122d0545e0'}, {'abstract': 'Justice Kennedy, the onetime altar boy from Sacramento and conservative Republican, has advanced legal equality for gays more than any other American jurist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/us/kennedys-gay-rights-rulings-seen-in-his-sacramento-roots.html', 'snippet': 'Justice Kennedy, the onetime altar boy from Sacramento and conservative Republican, has advanced legal equality for gays more than any other American jurist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — In the fall of 1987, a package arrived on the desk of Laurence H. Tribe, a Harvard law professor who had just lost a Supreme Court case on gay rights. It contained the legal opinions of Anthony M. Kennedy, a strait-laced, conservative Republican jurist from Sacramento who hardly seemed sympathetic to that cause.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 