ews_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/743a44fc-fe64-5e74-9a2a-a92f758ac1be', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/743a44fc-fe64-5e74-9a2a-a92f758ac1be'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Starz Cinema) THE FRENCH LIEUTENANT’S WOMAN (1981) Meryl Streep earned her third Oscar nomination portraying Anna, an actress whose love affair with a co-star, Mike (Jeremy Irons), mirrors the doomed relationship in 1867 England between Sarah, a lowborn governess, and Charles, a French naval officer, in the film they are making. Harold Pinter also received an Oscar nomination for his screenplay adaptation of John Fowles’s novel, to which he added the parallel story of Anna and Mike. Writing in The New York Times, Vincent Canby called this drama from Karel Reisz “an astonishingly beautiful film.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-22T04:03:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c954ace-71d6-5745-8864-4b60db59636f', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c954ace-71d6-5745-8864-4b60db59636f'}, {'abstract': 'The campaigns of Ted Cruz, Rick Santorum and Rand Paul received donations from the leader of the white supremacist group tied to Dylann Roof, the suspect of the church shooting in Charleston, S.C.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/us/campaign-donations-linked-to-white-supremacist.html', 'snippet': 'The campaigns of Ted Cruz, Rick Santorum and Rand Paul received donations from the leader of the white supremacist group tied to Dylann Roof, the suspect of the church shooting in Charleston, S.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The leader of a white supremacist group that apparently influenced Dylann Roof, the suspect in the killing of nine African-Americans in a Charleston, S.C., church last week, has donated tens of thousands of dollars to Republican campaigns, including those of 2016 presidential contenders such as Ted Cruz, Rick Santorum and Rand Paul, records show.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/us/22donations-1/22donations-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 566, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/us/22donations-1/22donations-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 566, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/us/22donations-1/22donations-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/22/us/22donations-1/22donations-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/22/us/22donations-1/22donations-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'White Supremacist Who Influenced Charleston Suspect Donated to 2016 G.O.P. Campaigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campaign Donations Linked to White Supremacist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holt, Earl III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Conservative Citizens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roof, Dylann Storm', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charleston, SC, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-22T04:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b24cab3c-a5d5-59dc-81c9-b78523b8d414', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'n