e51b683-3abc-59b8-a72c-d6d81dc843f8'}, {'abstract': 'A senior fellow at Rutgers’ School of Criminal Justice responds to a Sunday Review article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/opinion/justice-for-juveniles.html', 'snippet': 'A senior fellow at Rutgers’ School of Criminal Justice responds to a Sunday Review article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice for Juveniles', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice for Juveniles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-22T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8dd35b7-76e2-5fca-910d-0723a11e9173', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8dd35b7-76e2-5fca-910d-0723a11e9173'}, {'abstract': 'Despite changing attitudes on several fronts, race in America is an issue that won’t go away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/opinion/paul-krugman-slaverys-long-shadow.html', 'snippet': 'Despite changing attitudes on several fronts, race in America is an issue that won’t go away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'America is a much less racist nation than it used to be, and I’m not just talking about the still remarkable fact that an African-American occupies the White House. The raw institutional racism that prevailed before the civil rights movement ended Jim Crow is gone, although subtler discrimination persists. Individual attitudes have changed, too, dramatically in some cases. For example, as recently as the 1980s half of Americans opposed interracial marriage, a position now held by only a tiny minority.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page'