_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/2013-and-all-that/', 'snippet': 'Gotcha is the last refuge of failed economists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who can, cite evidence to support their position; those who cannot play gotcha. Events have overwhelmingly supported a Keynesian view of the effects of fiscal policy, but the anti-Keynesians have responded, not by reconsidering their views, but by seeking to discredit the messengers. In particular, there’s a lot of “Krugman said X would happen, and it didn’t, so Keynesian economics is wrong.” And in particular particular, the experience of 2013 – when British growth accelerated, and US growth continued despite the budget sequester, is claimed as some sort of decisive experiment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2013 And All That', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-22T19:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd46ccc0-59da-5bfa-94d8-de4e8c13e32c', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd46ccc0-59da-5bfa-94d8-de4e8c13e32c'}, {'abstract': 'GQ celebrated Jim Moore’s 35th anniversary at the magazine, and Details commemorated the 15-year mark for its editor, Dan Peres. Both were can’t-miss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/22/fashion/mens-style/in-milan-the-mens-fashion-crowd-practices-magazine-diplomacy.html', 'snippet': 'GQ celebrated Jim Moore’s 35th anniversary at the magazine, and Details commemorated the 15-year mark for its editor, Dan Peres. Both were can’t-miss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — In fashion, as Heidi Kl