’s play set a theater record during its final week on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway revival of “Skylight” closed out its Tony-winning run with one more bragging right: the most revenue ever grossed in a single week at the John Golden Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Skylight’ Closes Out Run With Healthy Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Skylight’ Closes Out Run With Healthy Box Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hare, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirren, Helen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulligan, Carey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nighy, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-22T20:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a89f1d5-810b-5b3b-b75b-9795174ff776', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a89f1d5-810b-5b3b-b75b-9795174ff776'}, {'abstract': 'As in his earlier works, an undertow of melancholy tugs at Mr. Swift’s characters in this new collection, with short, dense narratives that unfold into complex meditations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/books/review-graham-swifts-england-and-other-stories-a-darkness-across-time-and-fates.html', 'snippet': 'As in his earlier works, an undertow of melancholy tugs at Mr. Swift’s characters in this new collection, with short, dense narratives that unfold into complex meditations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An undertow of melancholy tugs at Graham Swift’s characters, threatening to pull them under — or at least backward. Time is a Möbius strip in his stories — time present contiguous with a Faulknerian time past and shadowed by secrets the reader only slowly pieces together. This is true of Mr. Swift’s early work, like “Waterland,” and his Booker Prize-winning novel, “Last Orders,” and it’s truer still of his new collection, “England and Other Stories.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 881, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 881}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1396, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWIFT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/arts/23BOOKSWIFT/23BOOKSWI