date': '2015-06-23T04:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68af6086-08d1-5239-9d30-c353998c7a84', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68af6086-08d1-5239-9d30-c353998c7a84'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 A.M. (HBO Signature) LIFE IS BEAUTIFUL (1997) Roberto Benigni, below, directed and stars in this Oscar winner for best foreign language film about an Italian Jew who concocts a ruse involving an elaborate game to protect his son (Giorgio Cantarini) from the realities of a Nazi concentration camp. “Mr. Benigni effectively creates a situation in which comedy is courage,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times. “And he draws from this an unpretentious, enormously likable film that plays with history both seriously and mischievously. Piety has no place here, nor do tears until the final reel. ‘Life Is Beautiful’ plays by its own rules.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T05:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c07ad76-0376-5027-a86b-c1a35dd4209a', 'word_count': 713, 'uri':