r terrible environmental and economic policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/opinion/fracking-and-the-franciscans.html', 'snippet': 'Pope Francis’ new encyclical contains beautiful ideas that would make for terrible environmental and economic policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pope Francis is one of the world’s most inspiring figures. There are passages in his new encyclical on the environment that beautifully place human beings within the seamless garment of life. And yet over all the encyclical is surprisingly disappointing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fracking and the Franciscans', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fracking and the Franciscans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Encyclicals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd6e61c-9d08-50a2-ae2f-e414c29fda88', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd6e61c-9d08-50a2-ae2f-e414c29fda88'}, {'abstract': 'Cuban-Americans and the G.O.P. must look to the future instead of the past. Ordinary Cubans need trade and engagement, not more isolation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/opinion/a-republican-case-for-obamas-cuba-policy.html', 'snippet': 'Cuban-Americans and the G.O.P. must look to the future instead of the past. Ordinary Cubans need trade and engagement, not more isolation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — I WAS born in Havana in November 1953, about six years before Fidel Castro led a revolution in Cuba. In July 1960, my family fled to the United States in search of freedom. Like many Cubans, they left behind close relatives, a business, property and memories. We lost everything.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Republican Case for Obama’s Cuba Policy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Obama’s Right About Cuba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutierrez, Carlos M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cuban-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlos M. Gutierrez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/944a3135-cc40-5f46-940f-f26e0175f0a1', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/944a3135-cc40-5f46-940f-f26e0175f0a1'}, {'abstract': 'It won’t actually buy us more time if Tehran decides to build a bomb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/opinion/the-iran-deals-fatal-flaw.html', 'snippet': 'It won’t actually buy us more time if Tehran decides to build a bomb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA’S main pitch for the pending nuclear deal with Iran is that it would extend the “breakout time” necessary for Iran to produce enough enriched uranium for a nuclear weapon. In a recent interview with NPR, he said that the current breakout time is “about two to three months by our intelligence estimates.” By contrast, he claimed, the pending deal would shrink Iran’s nuclear program, so that if Iran later “decided to break the deal, kick out all the inspectors, break the seals and go for a bomb, we’d have over a year to respond.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Iran Deal’s Fatal Flaw', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Iran Deal’s Fatal Flaw', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuperman, Alan J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan J. Kuperman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Kuperman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/953b0639-f34d-5418-b8c9-f93cf37d2f31', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953b0639-f34d-5418-b8c9-f93cf37d2f31'}, {'abstract': 'Another sampling of the outpouring of reaction to the Charleston tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/opinion/race-guns-a-flag-and-charleston.html', 'snippet': 'Another sampling of the outpouring of reaction to the Charleston