sm with an old sinking feeling: The defeatism that had been dormant since the early 1990s is now knocking at the door again, whispering to us, “Nothing will ever work.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil’s Shaken Optimism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '<b>Brazil’s Shaken Optimism  </b>', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Da Silva, Luiz Inacio Lula', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T10:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antonio Prata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antonio', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8180385b-8c8c-5d82-8e5c-c4ecd43542df', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8180385b-8c8c-5d82-8e5c-c4ecd43542df'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister David Cameron is pushing for an end to a pledge written into European treaties for an “ever closer union.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/europe/cameron-eu-brexit.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister David Cameron is pushing for an end to a pledge written into European treaties for an “ever closer union.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As an agglomeration of about 500 million people who speak at least two dozen tongues, the European Union is no stranger to disputes over language.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015