a and Matthew Blackwell, The Political Legacy of American Slavery. They show a strong relationship, at the county level, between the slave share of the population in 1860 and political attitudes today:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More on Slavery’s Shadow', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T13:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e0df82-7c98-5ac0-aa6a-e30c67c6b663', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e0df82-7c98-5ac0-aa6a-e30c67c6b663'}, {'abstract': 'The crossing on Monday of Nathu La signaled the official opening of a new pilgrimage route for Indians to the holy sites of Mount Kailash and Lake Manasarovar.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/china-opens-new-land-route-to-tibet-for-indian-pilgrims/', 'snippet': 'The crossing on Monday of Nathu La signaled the official opening of a new pilgrimage route for Indians to the holy sites of Mount Kailash and Lake Manasarovar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the high peaks of the Tibetan plateau,\xa0dozens of\xa0Indian pilgrims walked slowly through the sentry post, breathed in the thin air and continued to the town of Yadong, on the side of the rugged border controlled by China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/23/blogs/23sino-tibet3/23sino-tibet3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/23/blog