nd fennel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese City Defends Dog Meat Festival, Despite Scorn', 'kicker': 'Yulin Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City With a Taste for Dog Meat Won&#8217;t Back Down ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qin, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yulin (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slaughterhouses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangxi (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T16:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ce8ad57-4977-533b-9201-3e69a0e27b04', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ce8ad57-4977-533b-9201-3e69a0e27b04'}, {'abstract': 'The smartphone maker said that it sold only 1.1 million phones during its first quarter, a decline of 500,000 from the previous quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/technology/blackberry-q1-earnings.html', 'snippet': 'The smartphone maker said that it sold only 1.1 million phones during its first quarter, a decline of 500,000 from the previous quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — BlackBerry’s introduction of two phones aimed at its traditional base of corporate users failed to 