The Rwandan intelligence chief, Karenzi Karake, is wanted on war crimes charges involving genocide and the killing of Spanish aid workers in the 1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/europe/britain-holds-rwanda-spy-chief-on-spanish-war-crimes-charges.html', 'snippet': 'The Rwandan intelligence chief, Karenzi Karake, is wanted on war crimes charges involving genocide and the killing of Spanish aid workers in the 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The chief of Rwanda’s intelligence service, who is wanted in Spain on war crimes charges, was being held in London on Tuesday after his arrest prompted diplomatic and political protests and reopened debate about responsibility for killings in Rwanda two decades ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Holds Rwandan Spy Chief on War Crimes Warrant from Spain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rwandan Spy Chief Is Held in Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karake, Karenzi (1960- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rwandan Patriotic Front (RPF)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T17:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d563a6a4-a5de-5a43-832f-9b5bb9c3f7b1', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d563a6a4-a5de-5a43-832f-9b5bb9c3f7b1'}, {'abstract': 'New research suggests that a parent’s belief that one sibling is a better student than another can become a self-fulfilling prophecy.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/when-parents-compare-siblings-the-results-can-show-on-report-cards/', 'snippet': 'New research suggests that a parent’s belief that one sibling is a better student than another can become a self-fulfilling prophecy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard for parents of more than one child not to compare them. Our minds like to sort and categorize, and the result is often either labeling (athletic, academic) or ranking (better than, stronger than, more able in one area or another). New research suggests that those thoughts, even if they stay unexpressed, may affect our children’s academic successes. The same research suggests that those parental expectations form early and aren’t affected by changes in a child’s performance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/us/motherlode-parrots/motherlode-parrots-articleLarge.png', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/03/us/motherlode-parrots/motherlode-parrots-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo',