word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/407cc110-e5b8-5519-9162-2614eb784409'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Tess’s dance for the River to River festival invites audience members to move, too, as they follow the performance from space to space on Governors Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/arts/dance/review-souvenir-undone-beckons-its-audience-through-historic-fort-jay.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel Tess’s dance for the River to River festival invites audience members to move, too, as they follow the performance from space to space on Governors Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Tess, a Portland, Ore., choreographer now based in Sweden, is obsessed with relationships between forms: architecture and choreography, silence and sound, light and dark. Ms. Tess, a Juilliard graduate whose scenes resemble dioramas, may have discovered the performance site of her dreams at Governors Island, where, as part of the River to River festival, she presented “Souvenir Undone” on Friday at the Fort Jay magazine, a medley of arched brick rooms once used to store gunpowder.\xa0', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24TESS/24TESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24TESS/24TESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24TESS/24TESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24TESS/24TESS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r