e founder and president of the Fox Residential Group, a boutique brokerage firm that does business mainly in Manhattan and Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ms. Fox is the founder and president of the Fox Residential Group, a boutique brokerage firm that does business mainly in Manhattan and Brooklyn. The firm, which was founded in 1989, has about 50 agents. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1473, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/business/24INTERVIEW/24INTERVIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Barbara S. Fox', 'kicker': 'The 30-Minute Interview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barbara S. Fox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Vivian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Residential Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-23T21:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Marino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/219583b9-31ed-5a0a-80e3-dd50c5a182eb', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/219583b9-31ed-5a0a-80e3-dd50c5a182eb'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary, directed by Liz Garbus, chronicles the life of Nina Simone, the singer-musician whose social circle and civil rights activism grew along with her fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/movies/review-what-happened-miss-simone-documents-nina-simones-rise-as-singer-and-activist.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary, directed by Liz Garbus, chronicles the life of Nina Simone, the singer-musician whose social circle and civil rights activism grew along with her fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Partway through “What Happened, Miss Simone?,” an often electric, bracingly urgent documentary on the singer-musician Nina Simone, we reach that catastrophic year 1968, and the assassination of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. On screen, photographs of other murdered black men flicker past — Malcolm X, the civil rights activist Medgar Evers and the Black Panther Fred Hampton — followed by a photo of a young black mourner holding a sign that reads: “You better kill all blacks.” I can’t be the only American who will despair at the relevance of those words in 2015. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/arts/24WHATHAPPEN/24WHATHAPPEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘What Happened, Miss Simone?’ Documents Nina Simone’s Rise as Singer and Activist', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Voice for the Stage and the Str