 first major changes in 39 years to a law intended to protect people from exposure to toxic chemicals. The House voted. 398 to 1, to pass a bill designed to update and strengthen the 1976 Toxic Substances Control Act, which has been criticized as outdated and toothless by environmental advocates and the chemical industry. The Senate is expected to take up a companion bill next month. The bills would require the Environmental Protection Agency to begin studying the health effects of about 64,000 chemicals that are used in commerce. But public health advocates complain that the pace of study would be too slow. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chemical Safety Bill Advances ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chemical Safety Bill Advances ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemicals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T01:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb84254b-6889-5019-a920-646165bdbd18', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb84254b-6889-5019-a920-646165bdbd18'}, {'abstract': 'A fire Tuesday killed 16 residents of a nursing home on the outskirts of Mexicali, the capital of Baja California, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/americas/mexico-deadly-fire-hits-nursing-home.html', 'snippet': 'A fire Tuesday killed 16 residents of a nursing home on the outskirts of Mexicali, the capital of Baja California, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A fire Tuesday killed 16 residents of a nursing home on the outskirts of Mexicali, the capital of Baja California, officials said. Mayor Jaime Díaz said five people rescued from the home near the California border had been hospitalized. A local charity runs the home, Beautiful Twilight, which houses indigent elderly people. There was no immediate evidence of an electrical fault or gas leak, Mr. Díaz said, and investigators were theorizing that the fire had been intentionally set. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Deadly Fire Hits Nursing Home', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Americas; Mexico: Deadly Fire Hits Nursing Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexicali (Mexico)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T01:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b7e53a-bb79-50f4-a0c8-975afd61e01f', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b7e53a-bb79-50f4-a0c8-975afd61e01f'}, {'abstract': 'The number of Egyptian Jews has dwindled to only a few dozen today, from as many as 85,000 in the middle of the last century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/middleeast/a-timeline-of-jews-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The number of Egyptian Jews has dwindled to only a few dozen today, from as many as 85,000 in the middle of the last century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a timeline of the history of Jews in Egypt, based in part on information provided by Professor Joel Beinin of Stanford University, author of “The Dispersion of Egyptian Jewry.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Timeline of Jews in Egypt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beinin, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T01:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1c16170-e256-5a99-a3f3-08497728bf2e', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1c16170-e256-5a99-a3f3-08497728bf2e'}, {'abstract': 'The return of Ian Livengood and the J.A.S.A. class.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/23/visible-in-melbourne-and-sydney/', 'snippet': 'The return of Ian Livengood and the J.A.S.A. class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — If the FIVE STARS — or asterisks — had been kept as the theme clues, as Ian Livengood says below in his notes, this would have been a much different puzzle. This would have been a tough Thursday or a themed Friday, in my estimation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Visible in Melbourne and Sydney', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T02:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31884457-dadb-52de-89d1-aaf4c24978d7', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31884457-dadb-52de-89d1-aaf4c24978d7'}, {'abstract': 'The unidentified Britons were accused of stealing artifacts, including a razor, buttons and pieces of glass and cutlery, which once belonged to prisoners at the camps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/europe/poland-british-youths-are-charged-with-stealing-from-auschwitz-site.html', 'snippet': 'The unidentified Britons were accused of stealing artifacts, including a razor, buttons and pieces of glass and cutlery, which once belonged to prisoners at the camps.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two British teenagers have been charged with stealing items from the former\xa0Auschwitz-Birkenau\xa0death camps, the spokeswoman for prosecutors in Krakow, Poland, said Tuesday. The unidentified Britons, ages 17 and 18, were arrested Monday during a field trip to the Auschwitz-Birkenau State Museum and accused of stealing artifacts, including a razor, buttons and pieces of glass and cutlery, which once belonged to prisoners at the camps. The maximum sentence for the\xa0theft of items of special cultural importance is 10 years in prison, said Boguslawa Marcinkowska, the spokeswoman. Still, she suggested that more likely penalties for the teenagers, who were released Monday, would include fines, conditionally suspended prison sentences and probation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poland: British Teenagers Are Charged With Stealing From Auschwitz Site', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe; Poland: British Teenagers Are Charged With Stealing From Auschwitz Site', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auschwitz-Birkenau Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concentration Camps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auschwitz Concentration Camp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T02:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Berendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f2f93fb-2593-5105-8f8a-452864abb0f7', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f2f93fb-2593-5105-8f8a-452864abb0f7'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal would l