://interactive/17b7f181-446f-574a-bdab-cfaa8f65f8e9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/17b7f181-446f-574a-bdab-cfaa8f65f8e9'}, {'abstract': 'Gordon Harrison Hull’s “emotional landscapes” will be on display at the Bryce Wolkowitz Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/t-magazine/notes-from-one-artists-interior-monologue.html', 'snippet': 'Gordon Harrison Hull’s “emotional landscapes” will be on display at the Bryce Wolkowitz Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The multidisciplinary artist Gordon Harrison Hull describes his latest works as “emotional landscapes” that map a journey through his psyche; they are collected for an exhibition at the Bryce Wolkowitz Gallery, fittingly dubbed “Department of the Interior.” “The show has smaller, medium-sized and bigger pieces and they all come from a similar place,” he explains, “but the smaller ones are more intimate — they express one particular thought. Then, the medium pieces are an extrapolation of those and the bigger ones really go to town and express a lot of different emotions.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From One Artist’s Interior Monologue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/650f7afb-d39c-5bca-912f-81c77920ea94', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/650f7afb-d39c-5bca-912f-81c77920ea94'}, {'abstract': 'Human Rights Watch says Colombian prosecutors face numerous obstacles in trying to hold high-level officials in the armed forces accountable for killings, in which civilians are presented as armed insurgents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/world/americas/colombia-military-accused-of-deception-on-civilian-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'Human Rights Watch says Colombian prosecutors face numerous obstacles in trying to hold high-level officials in the armed forces accountable for killings, in which civilians are presented as armed insurgents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many generals and other high-ranking officers in Colombia’s armed forces may have known about a pattern of soldiers killing civilians and passing off the deaths as guerrilla casualties in the campaign against rebel insurgencies, according to a report to be released on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colombia Military Accused of Deception on Civilian Deaths', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colombia Military Accused of Deception on Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T04:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34b24837-2cad-5002-9a4f-83307a3e2199', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34b24837-2cad-5002-9a4f-83307a3e2199'}, {'abstract': 'Cami Anderson, in an interview one day after she resigned as schools superintendent, lamented that the fight over education reform had become “personalized.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/nyregion/schools-chief-in-newark-says-debate-lost-its-focus.html', 'snippet': 'Cami Anderson, in an interview one day after she resigned as schools superintendent, lamented that the fight over education reform had become “personalized.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cami Anderson knew the challenges when she arrived in Newark as its schools superintendent four years ago. In the city’s South Ward, for example, there were 12 elementary schools and not at a single one were more than 30 percent of students reading at or above grade level. Students were fleeing to charter schools, taking money from the traditional public schools with them. She had been warned that the city’s politics could be contentious, with a tradition of long and rancorous public meetings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/nyregion/24NEWARK/24NEWARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/nyregion/24NEWARK/24NEWARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/nyregion/24NEWARK/24NEWARK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/nyregion/24NEWARK/24NEWARK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'