l Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T10:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a95b9088-769c-5204-822e-9175bcfaabbb', 'word_count': 1250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a95b9088-769c-5204-822e-9175bcfaabbb'}, {'abstract': 'A compulsion to coerce men into relationships becomes self-destructive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/magazine/confessions-of-a-seduction-addict.html', 'snippet': 'A compulsion to coerce men into relationships becomes self-destructive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It started with a boy I met at summer camp and ended with the man for whom I left my first husband. In between, I careened from one intimate entanglement to the next — dozens of them — without so much as a day off between romances. You might have called me a serial monogamist, except that I was never exactly monogamous. Relationships overlapped, and those overlaps were always marked by exhausting theatricality: sobbing arguments, shaming confrontations, broken hearts. Still, I kept doing it. I couldn’t not do it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '47', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/magazine/28seductionside/28seductionside-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/magazine/28seductionside/28seductionside-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub