dge-halts-syscos-takeover-of-us-foods/', 'snippet': 'Judge Halts Sysco’s Takeover of US Foods | Investors Look Beyond Greece | Ahold and Delhaize Agree to Merger | Dutch Defenses in Mylan-Teva Takeover War', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUDGE HALTS SYSCO’S TAKEOVER OF US FOODS | Sysco’s $3.5 billion bid to buy US Foods was dealt a potentially fatal blow after a federal judge issued a preliminary injunction against the deal,  Michael J. de la Merced writes in DealBook. The merger of the country’s two biggest food distribution companies, which was first proposed in December 2013, has been opposed by the Federal Trade Commission. The commission sued in February to block the deal on the grounds that it would reduce competition in 32 markets and lead to higher prices and worse service for customers like restaurants and schools. In his ruling on Tuesday, Judge Amit P. Mehta of the Federal District Court for the District of Columbia sided with the F.T.C. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Judge Halts Sysco’s Takeover of US Foods', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's