ey’s Twitter post on the Confederate battle flag is credited with kick-starting the debate among Republicans and putting the issue at the forefront of the 2016 presidential campaign, the retweets he received were modest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A successful tweet is often measured by how often it’s retweeted, but Twitter’s data experts are focusing on a new statistic – impressions – that they argue better quantify impact. And they have found some exceptional numbers behind Mitt Romney and President Obama’s exchange over the Confederate battle flag.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s and Obama’s Confederate Flag Tweets Made Millions of Impressions', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T13:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d921fbbc-27dc-54a6-95ae-11ddf2ad45a0', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d921fbbc-27dc-54a6-95ae-11ddf2ad45a0'}, {'abstract': 'Home prices in Portugal fell by about 20 percent, and in