': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/24artsbeat-ross/24artsbeat-ross-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/24artsbeat-ross/24artsbeat-ross-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/24artsbeat-ross/24artsbeat-ross-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Ross Arrested and Charged With Kidnapping', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Rick (1976- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T15:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca6d720-f8e7-520b-bd77-a69ea9829339', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca6d720-f8e7-520b-bd77-a69ea9829339'}, {'abstract': 'A little boy finds independence despite his hovering family in a funny, refreshing new picture book.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/books/review/a-cure-for-hovering.html', 'snippet': 'A little boy finds independence despite his hovering family in a funny, refreshing new picture book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neglectful parents, too-busy parents, dead parents, parents who are just not in the picture, who knows why. … What would children’s literature be without them? Or rather: with them. It’s always a better story when children figure things out for themselves and adults are somewhere just offstage. But times have changed since the days when a 12-year-old and her 9-year-old brother could spend a couple of nights hiding out at the Metropolitan Museum, then head by train to the Connecticut home of one Mrs. Basil E. Frankweiler, pretty much eluding the entire adult world. We’re deep into the hovering era now. As evidence I offer this: Overinvolved parents —like the ones you see at the playground giving their offspring detailed instructions on how to play — have even begun storming the plots of children’s books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 261, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 261}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/books/review/24childrens/24childrens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cure for Hovering', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urban, Linda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valentine, Madeline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Little Red Henry (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T15:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Russo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18939b76-3fc7-59d5-bd67-0a48b0bebbe9', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18939b76-3fc7-59d5-bd67-0a48b0bebbe9'}, {'abstract': 'Starting Wednesday, Google Maps, using its Street View technology, will offer web users views of El Capitan from a rock climber’s perspective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/sports/googles-street-view-takes-armchair-climbers-up-el-capitan.html', 'snippet': 'Starting Wednesday, Google Maps, using its Street View technology, will offer web users views of El Capitan from a rock climber’s perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, El Capitan has been the most iconic rock climbing wall in the United States, if not the world. From the first ascent by Warren Harding and others in 1958 to the Dawn Wall climb by Tommy Caldwell and Kevin Jorgeson in January, 3,000-foot El Capitan has been the vertical domain of climbing pioneers.', '