itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d548dbe-60d2-5df9-8cd1-b2b6af21bafe', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d548dbe-60d2-5df9-8cd1-b2b6af21bafe'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Hepworth’s new exhibition at the Tate Britain is accompanied by a capsule collection inspired by the artist.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/barbara-hepworth-tate-britain-margaret-howell-range/', 'snippet': 'Barbara Hepworth’s new exhibition at the Tate Britain is accompanied by a capsule collection inspired by the artist.', 'lead_paragraph': '“She is almost always photographed wearing overalls and an anorak,” explains assistant curator Inga Fraser of the subject of a new exhibition, “Barbara Hepworth: Sculpture for the Modern World,” which opens at the Tate Britain in London this week. Though handy for stashing the pebbles she liked to gather on walks she took at dawn along her favorite Cornish beaches, Hepworth’s self-imposed workwear uniform was more than a function of practical necessity: “As a woman sculptor in the early 20th century trying to be seen on equal terms with her male counterparts, Hepworth had to put her work before everything else. She saw style as secondary.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24hepworth-farrell-1/24hepworth-farrell-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24hepworth-farrell-1/24hepworth-farrell-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24hepworth-farrell-1/24hepworth-farrell-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam