ured by Sarah Aubel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Diary: Walter Van Beirendonck Spring/Summer 2016 Men’s', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T18:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Aubel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aubel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/638a78df-299c-5e4f-bfe1-1dfd030396f0', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/638a78df-299c-5e4f-bfe1-1dfd030396f0'}, {'abstract': 'The boutique and site Austere and the Maidstone have teamed up to make the entire experience of staying at the inn available to buy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/austere-scandinavian-design-maidstone/', 'snippet': 'The boutique and site Austere and the Maidstone have teamed up to make the entire experience of staying at the inn available to buy.', 'lead_paragraph': "“My daughter calls that ‘my daddy’s swing,'” says Fredrik Carlstrom, pointing to Alexander Lervik’s Sense Light swing, affixed to the porch of the Maidstone hotel in East Hampton. In fact, the plexi-and-LED-lit version of the playground staple neither belongs to nor was crafted by Carlstrom, even if his daughter is, as he says, “very protective of it.” Rather, it’s an extension of the retail collaboration “Austere c/o the Maidstone,” currently overtaking the historic Hamptons inn. Last year, Carlstrom, who is by trade a marketing executive, launched Austere, a multichannel retail venture focusing mostly on Scandinavian heritage brands, which has been dubbed “a magazine you can walk into.” Austere exists as both a 5,000-square-foot store in Los Angeles and an active online portal, which on top of shilling wares satisfies customers’ curiosity with an editorial component that tells the tales of these Nordic brands and the region’s cultural values. “We noticed there are people who make things, people who sell things and people who talk about cool things,” explains Carlstrom, “No one was doing all of it. And so we’re trying to do that.”", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24austere-baumgardner-1/24austere-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24austere-baumgardner-1/24austere-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24austere-baumgardner-1/24austere-baumgardner-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24austere-baumgardner-1/24austere-baumgardner-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/t-magazine/24austere-baumgardner-1/24austere-baumgardner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2