me': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-24T21:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c617538-1f2e-5328-87ab-160ff4c8403e', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c617538-1f2e-5328-87ab-160ff4c8403e'}, {'abstract': 'The images in Jacob Lawrence’s Migration Series are perhaps the most recognizable images of \xadAfrican-Americans in the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/books/review/jacob-lawrence-the-migration-series-by-leah-dickerman-and-elsa-smithgall.html', 'snippet': 'The images in Jacob Lawrence’s Migration Series are perhaps the most recognizable images of \xadAfrican-Americans in the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One by one, the people left. Cotton sacks shed in place, a silent seepage from the fields, a human rivulet, and then a flood of six million black refugees fleeing the terrors of the Jim Crow South from World War I to 1970, an Overground Railroad that churned for nearly three generations and transformed the culture and social geography of 20th-century America. This leaderless revolution would come to be known as the Great Migration, and it would reshape every Northern and Western city it touched. By the time it was over, a rural people had become urban, and a Southern people had spread themselves over the country. Yet it was largely unrecognized, invisible to a majority of Americans while it was underway and almost too big to grasp even for those who were part of it.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28WILKERSON/28WILKERSON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jacob Lawrence: The Migration Series,’ by Leah Dickerman and Elsa Smithgall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pictures of Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 