hott, the French musician who performs as Colleen, used a treble viola da gamba to recreate songs from her recent album at SubCulture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At SubCulture in Manhattan on Tuesday night, Cecile Schott, the French musician who performs as Colleen, was preoccupied with precision. In her hands was a treble viola da gamba, an instrument largely associated with Baroque music. At her feet, a set of loop and delay pedals. She played a bit on her instrument, captured the sound with the pedals, then used that loop as a base from which to add layers and depth.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25COLLEEN/25COLLEEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/arts/25CO