e': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/252b4d60-1a94-521d-bc1a-dcc4188ecc80', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/252b4d60-1a94-521d-bc1a-dcc4188ecc80'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s supreme leader must decide whether his country can live with the economic and political consequences if he sabotages the nuclear deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/opinion/ayatollah-khameneis-fateful-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s supreme leader must decide whether his country can live with the economic and political consequences if he sabotages the nuclear deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 13 years since Iran’s nuclear program was discovered, the Iranians have worked to keep the program alive and the major powers at bay. Now they are jeopardizing the nuclear agreement that would benefit them and the security of the region. The agreement, under negotiation with the United States, Britain, France, Russia, China and Germany, is supposed to be completed on June 30, though a delay is now considered likely.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/opinion/25thurs1/25thurs1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/opinion/25thurs1/25thurs1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 744}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/opinion/25thurs1/25thurs1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/opinion/25thu