age and sentenced to death, but the charge was later reduced to helping a hostile power, with a 10-year imprisonment. Mr. Hekmati has asserted his innocence and described himself as a political hostage of Iran. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Captive’s Family Tries New Appeal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Middle East; Iran: Captive’s Family Tries New Appeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hekmati, Amir Mirzaei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Montel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vienna (Austria)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T01:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b0fc88e-c094-501f-81bd-47eb357cdefb', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b0fc88e-c094-501f-81bd-47eb357cdefb'}, {'abstract': 'In which David Poole takes away my solving snack for no reason at all.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/24/legendary-guitarist/', 'snippet': 'In which David Poole tak