ves as a reminder of one of baseball’s unwritten rules: ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/sports/SUB-CITY-METS/SUB-CITY-METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Struggle to Make More Places Like Home', 'kicker': 'Brewers 4, Mets 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Extend Search for More Places Like Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T03:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b546db-0a3b-5384-84cc-38334fae12a4', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b546db-0a3b-5384-84cc-38334fae12a4'}, {'abstract': 'The “Illmatic” rapper shares his rules of style with T ahead of the release of his film “Fresh Dressed.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/t-magazine/nas-fresh-dressed-style.html', 'snippet': 'The “Illmatic” rapper shares his rules of style with T ahead of the release of his film “Fresh Dressed.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Your coming of age is about representing who you are, and hip-hop music contains a message — it tells a story about who you are — and what you wear is also proof of it,” says the rapper Nasir Jones, a.k.a. Nas. It was with this in mind that he and a business partner, Sacha Jenkins — both onetime Queens residents currently in their 40s — set out to provide a cinematic reminder of “the importance of something that we’d grown up around and that is still strong in pop culture — clothes, fashion or what we call ‘gear.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25nas-moss/25nas-moss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A History of Hip-Hop and Fashion, as Told by Nas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f4db00-b6b0-5aba-929f-b63b01108e03', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f4db00-b6b0-5aba-929f-b63b01108e03'}, {'abstract': 'The real-life pals hang at a playground and discuss the fate of Jon Snow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/t-magazine/adam-scott-jason-schwartzman-playground-video.html', 'snippet': 'The real-life pals hang at a playground and discuss the fate of Jon Snow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Overnight,” Jason Schwartzman and Adam Scott play L.A. dads whose chance meeting on a playground leads to a family fun night that takes a wild turn after the kids go to bed. The film is a wry examination of the issues facing young parents: namely, the ways in which couples make new friends, and the challenge of keeping romance alive once there’s a mortgage to pay. It’s also filled with raucous twists that are best left a surprise — a fact that might disappoint Schwartzman, who cops to loving spoilers in real life. In the video above, watch as Scott responds to his co-star’s admission by putting his own creative spin on the ending to “Star Wars,” including a mysterious cameo by the brooding “Game of Thrones” heartthrob Jon Snow. (We knew he wasn’t dead!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch Adam Scott Spoil “Star Wars” for His “Overnight” Co-Star Jason Schwartzman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4f38b1-5bf4-570a-9bd7-a52a3b9777fb', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4f38b1-5bf4-570a-9bd7-a52a3b9777fb'}, {'abstract': 'The artist shares how to make one of his favorite breakfast staples, which he\'ll be serving at Doug Aitken\'s "Station to Station" in London beginning this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/t-magazine/ed-ruscha-cactus-omelet-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'The artist shares how to make one of his favorite breakfast staples, which he\'ll be serving at Doug Aitken\'s "Station to Station" in London beginning this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Desert life has always been on the periphery of Ed Ruscha’s work. In 1980, the artist constructed a fake resin boulder, dubbed “Rocky II,” which he hid in the Mojave Desert, the hunt for which is the subject of an upcoming feature film by Pierre Bismuth. In that same arid vein comes Ruscha’s latest, and equally unorthodox, outing: the recipe for a cactus omelet that will be served for lunch, for five consecutive Saturdays beginning this weekend, to visitors at the Barbican Art Gallery in London. It’s his quirky contribution to fellow Californian artist Doug Aitken’s collaborative exhibition, “Station to Station: A 30 Day Happening,” which also sees a series of art yurts (and Beck) installed at the Brutalist mecca this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/t-magazine/25ruscha-farrell/25ruscha-farrell-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ed Ruscha’s Recipe for a Cactus Omelet', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cacti (Plants)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruscha, Edward', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a83a44c-da25-5e4d-af26-8d95e1199115', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a83a44c-da25-5e4d-af26-8d95e1199115'}, {'abstract': 'The designer’s rural retreat, Cricket Court, is filled with family, disco balls and an array of antique knickknacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/t-magazine/alice-temperleys-british-country-house.html', 'snippet': 'The designer’s rural retreat, Cricket Court, is filled with family, disco balls and an array of antique knickknacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cricket Court, the country house that the British fashion designer Alice Temperley owns with her husband and business partner, Lars von Bennigsen, fully reflects both her personal style and her brand. Located down the road from the cider farm on which Temperley and her three siblings, Mary, Mathilda and Harry, grew up in the magical West Country county of Somerset, Cricket Court is the headquarters of the family’s younger generation. (Temperley’s parents, Julian and Diana, still live on the farm, and have the only commercial license in the country to make cider brandy.) Its look, like its owner’s, is borne out of the Somerset hills and romantic summer fetes — the kind of life that inspires Temperley’s floaty, lacy, feminine designs, which are worn by everyone from Beyoncé to Florence Welch to the Duchess of Cambridge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/03/25/t-magazine/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/03/25/t-magazine/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/03/25/t-magazine/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/03/25/t-magazine/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF/25temperley-konig-slide-8RGF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_nam