ness/dealbook/transunion-valued-at-4-billion-in-initial-public-offering.html', 'snippet': 'The credit reporting agency’s stock was priced at $22.50 a share, near the upper end of its expected pricing range of $21 to $23 a share.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TransUnion, one of the largest consumer credit reporting agencies in the United States, said on Thursday that its initial public offering was priced at $22.50 a share, valuing the company at about $4 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TransUnion Valued at $4 Billion in I.P.O.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransUnion LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVENT INTERNATIONAL CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T08:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4db5586-df9a-5ffc-a9ac-f60bd000653d', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4db5586-df9a-5ffc-a9ac-f60bd000653d'}, {'abstract': 'They appear to have drawn substantial numbers of younger, healthier people into the new insurance markets, stabilizing premiums, even for those who pay the full cost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/us/measuring-the-success-of-health-insurance-subsidies.html', 'snippet': 'They appear to have drawn substantial numbers of younger, healthier people into the new insurance markets, stabilizing premiums, even for those who pay the full cost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Affordable Care Act, saved by the Supreme Court for the second time in three years, has changed the fabric of health care in America, providing treatment and coverage to millions of the uninsured while transforming the insurance and hospital industries. But the law still faces stiff political resistance in many quarters and could yet return as an explosive issue in the 2016 elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/24/us/25SUBSIDIESWEB1/25SUBSIDIESWEB1-t