e-over-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Greece and Creditors at an Impasse Over Taxes | Is Greece Like Lehman Brothers or RadioShack? | Ahold-Delhaize Merger Reflects Flat Growth in Grocery Market', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREECE AND CREDITORS AT AN IMPASSE OVER TAXES | After the eurozone finance ministers abruptly ended their meeting on the Greek debt crisis on Wednesday, they were set to meet again at 1 p.m. in Brussels on Thursday (7 a.m. E.D.T.),  James Kanter writes in The New York Times. That makes it likely that the Greek debt crisis will dominate a summit meeting of all 28 European Union leaders that will begin later on Thursday afternoon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Greece and Creditors at an Impasse Over Taxes', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Value-Added Tax', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delhaize Group', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koninklijke Ahold N.V.', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RadioShack Corporation', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T11:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a71a551-32ba-549a-bc15-7e5d6f0163a3', 'word_count': 1621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a71a551-32ba-549a-bc15-7e5d6f0163a3'}, {'abstract': 'What do the creditors think they’re doing?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/breaking-greece/', 'snippet': 'What do the creditors think they’re doing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been staying fairly quiet on Greece, not wanting to shout Grexit in a crowded theater. But given reports from the negotiations in Brussels, something must be said — namely, what do the creditors, and in particular the IMF, think they’re doing?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Greece', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T11:22:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person':