ticle/dee2e718-6c6f-5fab-9240-2e996416f1ae', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dee2e718-6c6f-5fab-9240-2e996416f1ae'}, {'abstract': 'Shen Bolun and Wu Xia, who are not married, celebrated the smooth delivery of a healthy girl in Beijing on Sunday, but it came at a price: A government fine of about $7,200.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/fined-for-having-baby-unwed-couple-ask-chinese-public-to-pitch-in/', 'snippet': 'Shen Bolun and Wu Xia, who are not married, celebrated the smooth delivery of a healthy girl in Beijing on Sunday, but it came at a price: A government fine of about $7,200.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shen Bolun and Wu Xia, who are not married, celebrated the smooth delivery of a healthy girl in Beijing on Sunday. But the joyous event came with a price tag: a government fine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fined for Having Baby, Unwed Couple Ask Chinese Public to Pitch In', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Yimou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T11:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Boehler and Adam Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boehler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9653a60e-471b-5258-a4bf-d710434cab56', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9653a60e-471b-5258-a4bf-d710434cab56'}, {'abstract': 'A full-time aide seemed like the perfect solution for my son — until he came to rely on her aid far too much.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/for-a-child-with-a-learning-disability-theres-such-a-thing-as-too-much-help/', 'snippet': 'A full-time aide seemed like the perfect solution for my son — until he came to rely on her aid far too much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a kindergartner in a large public school, my son, who has a language-based learning disability, was mainstreamed in a general education classroom and shadowed throughout the day by an aide, or paraprofessional. We requested this additional support so my son could manage basic 5-year-old tasks that proved difficult for him. Being asked to line up with his classmates for recess, for example, wasn’t easy for my son. Although he heard the words, he didn’t necessarily understand their meaning straightaway. He needed time to process the information, then to respond. But in a school where academic rigor began on day one, there was no flextime for my son, who sauntered through his days with unhurried ease. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/motherlode-canoe/motherlode-canoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/24/us/motherlode-canoe/motherlode-canoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/24/us/motherlode-canoe/motherlode-canoe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra