veils its latest pavilion, and looks to the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Every summer here since 2000, a temporary pavilion pops up on the front lawn of the Serpentine Gallery in Kensington Gardens. The structure — which is open to the public for more than three months — is one of the world’s top architectural commissions in terms of public exposure. Made of materials that might include wood, cork or canvas, it plays host to the gallery’s annual fundraising party and gives an internationally recognized architecture firm the chance to show its first work in Britain.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26iht-serpentine26-a/26iht-serpentine26-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thu