: None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/853e4505-ec04-59e6-af8d-7800d6faf9ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/853e4505-ec04-59e6-af8d-7800d6faf9ca'}, {'abstract': 'King goes down.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/regicide-relief/', 'snippet': 'King goes down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: Just to put this out there, and let my 60s roots show: Hey, hey, ACA, how many lives did you save today?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regicide Relief', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T14:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa34695-11a0-542f-ae7a-ffc28f426097', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa34695-11a0-542f-ae7a-ffc28f426097'}, {'abstract': 'Jed Rasula uncovers why Dada didn’t expire along with the isms it either spawned or incorporated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/books/review/destruction-was-my-beatrice-dada-and-the-unmaking-of-the-twentieth-century.html', 'snippet': 'Jed Rasula uncovers why Dada didn’t expire along with the isms it either spawned or incorporated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jed Rasula’s history of Dada, “Destruction Was My Beatrice,” dispenses with a few old chestnuts of art history, chief among them the chronological fixation on Dada as a precursor to Surrealism, or a younger sibling of Futurism. The ordering by art critics of 20th-century avant-garde movements has required that they be both recognizable and dead. This has made them convenient and marketable, while draining away their revolutionary content. The art market embraced the products of every “ism” as soon as it recognized its distinct style. The only avant-garde that escaped the zombie line is Dada. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 650}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 946, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1846, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28Codrescu/28Codrescu-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Destruction Was My Beatrice: Dada and the Unmaking of the Twentieth Century’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headlin