uri': 'nyt://article/65dd1f4a-9db6-56ad-a29b-b4402565d14e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Biaggi had been a highly decorated police officer and a popular House member when he fell from grace in corruption scandals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/nyregion/mario-biaggi-10-term-new-york-congressman-who-went-to-prison-dies-at-97.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Biaggi had been a highly decorated police officer and a popular House member when he fell from grace in corruption scandals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mario Biaggi, a highly decorated former New York City police officer who became a popular 10-term Democratic congressman from the Bronx only to land in prison in a wave of corruption scandals in the late 1980s, died on Wednesday at his home in the Bronx. He was 97.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 818, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 818}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 752, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1503, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/nyregion/26biaggiobit2/26biaggiobit2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mario Biaggi, 97, Popular Bronx Congressman Who Went to Prison, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Mario Biaggi, 97, Official Undone by Scandals, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFadden, Robert D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biaggi, Mario', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T14:38:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7894bdd5-dc1f-5d0f-8fb0-7f626e0eaeaa', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7894bdd5-dc1f-5d0f-8fb0-7f626e0eaeaa'}, {'abstract': 'In a quest to be a husband and father, the character voiced by Seth MacFarlane aligns his struggle with that of enslaved black Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/movies/review-in-ted-2-the-foulmouthed-bear-tries-to-prove-hes-human.html', 'snippet': 'In a quest to be a husband and father, the character voiced by Seth MacFarlane aligns his struggle with that of enslaved black Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At one point in the comedy dead zone known as Seth MacFarlane’s “Ted 2,” the title character — a stuffed toy bear voiced by Mr. MacFarlane — and his dimwitted best friend, John (Mark Wahlberg), visit a comedy club to engage in a favorite pastime: throwing bleak improv ideas at the comics onstage. So, seated in the back of the auditorium while cloaked in darkness, the friends start shouting out suggestions like 9/11, Robin Williams and Charlie Hebdo to the unnerved comics. The topics don’t mean anything to Ted and John, who, like Mr. MacFarlane, take great pleasure in making others squirm. They could have just as easily yelled gang rape, the Holocaust and dead puppies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 957, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626TED2/0626TED2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Ted 2,’ the Foulmouthed Bear Tries to Prove He’s Human', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legal Offensive of a Lewd Bear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacFarlane, Seth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ted 2 (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T14:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/40c6e19d-dbb2-5f87-8813-933efa154cdc', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40c6e19d-dbb2-5f87-8813-933efa154cdc'}, {'abstract': 'One result of the ruling is that even states that started their own exchanges, facing technical challenges, may let the federal government take over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/upshot/obamacare-ruling-may-have-just-killed-state-based-exchanges.html', 'snippet': 'One result of the ruling is that even states that started their own exchanges, facing technical challenges, may let the federal government take over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the Supreme Court has ruled that health insurance consumers can receive federal subsidies regardless of their state’s role in running their insurance market, fewer states may stay in the game.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/upshot/sub-26UP-ACA/sub-26UP-ACA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obamacare Ruling May Have Just Killed State-Based Exchanges', 'kicker': 'King v. Burwell', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Law Lives, but Will State-Based Exchanges?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger-Katz, Margot', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T14:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6347fcd8-c585-58fc-b3f7-ce452c18e88f', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6347fcd8-c585-58fc-b3f7-ce452c18e88f'}, {'abstract': 'Two recent exhibition catalogs situate the work of Jean-Michel Basquiat within our potent cultural poles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/books/review/basquiat-and-the-bayou-and-jean-michel-basquiat-nows-the-time.html', 'snippet': 'Two recent exhibition catalogs situate the work of Jean-Michel Basquiat within our potent cultural poles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the American historical imagination, the North (even beyond our borders into Canada) symbolizes freedom, individual expression and progress, while the South conjures a mix of hospitality, religious fervor and persistent racial prejudice. It’s a cultural civil war that in some ways enables us to sidestep the more complicated realities of our national identity.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/books/review/28BASS/28BASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {