ndustry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The idea of a publication of any new Michael Wolff book inevitably elicits discomfort in those likely to come into his line of fire. Mr. Wolff’s studied unpleasantness has emerged as a brand of sorts. USA Today has even capitalized on it, running an ad campaign for his column featuring a potential subject running away from his office via a rope and grappling hook just to avoid an interview with the feared columnist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 1995, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/dbpix-wolff-2/dbpix-wolff-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Wolff’s New Book Celebrates the Success of Old Media', 'kicker': 'Book Entry', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Television Is the New Television: The Unexpected Triumph of Old Media in the Digital Age (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolff, Michael (1953- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T16:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan A. Knee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Knee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a17b2c97-5994-5d8a-bbd8-395a4515e0c5', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17b2c97-5994-5d8a-bbd8-395a4515e0c5'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian Aziz Ansari, whose “Modern Romance” is No. 2 on the hardcover nonfiction list, is the third star of “Parks and Recreation” to achieve best-sellerdom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian Aziz Ansari, whose “Modern Romance” is No. 2 on the hardcover nonfiction list, is the third star of “Parks and Recreation” to achieve best-sellerdom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sparks and Recreation: With “Modern Romance” — new at No. 2 on the hardcover nonfiction list — the comedian Aziz Ansari becomes the third star of NBC’s late, great sitcom “Parks and Recreation” to achieve best-sellerdom. (The others are Nick Offerman, whose “Gumption” is No. 15 in its fourth week on the list, and Amy Poehler, whose “Yes Please” is No. 2 on the monthly humor list after logging 26 weeks in hardcover nonfiction.) Ansari wrote “Modern Romance” with the N.Y.U. sociologist Eric Klinenberg, framing it as a comprehensive study of dating in the digital age. “Sociology, in a strange way, is similar to comedy,” he said on NPR recently. “It’s a lot about observation and making observations that resonate with people and trying to learn about why people do the things they do. And one idea that really applied to modern romance, in my opinion, was this whole notion of the paradox of choice. .\u2008.\u2008. Right now we have the most romantic options that any generation has ever had. And you would think, oh, more options, that’s better. But whenever you look at any studies they’ve done, they always find the more options people have, the harder it is for them to make a choice, and that when they do make a choice they’re less satisfied because they’re scared that they maybe chose the wrong thing. And whenever we talked to people about this in regards to dating, it totally resonated.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25insidelist/25insidelist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25insidelist/25insidelist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25insidelist/25insidelist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25insidelist/2