dwood coals creates a char that is robust and earthy, but never too ashy or excessive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/dining/steak-on-charcoal-cooking.html', 'snippet': 'Cooking meat directly on glowing hardwood coals creates a char that is robust and earthy, but never too ashy or excessive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve never been the kind of guys to worship outdoor grilling gear and technology. When we were growing up, Dad set the tone, making do with a rusty hardware store hibachi and a metal chimney. We’ve written about the ascetic thrill of using government-issue grills in state parks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Better Steak, Cook Directly on Charcoal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heeding Your Inner Rambo at the Grill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Ted', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beef', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byres, Tim (Chef)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T16:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Lee and Ted Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/313a570d-9fab-586c-8537-b363a4d9ca23', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/313a570d-9fab-586c-8537-b363a4d9ca23'}, {'abstract': 'The privately held Palantir is reported to be valued at $20 billion, but getting an accurate reading of its worth in the public markets seems unlikely.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/business/dealbook/palantir-technologies-intrigues-investors-despite-its-mysteries.html', 'snippet': 'The privately held Palantir is reported to be valued at $20 billion, but getting an accurate reading of its worth in the public markets seems unlikely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Palantir Technologies’ mystery inflates its valuation. The firm, a private data analytics company backed and beloved by government intelligence, is raising $500 million in fresh cash, giving it a potential valuation of $20 billion and landing it fairly high on the list of so-called unicorns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1222, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/01/business/01-PALANTIR-JP4/01-PALANTIR-JP4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Palantir Technologies Intrigues Investors Despite Its Mysteries', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palantir Technologies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T17:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42178d6b-f91d-53c7-a079-de58149c0d77', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42178d6b-f91d-53c7-a079-de58149c0d77'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of 30 essays by the pioneer scholar of feminist art history Linda Nochlin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/books/review/women-artists-the-linda-nochlin-reader.html', 'snippet': 'A collection of 30 essays by the pioneer scholar of feminist art history Linda Nochlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1971, Linda Nochlin published her groundbreaking article “Why Have There Been No Great Women Artists?,” a passionate and rigorous attack on nearly all the received ideas of her day. While it was necessary (she argued) to question “the unstated domination of white male subjectivity” that shaped the art historical canon, she found equally suspect the feminist impulse to resurrect forgotten or underappreciated women artists and elevate devalued “feminine” qualities. To get to the heart of the problem, it was necessary to question the notion of “greatness” or “genius” itself. Nochlin was then 40 years old. Two years before, she had experienced a feminist awakening when an acquaintance gave her a briefcase of radical feminist zines. A twice-married mother of two, teaching art history at Vassar College and leading what she had considered until then a fashionable and liberated life, she read until 2\u202fa.m., light bulbs going off in her head. “I kept opening doors,” she would write later, “onto an endless series of bright rooms, each one opening off from the next, each promising a new revelation.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25kraus/25kraus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25kraus/25kraus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25kraus/25kraus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/books/review/25kraus/25kraus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1605, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio