ord_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43908265-28c3-5480-a360-103b9763c854'}, {'abstract': 'A climate blogger thinks that because there is no uncertainty on climate basics, there’s no justification for examining the uncertainty about the severity of climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/25/in-weighing-responses-to-climate-change-severity-and-uncertainty-matter-more-than-reality/', 'snippet': 'A climate blogger thinks that because there is no uncertainty on climate basics, there’s no justification for examining the uncertainty about the severity of climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted in an update to a previous post, Greg Laden, who writes a spirited global warming blog, published a rather biting critique of my approach to blogging and climate science a few days ago. He’s both wrong in how he portrays my views of climate science and, to my mind, failing to recognize there can be more than one approach — in communication, technology, politics and other arenas — aimed at a common goal: in this case improving humanity’s intensifying two-way relationship with the climate system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/blogs/dothuntsafe/dothuntsafe-jumbo.png', 'height': 220, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/blogs/dothuntsafe/dothuntsafe-superJumbo.png', 'height': 220, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/blogs/dothuntsafe/dothuntsafe-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/25/blogs/dothuntsafe/dothuntsafe-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/25/blogs/dothuntsafe/dothuntsafe-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Weighing Responses to Climate Change, Severity and Uncertainty Matter More than ‘Reality’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coast Erosion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Gernot (1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grist (Magazine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T20:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e1d820-ad24-53a9-aebd-7fee7af2f879', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e1d820-ad24-53a9-aebd-7fee7af2f879'}, {'abstract': 'The drawstrings in hoodies and other tops can snap back in the wearer’s face and have caused seven injuries so far, the Consumer Product Safety Commission said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/business/lululemon-recalls-elastic-drawstrings-in-womens-tops.html', 'snippet': 'The drawstrings in hoodies and other tops can snap back in the w