': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6c56ade-c63f-56b5-8a51-06f25308bb96', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6c56ade-c63f-56b5-8a51-06f25308bb96'}, {'abstract': 'Humana, the smallest of the big five insurers, could reach a deal by next week. Among those in the running are two bigger competitors, Aetna and Cigna.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/business/dealbook/humana-said-to-pursue-sale-as-courts-ruling-gives-insurers-a-lift.html', 'snippet': 'Humana, the smallest of the big five insurers, could reach a deal by next week. Among those in the running are two bigger competitors, Aetna and Cigna.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new round of consolidation in the health insurance industry appeared closer as companies seek to grow larger, driven in part by cost-cutting and opportunities that are part of the Affordable Care Act.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 666}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1926, 'width': 1734, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/business/26db-humana/26db-humana-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Humana Said to Pursue Sale as Supreme Court Ruling Gives Insurers a Lift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Ruling Seen as a Spur to Consolidation of Insurers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Merced, Michael J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Humana Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AETNA INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CIGNA Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T23:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81a53818-ecb5-5cd4-9768-6223e8119313', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81a53818-ecb5-5cd4-9768-6223e8119313'}, {'abstract': 'With the Supreme Court’s decision upholding Obamacare, Republicans avoid a no-win situation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/opinion/a-turning-point-for-health-care-and-its-gop-opponents.html', 'snippet': 'With the Supreme Court’s decision upholding Obamacare, Republicans avoid a no-win situation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the second June in four years, the Supreme Court, led by its conservative chief justice, John G. Roberts Jr., has affirmed the legal framework of the Affordable Care Act of 2010 — the signature achievement of the Obama-era Democratic Party and a national social policy landmark. In so doing, the Roberts court assured the permanent expansion of social protections in America, and also saved the Republican Party from a no-win explosion its own extreme right-wingers tried to ignite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Turning Point for Health Care — and Its G.O.P. Opponents', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-25T23:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theda Skocpol and Lawrence R. Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Skocpol', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/04d9f116-6183-513d-9e33-b5204b20d06a', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04d9f116-6183-513d-9e33-b5204b20d06a'}, {'abstract': 'Dana Nachman documents the overwhelming response to a 5-year-old cancer patient’s wish to become Batman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/movies/review-in-batkid-begins-a-boys-simple-wish-whips-up-frenzied-adulation.html', 'snippet': 'Dana Nachman documents the overwhelming response to a 5-year-old cancer patient’s wish to become Batman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last few decades, the image of the cancer patient has transformed from that of private victim to public warrior. That extreme pendulum swing, however, is only one thread in the cord of concern woven by “Batkid Begins,” Dana Nachman’s awestruck documentary about the overwhelming response to a child’s simple wish.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/0626BATKID/0626BATKID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge'