'uri': 'nyt://article/0f52745b-b225-585a-ad4f-b5624c80798a'}, {'abstract': 'Three friends decide to commit a crime, greatly underestimating the difficulty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/movies/review-in-7-minutes-from-jay-martin-a-bank-robbery-plan-implodes.html', 'snippet': 'Three friends decide to commit a crime, greatly underestimating the difficulty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Jay Martin’s tightly wound debut film, “7 Minutes,” is the time that three aspiring bank robbers imagine it will take to pull off a heist that might net them a half-million dollars. These naïve co-conspirators — Sam (Luke Mitchell), a former high school football star with a pregnant girlfriend and a nightmarish factory job; his drug-dealing older brother, Mike (Jason Ritter), who is married with a small child; and his best friend, Owen (Zane Holtz) — fantasize that robbing Sam and Mike’s crooked uncle’s bank will be a snap. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26SEVENMINUTES/0626SEVENMINUTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26SEVENMINUTES/0626SEVENMINUTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26SEVENMINUTES/0626SEVENMINUTES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/arts/26SEVENMINUTES/0626SEVENMINUTES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1803, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':