t': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc4d0cc-780f-5609-af0b-09272fb16bfe'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of companies are using artisanal ingredients and interesting flavors to create lunches to enjoy outdoors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/nyregion/picnics-to-go-are-growing-in-the-hamptons.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of companies are using artisanal ingredients and interesting flavors to create lunches to enjoy outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The local harvest may be delayed by an unusually cold spring this year, but as the sweet corn, heirloom tomatoes and summer squash come to market, several new picnic purveyors on the East End will be dreaming up ways to enjoy them alfresco. For many of us, a French baguette and a hunk of artisanal cheese from the Village Cheese Shop in Mattituck make a magnificent movable feast. But recently, picnic options from East Marion to Southampton have expanded, reflecting a locavore-inspired mission: Food that is grown in these fields can also be savored in them.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28DINELI3/28DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28DINELI3/28DINELI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28DINELI3/28DINELI3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28DINELI3/28DINELI3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub