ct', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-26T07:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/377c5199-0b54-5386-93c4-66526b5f57ac', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377c5199-0b54-5386-93c4-66526b5f57ac'}, {'abstract': 'Fierce temperatures and strict adherence to fasting rules during the holy month are killing hundreds of Pakistanis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/opinion/in-pakistan-heat-waves-and-the-holy-month-dont-mix.html', 'snippet': 'Fierce temperatures and strict adherence to fasting rules during the holy month are killing hundreds of Pakistanis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARACHI, Pakistan — WHEN I go to buy my drinking water, I don’t ask for water. I ask for Nestlé. Then I drive home with five 20-liter plastic bottles and make sure that we make every cup of tea, and all our ice, from this water. Like other people in this city, I believe the tap water is poisonous. During the summer, many of us follow the practice of putting out a water cooler on the street for passers-by. There are chic restaurants, cafes and art galleries in my neighborhood, but not a single public source of clean drinking water. Street vendors, security guards, trash pickers and maids rushing from one job to another often stop by to have a drink from this cooler. Like most such water coolers, mine is secured with a padlock; even the plastic tumbler is tied to it with a small chain.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1318, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26Hanif/26Hanif-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Karachi, a Fatal Mix of Heat and Piety', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heat Waves and the Holy Month', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanif, Mohammed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fasting', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-26T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohammed Hanif', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohammed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hanif', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6391a57-f6e6-5f2d-b2dd-79d161e72067', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6391a57-f6e6-5f2d-b2dd-79d161e72067'}, {'abstract': 'The European private equity firm will buy a controlling share in the German laboratory testing company, in a deal that values Synlab at about $2 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/27/business/dealbook/cinven-agrees-to-buy-a-majority-stake-in-synlab.html', 'snippet': 'The European private equity firm will buy a controlling share in the German laboratory testing company, in a deal that values Synlab at about $2 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Funds advised by BC Partners have agreed to sell a majority stake in Synlab, one of Europe’s largest independent providers of laboratory services, to the European private equity firm Cinven.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cinven Agrees to Buy a Majority Stake in Synlab', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BC Partners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cinven Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank