_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04cce526-86d9-5937-b4d9-c7d3179daa9d', 'word_count': 1896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04cce526-86d9-5937-b4d9-c7d3179daa9d'}, {'abstract': 'Our Summer Reading Contest is in its third week. To participate, just post a comment here by 7 a.m. Eastern on July 3 and answer the question, “What interested you most in The Times this week?”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/summer-reading-contest-week-3-what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week-2/', 'snippet': 'Our Summer Reading Contest is in its third week. To participate, just post a comment here by 7 a.m. Eastern on July 3 and answer the question, “What interested you most in The Times this week?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A short video from the Summer of Science series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Reading Contest, Week 3 | What Interested You Most in The Times This Week?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-26T11:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9de4afd8-763c-57e5-8ac8-48609e1bb556', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9de4afd8-763c-57e5-8ac8-48609e1bb556'}, {'abstract': 'As I decrease my medications, the urgency I feel around men and relationships subsides.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/26/singleminded/', 'snippet': 'As I decrease my medications, the urgency I feel around men and relationships subsides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m almost unmedicated. Each morning, I take just 100 milligrams of bupropion. At bedtime, I take a quarter milligram of lorazepam. I’ve eliminated trazodone. And I’m single. My ex and I are friends again — we were friends for years before we dated — and now that my heartbreak has receded, I don’t miss the upstream swim of that relationship. I still pop awake in the middle of the night, and often stay awake for two or three hours, but there’s a peacefulness to my days now. Summer is helping. It always does. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1606, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/opinion/26anxiety/26anxiety-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Singleminded',