: 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/d35fc5d3-be2b-5f29-bc8e-772296deb8c1', 'word_count': 2495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d35fc5d3-be2b-5f29-bc8e-772296deb8c1'}, {'abstract': 'The provider of office space is growing fast, but based on rivals’ metrics, earnings would need to jump fifteenfold to justify a $10 billion valuation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/27/business/dealbook/wework-stretches-sharing-economy-valuations.html', 'snippet': 'The provider of office space is growing fast, but based on rivals’ metrics, earnings would need to jump fifteenfold to justify a $10 billion valuation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WeWork is stretching valuations for the sharing economy. The company, an American provider of office space to millennial workers, is valued by investors at $10 billion after its latest private funding round, doubling in just six months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'WeWork Stretches Sharing-Economy Valuations', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regus Business Centers PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WeWork Companies Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-26T19:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b963603-8cef-5141-9eed-4cf3e596da1a', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b963603-8cef-5141-9ee