tting-better/', 'snippet': 'Can’t get no worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, it has been a pretty good few days: health reform, marriage rights, fair housing, and a long-overdue recognition that fighting for slavery was wrong. And for some reason, I find myself reaching back to the past. Maybe it’s because Justice Scalia told us to go ask the nearest hippie. Maybe because today’s Times real-estate-section report on “what it’s like to live in …” features the town where I grew up. (I remember the split-level ranches — those were the fancy houses. We had an ordinary, small ranch on a slab foundation — no basement. I believe my parents bought it for $15,000.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Got To Admit It’s Getting Better', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-26T21:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d45a87f-d0c9-58e4-b5ec-561b01d0eb56', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d45a87f-d0c9-58e4-b5ec-561b01d0eb56'}, {'abstract': 'How high can a Lego tower go?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000003767116/skyscraper.html', 'snippet': 'How high can a Lego tower go?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How high can a Lego tower go?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/26/multimedia/tallest-legos-milan/tallest-legos-milan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/26