-c969-539e-92f8-be76e74ff6c9'}, {'abstract': 'Grove Street Cemetery in New Haven, where Eli Whitney, Noah Webster and other notable figures lieare buried, was started because of epidemics of yellow fever and scarlet fever and opened in 1797.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/nyregion/the-nations-first-planned-burial-ground.html', 'snippet': 'Grove Street Cemetery in New Haven, where Eli Whitney, Noah Webster and other notable figures lieare buried, was started because of epidemics of yellow fever and scarlet fever and opened in 1797.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Fourth of July, a column of the Governor’s Foot Guard in Connecticut, one of the country’s oldest military units, marches in procession through the gates of the New Haven Burial Ground, one of the country’s oldest operating cemeteries. In their red jackets and thick gold epaulets, the men proceed to the grave of David Humphreys, an aide-de-camp to George Washington during the Revolutionary War. Speeches are given, chests are puffed and afterward onlookers snap selfies with the guards.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28ARTSCT1/28ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28ARTSCT1/28ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28ARTSCT1/28ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/nyregion/28ARTSCT1/28ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'supe