es helicopter in Nepal that killed 13 people in May was caused by bad weather and the geography of the region, the Nepalese Army said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/27/world/asia/nepal-rough-terrain-and-bad-weather-led-to-helicopter-crash-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'The crash of a United States Marines helicopter in Nepal that killed 13 people in May was caused by bad weather and the geography of the region, the Nepalese Army said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The crash of a United States Marines helicopter in Nepal that killed 13 people in May was caused by bad weather and the geography of the region, the Nepalese Army said in a statement Friday. The UH-1 Huey helicopter had been on a relief mission to aid people affected by a major earthquake in April when it lost radio contact after a second earthquake hit the region. In the statement, the army said that a joint investigation by Nepalese and American military officials found that hilly terrain and bad weather caused the helicopter’s pilot to strike hard rock at 11,200 feet in the Kalinchowk area, east of the capital, Kathmandu. The Marines and Nepal’s army had originally said that six Marines and two Nepalese Army officials had been killed, but earlier this month Nepal’s army announced that five civilians had also been on the flight. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nepal: Rough Terrain and Bad Weather Led to Helicopter Crash, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia; Nepal: Rough Terrain and Bad Weather Led to Helicopter Crash, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States D