nted for all the teams’ runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — For rookies or veterans, there is always something special about returning home to play baseball.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/27/sports/ALT-CITY-YANKEES/ALT-CITY-YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Yanks Bask in Comforts of Home, Sinking Astros', 'kicker': 'Yankees 3, Astros 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Yanks Bask in Comforts of Home, Sinking Astros', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eovaldi, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Chris (1979- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-27T04:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbfe2fb5-f41d-551a-a98c-45f2b574f74a', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbfe2fb5-f41d-551a-a98c-45f2b574f74a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/27/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) JOHN WICK (2014) A fabled hit man (Keanu Reeves) unleashes mayhem on a Russian mobster (Alfie Allen) who has killed the puppy that was the last gift from his recently deceased wife (Bridget Moynahan) in this savage adventure directed by Chad Stahelski (Mr. Reeves’s stunt double in “Constantine” and two “Matrix” films). Willem Dafoe, John Leguizamo, Ian McShane and Michael Nyqvist provide backup. “Brilliant in its simplicity, the setup of ‘John Wick,’ like the rest of the movie, passes swiftly and efficiently,” Jeannette Catsoulis wrote in The New York Times, making the film a critics’ pick. “Harboring few ambitions beyond knock-your-socks-off action sequences, this crafty revenge thriller delivers with so much style — and even some wit — that the lack of substance takes longer than it should to become problematic. Until then, we’re content to tag along as John, revealed as the ne plus ultra of former assassins, comes out of retirement and into the cross hairs.” His quest, she added, “may be one-note, but that note could not be more perfectly pitched.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-27T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4215714-d0ce-5728-b27f-224ccfb86803', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4215714-d0ce-5728-b27f-224ccfb86803'}, {'abstract': 'For most neuroscientists, this is just a bad metaphor. But it’s still the most useful analogy that we have.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/opinion/sunday/face-it-your-brain-is-a-computer.html', 'snippet': 'For most neuroscientists, this is just a bad metaphor. But it’s still the most useful analogy that we have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SCIENCE has a poor track record when it comes to comparing our brains to the technology of the day. Descartes thought that the brain was a kind of hydraulic pump, propelling the spirits of the nervous system through the body. Freud compared the brain to a steam engine. The neuroscientist Karl Pribram likened it to a holographic storage device.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'p