 two masters — the paper and the bookselling business?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/public-editor/public-editor-margaret-sullivan-on-reporters-writing-books.html', 'snippet': 'It’s understandable that so many reporters like to write books, but is it really possible to serve two masters — the paper and the bookselling business?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WRITING books must be in the DNA of Times journalists. Even the paper’s founding editor, Henry J. Raymond, cranked them out, including his “History of the Administration of President Lincoln” in 1864. The next year, he returned with another, which boasted an equally catchy title: “The Life and Public Services of Abraham Lincoln.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Reporters Write Books, Does The Times Win, Too?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Reporters Write Books, Does The Times Win, Too?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Margaret M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Margaret M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shane, Scott', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Andrew', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger, David', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-27T18:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aee040f-fbc7-535a-b6d4-d635a5cd3f1f', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aee040f-fbc7-535a-b6d4-d635a5cd3f1f'}, {'abstract': 'To hear your landlord laugh at your request for a new stove, press the star key.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/28/opinion/an-audio-tour-of-your-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'To hear your landlord laugh at your request for a new stove, press the star key.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HELLO! And welcome to your apartment. The goal of this audio guide is to foster a deeper appreciation of the place that, given your liberal arts degree and tenuous employment prospects, you certainly won’t be moving out of anytime soon. The guide will provide a historical overview of the events, traditions and sheer human drama that have made this place a must-see destination for journalists, scholars and that guy who delivers your Seamless orders. We hope it will give you a fresh and exciting perspective on Apartment 2B. Headset on? Ready? Good. Press 1, then the green arrow, to get started.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/opinion/sunday/28LOOSE/28loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/opinion/sunday/28LOOSE/28loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/opinion/sunday/28LOOSE/28loose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType':