ht': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/nyregion/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/29/nyregion/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/nyregion/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV/20150629PARADEsubss-slide-59AV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celebration of Gay Pride and a Supreme Court Ruling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T03:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3fb6f50d-777d-52be-9990-b01f81fb8297', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3fb6f50d-777d-52be-9990-b01f81fb8297'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s Rent Guidelines Board will vote on Monday on whether to increase rents for more than one million stabilized apartments. It has never voted for no increases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/nyregion/new-york-city-board-set-to-vote-on-rent-freeze-after-state-legislators-reach-deal.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s Rent Guidelines Board will vote on Monday on whether to increase rents for more than one million stabilized apartments. It has never voted for no increases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just days after state legislators agreed to extend rent regulations for another four years, New York City’s Rent Guidelines Board is scheduled to vote on Monday evening on whether to increase rents for more than one million rent-stabilized apartments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Board Set to Vote on Rent Freeze After State Legislators Reach Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Board Set to Vote on Rent Freeze After State Legislators Reach Deal ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navarro, Mireya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rent Guidelines Board', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T03:17:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d369d401-e9f3-5c45-84e3-846388f69e5f', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d369d401-e9f3-5c45-84e3-846388f69e5f'}, {'abstract': 'Bernhard Willhelm — known for his zany prints and creative cuts — recently relocated his home and studio to Los Angeles, bringing his entourage (and their wild ways) along for the party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/t-magazine/a-paris-designer-sets-up-a-creative-commune-in-the-hollywood-hills.html', 'snippet': 'Bernhard Willhelm — known for his zany prints and creative cuts — recently relocated his home and studio to Los Angeles, bringing his entourage (and their wild ways) along for the party.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I have an enormous need for freedom,” says Bernhard Willhelm. “I realized that I like being not too comfortable, but rather the opposite.” Earlier this year, the Bavarian-born fashion designer and provocateur — known for his outlandish prints and silhouettes and an ongoing shoe collaboration with Camper — uprooted his studio from Paris to a rustic 1957 house built into a steep hill in Hollywood’s Beachwood Canyon. Now, rather than the click-clack of heels along the boulevards, he hears hummingbirds as he works alongside his familial team, including his business partner, Jutta Kraus, who lives with him, and other designers and assistants who came along from Paris. “I think this choice turned out to be very spontaneous and a bit naïve, too, but it’s always been that way in my life,” says Wilhelm, who had visited California only once before making the move. “Germans make rational decisions and sometimes I decide to do emotional ones.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Paris Designer Sets up a Creative Commune in the Hollywood Hills', 'kicker': 'Home and Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e7f1cfc-8018-5632-8428-b33853a1271f', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e7f1cfc-8018-5632-8428-b33853a1271f'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of Candelaria, Glass and Le Mary Celeste recently opened Hero, where diners are encouraged to get messy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/t-magazine/paris-candelelaria-cocktails-korean-fried-chicken.html', 'snippet': 'The owners of Candelaria, Glass and Le Mary Celeste recently opened Hero, where diners are encouraged to get messy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emerge from the metro at the Strasbourg Saint-Denis station and you can’t help but instantly catch sight of the neon pink sign beaming the word “Hero.” The neighborhood’s colorful, late-night reputation might lead some to assume the sign marks yet another sex shop or dive bar. Instead, this spot beckons a hungry crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/29/t-magazine/29hero-tramuta/29hero-tramuta-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris’s New Korean Joint, From Some of the City’s Coolest Expats', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsey Tramuta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tramuta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3011059-3f2c-5c3b-9a31-8702115b4bc9', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3011059-3f2c-5c3b-9a31-8702115b4bc9'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Railroad Administration is hoping its new measure to integrate grade-crossing locations into mapping technology will curb the recent increase in crashes and fatalities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/technology/agency-taps-mapping-technology-to-curb-rail-crossing-accidents.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Railroad Administration is hoping its new measure to integrate grade-crossing locations into mapping technology will curb the recent increase in crashes and fatalities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a sharp increase in the number of rail crossing accidents last year, the Federal Railroad Administration plans to announce a new partnership with Google on Monday to provide the locations of all grade crossings in the company’s popular map application. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':