oad Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2d5db42-8438-55a0-bc34-72caf492e48d', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2d5db42-8438-55a0-bc34-72caf492e48d'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 59 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/word-of-the-day-unrequited/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 59 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'unrequited • \\ˌən-ri-ˈkwi-təd\\ • adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | unrequited', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:03:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb517ea2-ae7f-5433-a394-06af42f4f26f', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb517ea2-ae7f-5433-a394-06af42f4f26f'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '5 P.M. (Lifetime) WHILE YOU WERE SLEEPING (1995) Lucy (Sandra Bullock), a lonely Chicago train station clerk, leaps to the rescue when Peter (Peter Gallagher), the object of her unspoken desire, is pushed onto the train tracks and falls into a coma. But after a nurse mistakenly identifies her as Peter’s fiancée, she suddenly finds herself surrounded by the family she never had — including his charmingly suspicious brother, Jack (Bill Pullman). When a romantic comedy is “as breezy and adorable” as this one from Jon Turteltaub, “it’s time to fall in love,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times. “This is a formula film, but it has the kind of good cheer and fine tuning that occasionally give slickness a good name.” Ms. Bullock, above with Micole Mercurio, left, Monica Keena and Jack Warden, brings “a warm smile and a winning array of mannerisms to her role,” she added. And “as Jack does a perpetual slow burn in Lucy’s presence, Mr. Pullman smolders with consummate ease,” engaging in “the graceful teamwork that really makes this story click.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/62479ec3-0609-5f0c-877c-8b702883b3e4', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62479ec3-0609-5f0c-877c-8b702883b3e4'}, {'abstract': 'A week ahead of his 80th birthday, the exiled Tibetan spiritual leader took to the stage at the British music festival and expressed a desire to be as active as the veteran musicians around him.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/dalai-lama-reflects-on-aging-at-glastonbury/', 'snippet': 'A week ahead of his 80th birthday, the exiled Tibetan spiritual leader took to the stage at the British music festival and expressed a desire to be as active as the veteran musicians around him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week ahead of his 80th birthday, the Dalai Lama thanked thousands of well-wishers at one of Europe’s largest music festivals on Sunday as they sang “Happy Birthday” to\xa0the exiled Tibetan spiritual leader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dalai Lama Reflects on Aging at Glastonbury', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T04:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Boehler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boehler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3ec7ba-8d03-5090-816a-92b97b629b59', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3ec7ba-8d03-5090-816a-92b97b629b59'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, June 29, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, June 29, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I feel like a full citizen for the first time in my life. And I feel that people that still hate no longer have the government backing them up.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kick