tract': 'Readers write about why being nice in the workplace is better for organizations and their employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/opinion/nice-is-better-the-cost-of-incivility-in-the-workplace.html', 'snippet': 'Readers write about why being nice in the workplace is better for organizations and their employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nice Is Better: The Cost of Incivility in the Workplace', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nice Is Better: The Cost of Incivility in the Workplace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2944d57-8d89-5f4e-b6be-e153f414a3a1', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2944d57-8d89-5f4e-b6be-e153f414a3a1'}, {'abstract': 'Digital media has rediscovered a very old business model. Make your customers pay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/opinion/how-television-won-the-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Digital media has rediscovered a very old business model. Make your customers pay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RUPERT MURDOCH recently appointed his son James chief executive of 21st Century Fox, prompting the obvious question: How can a guy whose main credential is a silver spoon compete with Silicon Valley’s meritocratic coders and entrepreneurs?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Television Won the Internet', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Media, New Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolff, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, James R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wolff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f07c6490-2e0b-5ff2-a703-da516abf985b', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f07c6490-2e0b-5ff2-a703-da516abf985b'}, {'abstract': 'Ever-harsher austerity has been a dead end, and those who demand more of it have been wrong every step of the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/opinion/paul-krugman-greece-over-the-brink.html', 'snippet': 'Ever-harsher austerity has been a dead end, and those who demand more of it have been wrong every step of the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been obvious for some time that the creation of the euro was a terrible mistake. Europe never had the preconditions for a successful single currency — above all, the kind of fiscal and banking union that, for example, ensures that when a housing bubble in Florida bursts, Washington automatically protects seniors against any threat to their medical 