ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3802463-faa5-5fba-b0b5-8a757861d458', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3802463-faa5-5fba-b0b5-8a757861d458'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: An aid worker takes out life insurance on a hostage held by the Viet Cong in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/29/1965-life-insurance-on-hostage/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: An aid worker takes out life insurance on a hostage held by the Viet Cong in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The government is investigating a bizarre case in which an AID employee in Vietnam allegedly applied for life insurance on a colleague and friend captured by the Viet Cong, it was disclosed today [June 29]. Gustav C. Hertz, who was taken prisoner by Viet Cong guerrillas Feb. 2, is under a threat of retaliatory execution if the Saigon government puts to death a terrorist arrested for the March 30 bombing of the U.S. embassy. The terrorist, Nguyen Van Thai, is still under death sentence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/blogs/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam-jumbo.png', 'height': 547, 'width': 531, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/blogs/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam-superJumbo.png', 'height': 547, 'width': 531, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/blogs/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam/30iht-oldjune30-vietnam-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/0