ear-old drummer. A moment later he caught himself, observing that this crowd probably didn’t need to be briefed. But he went on, “just in case somebody wandered in,” he said, “and didn’t realize it was a cult gathering.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilco Tinkers and Experiments at a Festival It’s Happy to Share', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wilco Tinkers and Experiments at a Festival It&#8217;s Happy to Share ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Adams (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tweedy, Jeff', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wilco (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-29T22:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/349d9d21-3f31-5c79-81be-66d525f2fa61', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/349d9d21-3f31-5c79-81be-66d525f2fa61'}, {'abstract': 'In a solo recital at Bargemusic, Ms. Oppens performed recent pieces alongside works by Schubert, Beethoven and Scriabin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/arts/music/review-pianist-ursula-oppens-seamlessly-connects-the-classics-with-new-music.html', 'snippet': 'In a solo recital at Bargemusic, Ms. Oppens performed recent pieces alongside works by Schubert, Beethoven and Scriabin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ursula Oppens is an eloquent pianist who has long been a persuasive advocate of new music, which she presents not as a discipline separate from the interpretation of the classics but as an extension of that work. The connection felt especially organic in the solo recital she presented at Bargemusic on Friday evening. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1085, 'width': 1934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/arts/30OPPENS/30OPPENS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Pianist Ursula Oppens Seamlessly Connects the Classics With New Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seamlessly Connecting the Classics and New M