ld/africa/peace-eludes-south-sudan-as-rivals-hold-talks-capture-malakal.html', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for the rebels said that “progress is being made” in negotiations to end South Sudan’s civil war, even as forces had seized the strategic city of Malakal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — Even as South Sudan’s president, Salva Kiir, and his longtime rival, the rebel leader Riek Machar, met here at the behest of Kenya’s president to end South Sudan’s civil war, Mr. Machar’s forces captured the strategic city of Malakal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peace Eludes South Sudan as Rivals Hold Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peace Eludes South Sudan as Rivals Hold Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Kushkush, Isma'il", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiir Mayardit, Salva', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Machar, Riek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malakal (South Sudan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T00:26:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': "By Isma'il Kushkush", 'person': [{'firstname': "Isma'il", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kushkush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7e89820-88e9-53ad-9884-7875139cee14', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7e89820-88e9-53ad-9884-7875139cee14'}, {'abstract': 'The three-man panel said it was not yet ready to make a complete recommendation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/nyregion/fast-food-restaurants-should-raise-minimum-wage-new-york-panel-says.html', 'snippet': 'The three-man panel said it was not yet ready to make a complete recommendation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The minimum wage for fast-food workers in New York should be raised substantially, maybe even to $15 an hour, a state panel appointed to study the issue said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast-Food Restaurants Should Raise Minimum Wage, New York Panel Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel Backs Raises at Fast-Food Chains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musolino, Mario J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wage', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T00:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43b27a0f-bbb2-59a5-b217-db5c41bc8b04', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43b27a0f-bbb2-59a5-b217-db5c41bc8b04'}, {'abstract': 'Germany and the United States were sharing a hotel before m