 Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T04:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/113d302d-fed0-5fb5-bd12-ddeb5628644a', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/113d302d-fed0-5fb5-bd12-ddeb5628644a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:05 P.M. (Starz Cinema) TALK TO HER (2002) In Pedro Almodóvar’s tragic comedy, two men — Benigno (Javier Cámara), a nurse, and Marco (Darío Grandinetti), a journalist — share an unusual friendship while they care for their girlfriends: Alicia (Leonor Watling), a dancer, and Lydia (Rosario Flores), a matador, who are both comatose. But their devotion isn’t what it seems: Benigno is obsessive, with no real ties to Alicia. And suddenly romance is tinged with horror. “Like all great doomed affairs, ‘Talk to Her,’\xa0” Elvis Mitchell wrote in The New York Times, “is full of lovely, sweet suffering. And when it’s over, the realization of how much the movie means to you really sinks in; you can’t get it out of your heart.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T05:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/263bc2c9-2e46-5adb-aba0-31f978633822', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263bc2c9-2e46-5adb-aba0-31f978633822'}, {'abstract': 'Later this summer, United Airlines will begin using fuel generated from farm waste and oil from animal fats to help power its commercial flights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/business/energy-environment/farm-waste-and-animal-fats-will-help-power-a-united-jet.html', 'snippet': 'Later this summer, United Airlines will begin using fuel generated from farm waste and oil from animal fats to help power its commercial flights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime this summer, a United Airlines flight will take off from Los Angeles International Airport bound for San Francisco using fuel generated from farm waste and oils derived from animal fats.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/business/30BIOFUELS/30BIOFUELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/30/business/30BIOFUELS/30BIOFUELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/business/30BIOFUELS/30BIOFUELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/business/30BIOFUELS/30BIOFUELS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'