ain after a 71-year-old man set himself on fire on Tuesday. He and a female passenger died, and dozens were hurt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/multimedia/japan-train-fire/japan-train-fire-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Clears Train After Self-Immolation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T10:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7e59eefc-bce6-5af6-ada7-d42038b80d45', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7e59eefc-bce6-5af6-ada7-d42038b80d45'}, {'abstract': 'Travel Noire, a resource for black globe-trotters, continues an online tradition of pulling together like-minded communities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/joy-of-a-black-planet.html', 'snippet': 'Travel Noire, a resource for black globe-trotters, continues an online tradition of pulling together like-minded communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2011, Zim Ugochukwu was traveling on the Jagriti Yatra, a 15-day train trip through India for aspiring entrepreneurs. Her time in India wound up sparking an idea for a start-up, though perhaps not in the way the trip’s organizers intended. Ugochukwu was struck by the fact that, out of a group of about 500, she was one of just three African-Americans. She thought about how mainstream travel publications, even those online, weren’t speaking to them or their experiences. ‘‘When I searched ‘black travel’ on Google, I saw a black suitcase,’’ she said. ‘‘That’s not what I meant.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-articleLarge-v9.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-articleLarge-v9.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-jumbo-v9.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-superJumbo-v9.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05search/05search-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joy of a Black Planet', 'kicker': 'Search Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joy of a Black Planet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Travel Noire', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1632407d-2d3a-5eb1-8209-0e091184ed5c', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1632407d-2d3a-5eb1-8209-0e091184ed5c'}, {'abstract': 'For millions of mixed-race people, identity fits more than one box, but we still see one another in black and white.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/americas-postracial-fantasy.html', 'snippet': 'For millions of mixed-race people, identity fits more than one box, but we still see one another in black and white.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Father’s Day, my dad and I had brunch with some close friends of mine. The conversation soon turned to their two sons: their likes, their dislikes, their habit of disrupting classmates during nap time at nursery school. At one point, as I ran my hand through one of the boys’ silky brown hair, I asked whether they consider their kids biracial. (The father is white; the mother is South Asian.) Before they could respond, the children’s paternal grandmother, in town for a visit, replied as if the answer were the most obvious thing in the world: ‘‘They’re white.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 569}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 971, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1943, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05firstwords/05mag-05firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s ‘Postracial’ Fantasy', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Background Checks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Anna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolezal, Rachel A (1977- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charleston, SC, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'b