}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c60edb43-4e11-59ca-9635-56606a09f68c', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c60edb43-4e11-59ca-9635-56606a09f68c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a game. But it’s also what we need in life: the freedom to be found.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/the-importance-of-hide-and-seek/', 'snippet': 'It’s a game. But it’s also what we need in life: the freedom to be found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve found myself wondering lately which of my patients were lucky enough as children to play hide-and-seek with their parents. When it’s played as it’s meant to be, it’s such a delightful game. Kids ask to play it, though, only when they’re confident that they’ll be found. In that way, it’s a bit like psychotherapy: Only when patients feel hopeful that their experiences and feelings will be understood does the work begin in earnest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Importance of Hide-and-Seek', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-06-30T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Carper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39e6bda7-09d5-5631-b553-a194e2796eb8', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39e6bda7-09d5-5631-b553-a194e2796eb8'}, {'abstract': 'A Hard-Line Stance on Greece | Few Cures for Heavy Debt Loads | Muted Response to Puerto Rico’s Debt Crisis | K.K.R. Settles Over ‘Broken Deal’ Expenses', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/06/30/morning-agenda-a-hard-line-stance-on-greece/', 'snippet': 'A Hard-Line Stance on Greece | Few Cures for Heavy Debt Loads | Muted Response to Puerto Rico’s Debt Crisis | K.K.R. Settles Over ‘Broken Deal’ Expenses', 'lead_paragraph': 'A HARD-LINE STANCE ON GREECE | Greece has until 6 p.m. E.D.T. on Tuesday to make a 1.6 billion euro, or $1.8 billion, payment to the International Monetary Fund, but in an interview on state television on Monday night, the Greek prime minister, Alexis Tsipras, strongly suggested that Greece would not make that payment,  Andrew Higgins and Alison Smale write in The New York Times. Late Monday, Jean-Claude Juncker, the head of the European Union’s executive branch, offered Mr. Tsipras a last-minute proposal that presented the possibility of a concession on demands for cuts in bonus payments for the poorest pensioners, European officials said. In return, Mr. Tsipras would have to accept all of the other creditors’ demands, which he had already turned down, and request an emergency meeting of eurozone finance ministers on Tuesday. So far, Mr. Tsipras has not responded publicly. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Hard-Line Stance on Greece', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '